#
# prima-materia — chaos magic: Hine, Prime Chaos
#
# The harvest of one work of the corpus of pmt:ChaosMagic, kept apart from
# traditions/chaos-magic.ttl, which declares the tradition and the work
# (pmw:PrimeChaos). Edition: Phil Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos
# Magic, foreword by Grant Morrison (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999); the copyright
# page names the first edition of 1993 (Chaos International Publications)
# and the second revised edition of 1999 (New Falcon). Read complete in the
# full-text layer of archive.org prime-chaos-adventures-in-chaos-magic-phil-
# hine-grant-morrison, second file, 483091 characters; pages from the running
# heads.
#
# Harvested under prima-materia#893 with two independent extraction passes
# per part, reconciled by offset and word overlap, then integrated by a third
# reader of the whole part. Every record was compared with the nodes of
# traditions/chaos-magic-condensed-chaos.ttl and
# traditions/chaos-magic-oven-ready-chaos.ttl: where an earlier Hine node
# carries the same claim, no node is written here; a node on the same topic
# in another form carries a note beginning "Differs from". Signs of success
# and conditions of failure carry a note beginning "Counted as a sign of
# success:" or "Counted as a condition of failure:".
#


#
# Foreword by Grant Morrison
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAParadigmChangeViolentDismemberment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Paradigm change as violent dismemberment (Chod)"@en, "Paradigmenwechsel als gewaltsame Zerstückelung (Chöd)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Morrison cites the Tibetan Chod rite, where the initiate visualises the body torn apart and eaten by demons as the higher self looks on untouched, as showing that spiritual or paradigm change can be violent and uncompromising."@en ;
    skos:note "Foreword; Tibetan Chod tradition reported by Morrison."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Morrison, foreword to Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition), p. 1; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAHinesExperimentsDuplicatedVerified a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hine's experiments are to be duplicated and verified"@en, "Hines Experimente sollen wiederholt und überprüft werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Morrison states that the book gives detailed practical material on the workings of magic and proposes experiments that can and should be replicated and checked."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on testability of the method."@en, "Stated by Grant Morrison in his foreword, not by Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Morrison, foreword to Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition), p. 1; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADirectConfrontationChaos a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Direct confrontation with Chaos"@en, "Unmittelbare Begegnung mit dem Chaos"@de ;
    skos:definition "An unmistakable direct encounter with Chaos, said to be open to anyone willing to put in the work and open its doors."@en ;
    skos:note "Morrison adds that theory cannot replace personal experience: read, then do."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Morrison, foreword to Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition), p. 2; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATheoryCannotSubstitutePersonalExperience a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Theory cannot substitute for personal experience"@en, "Theorie ersetzt keine eigene Erfahrung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Theory may inspire, but in the end only personal practice counts; the reader is told to read and then act."@en ;
    skos:note "Foreword."@en, "Stated by Grant Morrison in his foreword, not by Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Morrison, foreword to Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition), p. 2; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .



#
# Adventures in Magic
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAgainstWorkEthicModelMagicalTrainingDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the work-ethic model of magical training"@en, "Gegen das Arbeitsethos-Modell magischer Ausbildung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine attacks the implicit 'Protestant work ethic' of modern magic: regimented daily banishing, visualisation and meditation that becomes guilt-laden hard work, mocking a training programme in an unnamed book as public-school discipline."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the training programme he mocks is from an unnamed book."@en, "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBAgainstProtestantWorkEthicMagic (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node sets fun against the work ethic that calls rituals Workings; Prime Chaos aims at regimented training programmes and the guilt that comes when one slackens."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, p. 14; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicAdventureAbroad a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Magic as adventure abroad"@en, "Magie als Abenteuer in der Fremde"@de ;
    skos:definition "Travel to a place not saturated by media; cut off from friends, familiar language and television, devote time to intensive practice framed as an adventure rather than routine."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine says this is how he best sticks to a programme. If travel is impossible, make magic an adventure at home."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, pp. 14-15; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicAdventureAbroadYieldsEaseEnteringIntensive a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Magic as adventure abroad yields ease of entering intensive practice"@en, "Magie als Abenteuer in der Fremde: Ertrag Leichter Einstieg in intensive Praxis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magic as adventure abroad is said to yield ease of entering intensive practice."@en ;
    skos:note "Written by the integrator from the link pass A recorded between this practice and capacity; the source states the effect at the practice."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicAdventureAbroad ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEaseEnteringIntensivePractice ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, pp. 14-15; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAvoidNewAgeSpiritualPackageToursCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Avoid New Age spiritual package tours"@en, "Esoterische Pauschalreisen meiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shamanic or 'magical' guided tours amount to paying to have one's fantasies confirmed and lead to absurdities such as burying crystals at sacred sites; avoid them."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicAdventureAbroad ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, pp. 14-15; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEaseEnteringIntensivePractice a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ease of entering intensive practice"@en, "Leichter Einstieg in intensive Praxis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being able to throw oneself into intensive magical practice, partly because time is easier to find when detached from one's usual cushion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, p. 15; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicExperiencingWorldDifferently a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magic as experiencing the world differently"@en, "Magie als andersartiges Erleben der Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine places at the core of magic learning to experience the world in other ways so as to tweak it at the edges, and responding to what is demanded by one's environment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, p. 15; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAdHocEnchantment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ad hoc enchantment"@en, "Improvisierte Verzauberung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ability, from a freestyle approach, to shape ideas and pull together an improvised enchantment to resolve an unforeseen situation (e.g. lost luggage in Cairo)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, p. 15; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcANewcomersErrorSeekingReadyMadeSpellCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Newcomer's error: seeking a ready-made spell for each problem"@en, "Anfängerfehler: für jedes Problem ein fertiges Ritual suchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beginners identify a problem and look for an existing ritual to remove it; no catalogue can cover everything life brings, so improvising is better."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAdHocEnchantment ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, p. 15; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABasicSkillsBeforeAdvancedWorkPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Basic skills before advanced work (received wisdom)"@en, "Grundfertigkeiten vor fortgeschrittener Arbeit (überlieferte Lehre)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Received wisdom holds that proficiency in concentration, visualisation, mantra and breath control must precede contacting gods or summoning entities; those who skip it are said to come to grief later."@en ;
    skos:note "Reported as general received wisdom, which Hine then circumvents with a fun-based training for a friend."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAProficiencyBasicMagicalSkills ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAdvancedMagicalWork ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Those who leap in without the basic skills are often said to come to grief later on."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, pp. 15-16; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAProficiencyBasicMagicalSkills a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Proficiency in the basic magical skills"@en, "Beherrschung der magischen Grundfertigkeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Proficiency in concentration, visualisation, mantra and breath control, which received wisdom names the basic skills of magic."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, pp. 15-16; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAdvancedMagicalWork a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Advanced magical work"@en, "Fortgeschrittene magische Arbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The exciting part of magic in the received view, such as conversing with gods or summoning entities, which that view places after the basic skills."@en ;
    skos:note "Reported as received wisdom about magical training; Hine himself then sets it aside for a friend."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, pp. 15-16; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalExercisesBuiltEnjoyedActivities a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical exercises built from enjoyed activities"@en, "Magische Übungen aus Lieblingsbeschäftigungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ask the learner what they enjoy (raves, games, TV) and design magical skill exercises to be done while having fun, tied to everyday aims."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, p. 16; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

