pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalDiaryPrerequisiteSuccessPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical diary as prerequisite for success (generally accepted)"@en, "Magisches Tagebuch als Voraussetzung des Erfolgs (allgemein angenommen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "It is commonly held that a strict magical diary is required for successful practice; Hine loosens this, keeping one only in phases."@en ;
    skos:note "Reported as the general view; Hine loosens it and keeps a diary only in phases."@en, "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicOrcDiaryEssential (Oven-Ready Chaos, 1992): the 1992 node gives forgetting as the reason the diary is held essential; here the diary is held a prerequisite of successful practice, and Hine loosens it."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAKeepingMagicalDiary ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASuccessfulMagicalPractice ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Keeping a Magical Diary, p. 17; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAKeepingMagicalDiary a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Keeping a magical diary"@en, "Ein magisches Tagebuch führen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keep a record of one's magical activities and insights; Hine keeps one in phases rather than strictly."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondAMagicalDiary (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 practice prescribes full entries for every attempt; here Hine keeps a diary only in phases and warns against strictness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Keeping a Magical Diary, p. 17; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASuccessfulMagicalPractice a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Successful magical practice"@en, "Erfolgreiche magische Praxis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Success in magical practice, the end toward which both the diary and an open mind are named as requisites in this chapter."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Keeping a Magical Diary, p. 17; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADiaryGuiltTripCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Diary as guilt trip"@en, "Tagebuch als Schuldfalle"@de ;
    skos:definition "A strict diary is pointless if failing to keep it up turns into guilt."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAKeepingMagicalDiary ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Keeping a Magical Diary, p. 17; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAMemoryTrainingAssociationChains a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Memory training with association chains"@en, "Gedächtnistraining mit Assoziationsketten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Train recall by building chains of association using pictures, photos, scents or objects of one's choice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Keeping a Magical Diary, p. 17; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMemoryTrainingAssociationYieldsTrainedRecallExperiences a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Memory training with association chains yields trained recall of experiences"@en, "Gedächtnistraining mit Assoziationsketten: Ertrag Geschultes Erinnern von Erfahrungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Memory training with association chains is said to yield trained recall of experiences."@en ;
    skos:note "Written by the integrator from the link pass A recorded between this practice and capacity; the source states the effect at the practice."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAMemoryTrainingAssociationChains ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATrainedRecallExperiences ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Keeping a Magical Diary, p. 17; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATrainedRecallExperiences a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Trained recall of experiences"@en, "Geschultes Erinnern von Erfahrungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ability to remember activities and insights without a written record."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Keeping a Magical Diary, p. 17; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcARetreatWordsHeadspaceCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Retreat into words and headspace"@en, "Rückzug in Worte und Kopfraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magicians easily lock themselves away from the world in books, the internet and their own headspace; if one notices this happening, stop reading and go out."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAExplore ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Explore!, p. 17; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAExplore a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Explore!"@en, "Erkunden!"@de ;
    skos:definition "Put books aside, walk in the park or the local wild side, seek wonder in surroundings, and visit places one would not ordinarily go."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine: magic is engagement with the world, not retreat from it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Explore!, p. 17; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcACrowleysAdviceShootDisturbingDogDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Crowley's advice to shoot a disturbing dog"@en, "Crowleys Rat, den störenden Hund zu erschießen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Crowley reportedly advised shooting a dog that disturbs meditation; Hine proposes befriending it instead."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: Crowley's advice is given loosely from memory, not quoted from a work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Explore!, p. 17; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAFixedDailyPracticeBuildsCharacter a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fixed daily practice builds character (common view)"@en, "Feste tägliche Praxis bildet Charakter (verbreitete Ansicht)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many books prescribe daily routines of meditation, banishing and visualisation at set times, held to build character and self-discipline; Hine says this suits only lifestyles that can be so structured."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Daily Practice, p. 17; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAFittingMagicDailyLife a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Fitting magic into daily life"@en, "Magie in den Alltag einpassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Meditate while doing household chores; cast brief spells while washing the dishes."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine reports such spells seem neither more nor less potent than full ritual."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Daily Practice, p. 17; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAQuickSpellsEffectiveFullRitual a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Quick spells as effective as full ritual"@en, "Schnelle Zauber so wirksam wie volles Ritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine observes that spells done during chores appear neither more nor less effective than elaborate ritual."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how tested/fixed the method is (personal observation)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Daily Practice, p. 17; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcADoingNothing a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Doing nothing"@en, "Nichtstun"@de ;
    skos:definition "Occasionally take time off and do nothing at all; Hine notes this can be as hard as a complex mental exercise."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Daily Practice, pp. 17-18; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPracticeRoutinesRegimentLifeCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Practice routines regiment life"@en, "Übungsroutinen reglementieren das Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Routines can come to regiment one's life; total control, e.g. of dreams, is not necessarily desirable."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcACompleteMasteryDreamLife ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Daily Practice, p. 18; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcACompleteMasteryDreamLife a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Complete mastery of dream life"@en, "Vollständige Beherrschung des Traumlebens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Full control over one's dreams, attainable through years of dream-control techniques; Hine declines to pursue it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Daily Practice, p. 18; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicRequiresIntegratedPractisedSkills a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magic requires integrated practised skills"@en, "Magie erfordert eingeübte, integrierte Fertigkeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Practice is undeniably important: magic needs a range of skills developed both as separate disciplines and as integrated techniques; Hine has put himself through several training programmes by others."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Daily Practice, p. 18; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABeginnersMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Beginner's Mind"@en, "Anfängergeist"@de ;
    skos:definition "An open, naive, questioning attitude toward magic, possibly among the most important requisites for success; harder to keep than to adopt."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Beginner's Mind, p. 18; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAOpenMindRequisiteSuccessPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Open mind as a requisite for success"@en, "Offener Geist als Erfordernis des Erfolgs"@de ;
    skos:definition "Approaching practice with an open mind is said to be possibly among the most important requisites for success in magic."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABeginnersMind ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASuccessfulMagicalPractice ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Beginner's Mind, p. 18; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcANoExpertsMagic a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No experts in magic"@en, "Keine Experten in der Magie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magic has no experts, only people who have practised longer; beginners often invent the most novel techniques because they have not absorbed others' fixed notions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Beginner's Mind, pp. 18-19; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcACultivatingBeginnersMind a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Cultivating Beginner's Mind"@en, "Den Anfängergeist pflegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ask people questions, be naive, request clarification of authoritative claims, and state your own view without hesitation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Beginner's Mind, pp. 18-19; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAQuestioningYieldsBeginnersMind a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Questioning yields Beginner's Mind"@en, "Fragen ergibt Anfängergeist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asking, seeking clarification and voicing one's view keeps the Beginner's Mind."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcACultivatingBeginnersMind ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABeginnersMind ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Beginner's Mind, p. 18; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAFearAskingBeginnerCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Fear of asking as a beginner"@en, "Angst, als Anfänger zu fragen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The belief that a beginner has nothing to contribute keeps people from asking and speaking, which holds them back; likewise one tends to undervalue one's own experience against books or veterans."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABeginnersMind ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Adventures in Magic, Beginner's Mind, pp. 18-19; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .



#
# The Dynamics of Sorcery
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAFirstAttemptsDisappointFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "First attempts disappoint"@en, "Erste Versuche enttäuschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first few attempts at magic may fall short of expectations or fail dismally; this should not deter the practitioner."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of first attempts at magic, which may fall short of expectations or fail outright. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the operator's inexperience and preconceived expectations, and the reader is told not to be put off."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, p. 20; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcALurkingSuspicionMagicNonsenseCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Lurking suspicion that magic is nonsense"@en, "Lauernder Verdacht, Magie sei Unsinn"@de ;
    skos:definition "Embedded cultural programming keeps a suspicion, armed with rationalisations, that magic is superstition that cannot really happen; it must be overcome by proof through practice."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAProvingOneselfMagicWorks ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, p. 20; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAProvingOneselfMagicWorks a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Proving to oneself that magic works"@en, "Sich selbst beweisen, dass Magie wirkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Try magic out, even in small ways, until a result is seen; practical sorcery applied to everyday needs is a good starting point."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, p. 20; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAProvingMagicWorksYieldsExpandedAchievable a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Proving magic works yields expanded Achievable Reality and a magical world"@en, "Beweis der Wirksamkeit ergibt erweiterte Wirklichkeit und magische Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Seeing sorcery results, and continuing to practise, pushes the boundary of the achievable and finally makes the world magical."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAProvingOneselfMagicWorks ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAExpandedAchievableReality, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAWorldBecomingMagical, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAConfidenceAbilitiesTechniques ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, p. 20; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAExpandedAchievableReality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Expanded Achievable Reality"@en, "Erweiterte erreichbare Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pushing back the boundaries of what one accepts can be done with magic, so that nothing seems as clear-cut as before."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondAAchievableReality (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node defines magic as pushing back believed limits; here the widening is what follows from proving to oneself, even in small ways, that magic works."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, p. 20; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAWorldBecomingMagical a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The world becoming magical"@en, "Die Welt wird magisch"@de ;
    skos:definition "With sustained practice magic becomes woven into one's personal reality, no longer believed in as something separate; the world itself becomes magical."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, p. 20; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAConfidenceAbilitiesTechniques a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Confidence in abilities and techniques"@en, "Vertrauen in Fähigkeiten und Techniken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Seeing sorcery results raises confidence in one's own abilities and in the techniques, and leads to a broader outlook."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, pp. 20-21; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASelfAssessmentNeededSorcerySuccessPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-assessment needed for sorcery success"@en, "Selbstprüfung als Bedingung für Erfolg in der Zauberei"@de ;
    skos:definition "Success with sorcery requires developing the ability to assess one's own performance and scrutinise one's desires, and this itself brings change."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAssessingSelfPerformanceExaminingDesires ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASuccessSorceryTechniques ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, p. 21; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASuccessSorceryTechniques a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Success with sorcery techniques"@en, "Erfolg mit Zaubereitechniken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Success in changing the world directly by sorcery, which Hine says demands that the magician watch closely what he is doing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, p. 21; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAssessingSelfPerformanceExaminingDesires a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Assessing self-performance and examining desires"@en, "Eigene Leistung beurteilen und Wünsche prüfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ability to evaluate one's own magical performance and scrutinise one's desires; attention shifts to the world as experienced."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondAAssessingPerformance (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node relates techniques to outcomes; here the capacity also includes scrutinising one's own desires, and is named as a requirement of success with sorcery."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, p. 21; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPersonalSorceryTechniquesEasyDevise a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Personal sorcery techniques are easy to devise"@en, "Eigene Zaubertechniken sind leicht zu entwickeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "The dynamics of sorcery are simple, techniques many, and devising one's own unique techniques is not difficult."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, p. 21; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAThreeCoreElementsSorcery a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three core elements of sorcery"@en, "Drei Kernelemente der Zauberei"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's own overview of sorcery procedure in three numbered elements: intention (a precise statement of intent, refined by divination and by breaking the aim into stages), probability pathways (a route by which the result can plausibly manifest), and timing (choosing the right moment for the working)."@en ;
    skos:note "Author-made scheme (pm:Systematizing); related records A1-0052, A1-0062."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Prime Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Core Elements of Sorcery, pp. 21-23; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcADivinationRefineIntent a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Divination to refine intent"@en, "Divination zur Schärfung der Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use Tarot, runes, I Ching, astrology or a self-made system to analyse the elements of the situation behind a surface desire, find the blocking factor, and make that the focus of the enchantment; also to check one's motives and hidden factors when others are involved."@en ;
    skos:note "Example: job-seeker finds lack of confidence and enchants for self-confidence."@en, "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBDivinationExamineMotivesBehindDesire (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 practice examines the motives behind a desire; here divination also finds the blocking factor behind a surface desire and makes it the target, as when a job-seeker enchants for confidence."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Core Elements of Sorcery, pp. 21-22; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADivinationYieldsInsightBlocks a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Divination yields insight into blocks"@en, "Divination ergibt Einsicht in Hemmnisse"@de ;
    skos:definition "Divining the situation reveals the blocking factor and motives."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcADivinationRefineIntent ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAIdentifyingHiddenBlockingFactorsMotives ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Core Elements of Sorcery, p. 21; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAImprovedSelfConfidence a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Improved self-confidence (enchantment)"@en, "Gesteigertes Selbstvertrauen (Verzauberung)"@de ;
    skos:definition "An enchantment whose main focus is improving self-confidence, as the real target behind seeking employment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Core Elements of Sorcery, p. 22; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAIdentifyingHiddenBlockingFactorsMotives a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Identifying hidden blocking factors and motives"@en, "Verborgene Hemmnisse und Motive erkennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ability to discern the key obstacle behind a desire, one's own motives for intervening, and hidden factors in a situation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Core Elements of Sorcery, p. 22; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcACognitiveRestructuringIntent a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Cognitive restructuring of intent"@en, "Kognitive Umstrukturierung der Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Break an overall intention into smaller stages each more readily achieved, shifting the Achievable Reality threshold in steps rather than at once."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Core Elements of Sorcery, p. 22; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcASorceryEventSeries a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sorcery Event Series (S.E.S.)"@en, "Zauberei-Ereignisreihe (S.E.S.)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Break a long-term goal into a series of linked, related sorcery operations; as each result manifests, its momentum carries one into the next working, like toppling dominoes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Event Series, p. 22; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcARaisedProbabilityLongTermIntent a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Raised probability of a long-term intent"@en, "Erhöhte Wahrscheinlichkeit einer Langzeitabsicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each concluded event in the series raises the likelihood that the overall intent manifests; useful for establishing long-term projects."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Event Series, p. 22; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASESYieldsRaisedProbability a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "S.E.S. yields raised probability of long-term goal"@en, "S.E.S. ergibt höhere Wahrscheinlichkeit des Langzeitziels"@de ;
    skos:definition "Linked workings cumulatively raise the probability of the overall aim."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcASorceryEventSeries ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcARaisedProbabilityLongTermIntent ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Event Series, p. 22; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAProbabilityPathways a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Probability pathways"@en, "Wahrscheinlichkeitspfade"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magical results do not appear from nowhere; sorcery works best when a pathway exists for the result to manifest and its probability is at least slightly above zero."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBOpeningPathwayIntent (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node is the instruction to open a route for the result; here the point is stated as a probability that must be at least slightly above zero."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Probability Pathways, pp. 22-23; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAExamRitualWithoutRevisionFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Exam ritual without revision"@en, "Prüfungsritual ohne Lernen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A ritual to pass an exam without any study creates no reasonable probability of success."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of sorcery without a probability pathway: a ritual to pass an exam done without any revision sets up no reasonable chance of passing. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the operator, who opened no pathway. It concerns pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAProbabilityPathways."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Probability Pathways, p. 22; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAMultipleProjectsMoneyWorkings a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Multiple projects for money workings"@en, "Mehrere Projekte bei Geldzaubern"@de ;
    skos:definition "When working for financial gain, keep several projects running, any of which could bring in funds, so that the working has outlets."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBOpeningPathwayIntent (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node gives single routes for money (a book, a job application, a lottery ticket); here several projects are to run at once so that any may bring in funds."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Probability Pathways, p. 23; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMultipleProjectsYieldFinancialGain a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Multiple projects yield financial gain"@en, "Mehrere Projekte ergeben Geldgewinn"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sorcery for money is more likely to succeed with several pathways open."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAMultipleProjectsMoneyWorkings ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAFinancialGain ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Probability Pathways, p. 23; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAFinancialGain a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Financial gain"@en, "Finanzieller Gewinn"@de ;
    skos:definition "Increased funds through sorcery, more likely when several possible channels exist."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Probability Pathways, p. 23; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATimingSorcery a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Timing in sorcery"@en, "Zeitpunkt in der Zauberei"@de ;
    skos:definition "Situations are unfolding event series; early stages are more fluid and easier to influence, as visible macroscopic events arise from unseen microscopic fluctuations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Timing, p. 23; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAHealingImpedingProgressiveDisease a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Healing: impeding progressive disease"@en, "Heilung: Fortschreiten einer Krankheit hemmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sorcery workings to slow a long-term progressive illness, said to be likelier to succeed early than late in its course."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Timing, p. 23; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcALateInterventionLessEffectiveFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Late intervention less effective"@en, "Späte Intervention weniger wirksam"@de ;
    skos:definition "At later stages of a developing situation or illness, outcomes are harder to influence."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of workings on a developing situation such as a progressive illness: at a late stage outcomes are less easily influenced, so the working is likely to do less. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the stage the situation has reached, that is on timing rather than on the operator's skill. It concerns pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAHealingImpedingProgressiveDisease."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Timing, p. 23; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcANudgingSituationOpportuneMoment a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Nudging a situation at the opportune moment"@en, "Eine Situation im richtigen Moment anstoßen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pay close attention to a situation, identify small changes (with divination if useful), and influence them so they grow into the change named in the statement of intent."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Timing, p. 23; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAGeneralSorceryProcedure a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "General Sorcery Procedure"@en, "Allgemeines Verfahren der Zauberei"@de ;
    skos:definition "After formulating the statement of intent: enter a Free Area; clear awareness of everything but the act; move into Gnosis; at its peak project the desire in representative form (e.g. a sigil); banish it from awareness; close the Free Area (laughter, banishing, gesture); move on, treating the working as finished."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, pp. 23-25; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAGeneralSorceryProcedureYieldsManifestationDesireThrough a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "General Sorcery Procedure yields manifestation of a desire through sorcery"@en, "Allgemeines Verfahren der Zauberei: Ertrag Verwirklichung eines Wunsches durch Zauberei"@de ;
    skos:definition "General Sorcery Procedure is said to yield manifestation of a desire through sorcery."@en ;
    skos:note "Written by the integrator from the link pass A recorded between this practice and capacity; the source states the effect at the practice."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAGeneralSorceryProcedure ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAManifestationDesireThroughSorcery ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, pp. 23-25; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAStagesGeneralSorceryProcedure a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Stages of the General Sorcery Procedure"@en, "Stufen des allgemeinen Zaubereiverfahrens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Statement of intent; entry into Free Area; Gnosis; projection of the desire at the peak; forgetting it; closing the Free Area; moving on."@en ;
    skos:note "The source orders the steps as next steps of one procedure; it names no consequence of skipping any of them. Moving on after closing is not entered as its own member."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:ChaosMagicCondBStatementIntent ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAEnteringFreeArea ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAGnosis ;
    rdf:_4 pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAProjectingForgettingDesire ;
    rdf:_5 pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAClosingFreeArea ;
    pm:seriesStatement "The general sorcery procedure runs from the Statement of Intent through entry into a Free Area and the move into gnosis to projecting and forgetting the desire at its peak and closing the Free Area; each step is introduced as the next one, and projection has its sense only at the peak of gnosis reached in the step before." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, pp. 23-24; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAEnteringFreeArea a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Entering a Free Area"@en, "Eintritt in einen Freiraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Redefine a space or state of consciousness as a zone where Consensus Reality is put aside and Magical Reality operates, using anything from full banishing and altar to simply closing the eyes and concentrating; the choice depends on circumstances, available time, necessity and preference."@en ;
    skos:note "Orthodox equivalent: casting a circle, postures."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, pp. 23-24; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAFreeAreaBeforeGnosisPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Free Area before Gnosis"@en, "Freiraum vor Gnosis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Entry into the Free Area precedes moving toward gnosis."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAEnteringFreeArea ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAGnosis ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, p. 24; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAGnosis a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Gnosis"@en, "Gnosis"@de ;
    skos:definition "One-pointed consciousness in which awareness is emptied of all but the object of concentration, giving will intentionality and vector."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondAGnosisAtWill (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node is the ability to enter altered states at will; here gnosis is defined as one-pointed consciousness emptied of all but its object, giving will intention and direction."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, p. 24; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAThreeRoutesYieldGnosis a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Three routes yield Gnosis"@en, "Drei Wege ergeben Gnosis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Excitatory, inhibitory and indifferent-vacuity methods each lead to gnosis."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAExcitatoryRouteGnosis, pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAInhibitoryRouteGnosis, pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAIndifferentVacuity ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAGnosis ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, p. 24; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAThreefoldClassificationRoutesGnosis a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Threefold classification of routes to Gnosis"@en, "Dreiteilung der Wege zur Gnosis"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Chaos approach classes methods for gnosis as excitatory, inhibitory, or indifferent vacuity."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBExcitatoryInhibitoryTranceRoutes (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node sorts routes into trance in two classes; here the routes to gnosis are three, adding indifferent vacuity."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Prime Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, p. 24; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAExcitatoryRouteGnosis a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Excitatory route to Gnosis"@en, "Erregender Weg zur Gnosis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reach gnosis by stimulating the BodyMind: dancing, drumming, hyperventilation, sexual arousal."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondAInhibitoryExcitatoryGnosis (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node names two poles of physiological gnosis; here the excitatory route stands as one of three."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, p. 24; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAInhibitoryRouteGnosis a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Inhibitory route to Gnosis"@en, "Hemmender Weg zur Gnosis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reach gnosis by stilling the BodyMind: passive meditation, hypnotic agents, slow chanting, slow breathing."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondAInhibitoryExcitatoryGnosis (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node names two poles of physiological gnosis; here the inhibitory route stands as one of three and includes hypnotic agents."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, p. 24; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAIndifferentVacuity a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Indifferent Vacuity"@en, "Gleichgültige Leere"@de ;
    skos:definition "A no-mind state of non-disinterest in which the desired object flashes briefly in a mind empty of content, without emotional attachment to it."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBIndifferentVacuity (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 practice is a not-much-bothered state such as doodling sigils in a dull talk; here it is a state of no-mind in which the desire flickers briefly without emotional attachment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, p. 24; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAProjectingForgettingDesire a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Projecting and forgetting the desire"@en, "Projektion und Vergessen des Wunsches"@de ;
    skos:definition "At the peak of gnosis, send the desire in its chosen form (e.g. a sigil) toward its target or out into the void, then banish it from awareness by forgetting it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, p. 24; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPeakGnosisBeforeProjectionPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Peak of Gnosis before projection"@en, "Höhepunkt der Gnosis vor der Projektion"@de ;
    skos:definition "The desire is projected only upon reaching the peak of gnosis."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAGnosis ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAProjectingForgettingDesire ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, p. 24; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAClosingFreeArea a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Closing the Free Area"@en, "Schließen des Freiraums"@de ;
    skos:definition "After projection, close the Free Area by any preferred means such as a banishing, a gesture of the hand or manic laughter, and move on."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, p. 24; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAManifestationDesireThroughSorcery a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Manifestation of a desire through sorcery"@en, "Verwirklichung eines Wunsches durch Zauberei"@de ;
    skos:definition "Having set up conditions by which the projected desire will manifest accordingly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, p. 24; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcACompletedWorkingFinished a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A completed working is finished"@en, "Eine vollzogene Arbeit ist abgeschlossen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A key to sorcery: once complete, the working should be regarded, at least magically, as done, with no further magical work needed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, pp. 24-25; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADeepCertaintyOnesSorcery a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Deep certainty in one's sorcery"@en, "Tiefe Gewissheit im eigenen Zaubern"@de ;
    skos:definition "The settled certainty that one's sorcery will bring the desired result, said to come only through sustained practice, effort and refining."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBCertaintyThatMagicWorks (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node is the conviction that magic works; here it is the certainty that one's own sorcery will bring the desired result, said to come only from sustained practice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, p. 25; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAClaimedSuccessRate8090 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Claimed success rate of 80–90%"@en, "Behauptete Erfolgsquote von 80–90 %"@de ;
    skos:definition "Advanced practitioners not uncommonly claim around an 80-90% success rate for sorcery of this sort."@en ;
    skos:note "Claims of unnamed advanced practitioners; statement on how tested the method is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, p. 25; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAProlongedGroupSorceryRitual a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Prolonged group sorcery ritual"@en, "Langes Gruppenritual der Zauberei"@de ;
    skos:definition "A sorcery working done as a group ritual of some three hours with sustained dancing, drumming and chanting, the elaborate end of the range the general procedure covers."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, p. 25; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAElaborateRitualEmptyHandedMagicPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "From elaborate ritual to empty-handed magic"@en, "Vom aufwendigen Ritual zur Magie mit leeren Händen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magicians generally proceed from long, elaborate rituals to brief empty-handed acts."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine says magicians generally move from the elaborate to the brief kind of working; no consequence of skipping is named."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAProlongedGroupSorceryRitual ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondBEmptyHandedGesture ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, p. 25; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPsychocosm a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Psychocosm (personal Magical Reality)"@en, "Psychokosmos (persönliche magische Wirklichkeit)"@de ;
    skos:definition "With progress magic becomes part of daily experience as one moves from a widening Consensus Reality to building a Magical Reality of one's own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Sorcery Operations, Basic Procedure, p. 25; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicsGameRules a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magic's 'game rules'"@en, "Die 'Spielregeln' der Magie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Learning symbols and correspondences teaches magic's game rules; worthwhile rules are flexible and open to interpretation, and practice shows Consensus Reality's rules have more loopholes than expected."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Evolving a Psychocosm, p. 25; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAExperienceBeforeBeliefPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Experience before belief"@en, "Erfahrung vor Glauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do magic first, then decide which beliefs and concepts fit in view of personal experience; the Chaos approach stresses experience over pre-experiential belief."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAProvingOneselfMagicWorks ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAChoosingBeliefsLightExperience ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Evolving a Psychocosm, pp. 25-26; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAChoosingBeliefsLightExperience a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Choosing beliefs in the light of experience"@en, "Überzeugungen im Licht der Erfahrung wählen"@de ;
    skos:definition "After doing magic, consider which beliefs and concepts seem most fitting given one's own experience, rather than adopting them beforehand."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Evolving a Psychocosm, pp. 25-26; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAUninterestingSystemYieldsNothingFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Uninteresting system yields nothing"@en, "Uninteressantes System bringt nichts"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hardly anyone benefits from an approach that fails to interest them; choose a system that attracts you."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of working a magical system one is not interested in: few people get anything from such an approach. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the operator's choice of system."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Evolving a Psychocosm, p. 26; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalBeliefsChangeExperience a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical beliefs change with experience"@en, "Magische Überzeugungen wandeln sich mit der Erfahrung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beliefs about magic do not stay constant but shift with experience and perspective; a strong early belief (e.g. in the circle's inviolability) may be useful and later loosened through reality-testing."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine's anecdote: belief in the circle taught him self-organisation before ritual."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Evolving a Psychocosm, p. 26; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAUntestedBeliefsHardenDogmaCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Untested beliefs harden into dogma"@en, "Ungeprüfte Überzeugungen erstarren zum Dogma"@de ;
    skos:definition "When magicians lack chances for reality-testing, beliefs about magic quickly become dogmas defended at all costs."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalBeliefsChangeExperience ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Evolving a Psychocosm, pp. 26-27; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalTheoryBeliefNotScience a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical theory is belief, not science"@en, "Magische Theorie ist Glaube, nicht Wissenschaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unlike physics, magic needs no body of abstract theory before casting a spell; theory is rooted in personal belief, need not be unified, and the practitioner's degree of belief matters more to the outcome."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Theory and Glamour, p. 27; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcASelectiveBeliefModelWorking a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Selective belief in a model for one working"@en, "Selektiver Glaube an ein Modell für eine Arbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Choose a theory of magical action you find attractive and believe it true just for the length of a given ritual or phase of work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Theory and Glamour, p. 27; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATheoriesActionTreatedImmutableLawCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Theories-of-Action treated as immutable law"@en, "Handlungstheorien als unveränderliche Gesetze"@de ;
    skos:definition "Occult theories are often treated as true independent of experience, sometimes as laws handed down by higher intelligences beyond debate, with questioners dismissed as insufficiently initiated."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondATheoryInUse (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node describes theories-of-action passed from book to book; here the caution adds that some authors present them as laws from higher intelligences and brush off questioners as not initiated enough."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalTheoryBeliefNotScience ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Theory and Glamour, p. 28; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAOpenCuriousMindBenefitsMagic a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Open, curious mind benefits magic"@en, "Offener, neugieriger Geist nützt der Magie"@de ;
    skos:definition "From the Chaos perspective magic benefits from an open and curious mind rather than accepting claims at face value."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Theory and Glamour, p. 28; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATakingMetaphorLiterallyCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Taking metaphor literally"@en, "Metaphern wörtlich nehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Much magical experience can only be told in myth, poetry or metaphor, but westerners tend (possibly through their education) to believe that all metaphorical speech has a factual basis."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAChakraSystemsSymbolicNotFactual ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Mistaking Metaphors, pp. 28-29; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAChakraSystemsSymbolicNotFactual a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Chakra systems are symbolic, not factual"@en, "Chakrensysteme sind symbolisch, nicht faktisch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tantric texts describe differing numbers of chakras (six, seven, nine, eleven, twenty-four) in symbolic language that western authors have mistakenly read literally; the Western Esoteric Tradition largely assumes they physically exist."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Mistaking Metaphors, p. 29; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAWoodroffeAgainstLeadbeaterSahasraraPetalsDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Woodroffe against Leadbeater on the Sahasrara petals"@en, "Woodroffe gegen Leadbeater über die Blätter des Sahasrara"@de ;
    skos:definition "Leadbeater claimed to have clairvoyantly counted exactly 960 petals of the crown chakra rather than the traditional thousand; Woodroffe answers that the Indian 'thousand' denotes great magnitude, not a count, so the claim is nonsense. Hine endorses Woodroffe."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: Leadbeater's count (The Inner Life) and Woodroffe's reply (The Serpent Power) are both reported, not quoted, and Hine sides with Woodroffe."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Mistaking Metaphors, p. 29; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATheoriesCopiedBookBookBecomeDogmaCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Theories copied book to book become dogma"@en, "Von Buch zu Buch kopierte Theorien werden Dogma"@de ;
    skos:definition "Much occult theory passes from book to book without intervening thought; attempts to put magic on a scientific footing easily create dogmas, even to the point of declaring the original Indian sages wrong about chakras."@en ;
    skos:note "The phrase about theories passing from book to book is credited to Pete Carroll."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalTheoryBeliefNotScience ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Mistaking Metaphors, p. 29; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAClingingDiscreditedScientificModelsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Clinging to discredited scientific models"@en, "Festhalten an widerlegten Wissenschaftsmodellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Occultists often base a theory on a popular scientific model and, when it is revised, defend their belief and attack the scientists; such uncritical thinking leads to dogmatism, called the enemy of magic."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalTheoryBeliefNotScience ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Mistaking Metaphors, pp. 29-30; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMapNotTerritory a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Map is not territory"@en, "Die Landkarte ist nicht das Gebiet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magical maps such as the Tree of Life or chakras give a consistent framework for experience but change over time and are good at explaining some aspects and poor at others."@en ;
    skos:note "Robert Anton Wilson's maxim."@en, "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondAMapAndTerritoryCautela (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node warns against taking the model for the experience; here the maxim is credited to Robert Anton Wilson and models are described as changing over time and good for some aspects but not others."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Models and Maps, p. 30; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAGrandEsotericModelsDoomedFail a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Grand esoteric models doomed to fail"@en, "Große esoterische Gesamtmodelle zum Scheitern verurteilt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Attempts to build an esoteric model able to explain every magical event, like physics' grand theory, are in Hine's opinion doomed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Models and Maps, p. 30; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAgainstReducingMagicPsychology a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against reducing magic to psychology"@en, "Gegen die Reduktion der Magie auf Psychologie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Psychology has aided understanding of magic as self-development, but reducing all phenomena to it is a mistake: curses explained as autosuggestion fail to account for victims who knew nothing and still fell ill."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Models and Maps, p. 30; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcACursingSomeoneIllness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cursing someone into illness"@en, "Jemanden krank verfluchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine points to cases in which the target of a curse falls ill without knowing that a curse was laid, against the account of curses as autosuggestion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Models and Maps, p. 30; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAModelChoiceJudgedWhetherWorks a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Model choice judged by whether it works"@en, "Modellwahl danach, ob es funktioniert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Which theory or model one adopts is personal choice; the only yardstick is whether it works for you."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Models and Maps, p. 30; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADevelopmentBringsThreateningExperiencesCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Development brings threatening experiences"@en, "Entwicklung bringt bedrohliche Erlebnisse"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some experiences in magical development will be life-changing, unpleasant or even threatening; this is part of the course."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAIntenseStatesVisionsPrecognition ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Results and Magical Advancement, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAIntenseStatesVisionsPrecognition a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intense states, visions and precognition"@en, "Intensive Zustände, Visionen und Vorahnung"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the course of magical development one is said to be quite likely to meet heightened states of awareness, visions, odd perceptions and precognition, some of them life-changing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Results and Magical Advancement, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAReadingExperiencesSignsIlluminationCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Reading experiences as signs of illumination"@en, "Erlebnisse als Zeichen der Erleuchtung deuten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Intense states, visions, precognition or a successful candle spell are part of development, but the problem comes when they are taken as signs of great illumination; Dogen told a student who saw the Buddha in light that it would go away if he concentrated on his breathing."@en ;
    skos:note "Zen anecdote of Dogen, reported."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAIntenseStatesVisionsPrecognition ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Results and Magical Advancement, pp. 30-31; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADeliberatelyProjectingOnesPresenceAnother a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Deliberately projecting one's presence to another"@en, "Die eigene Gegenwart gezielt zu jemandem projizieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine allows that deliberately projecting one's presence to someone could cause them to see visions of one; he denies he did so in the reported case."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Results and Magical Advancement, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAUniversePartlyConformsBelief a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The universe partly conforms to belief"@en, "Das Universum fügt sich teilweise dem Glauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Central to magic is what one chooses to believe about magic and oneself; in some respects the universe follows those beliefs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Metaprogramming & Magical Belief, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcACommitmentEmotionalInvestmentMakeBeliefSystemPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Commitment and emotional investment make a belief system workable"@en, "Hingabe und emotionale Bindung machen ein Glaubenssystem tragfähig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Any belief system can serve as a basis for magic provided one can put commitment and emotional attachment in it."@en ;
    skos:note "The condition is stated as a proviso; no consequence of lacking it is spelled out."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAInvestingCommitmentBeliefSystem ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCAnyBeliefSystem ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Metaprogramming & Magical Belief, p. 32; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAInvestingCommitmentBeliefSystem a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Investing commitment in a belief system"@en, "Hingabe in ein Glaubenssystem legen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to put commitment and emotional attachment into a belief system."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Metaprogramming & Magical Belief, p. 32; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABeliefAncientTraditionConfidenceAid a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Belief in 'ancient tradition' as confidence aid"@en, "Glaube an 'alte Überlieferung' als Stütze des Vertrauens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's early belief that his system was ancient initiatory wisdom proved largely glamour or hype, yet it helped him gain confidence in his magical ability."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Metaprogramming & Magical Belief, p. 32; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADiscrimination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Discrimination"@en, "Unterscheidungsvermögen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magically understood: moving beyond accepting others' models by one's own research and magical work, and finding what is appropriate for oneself from one's own feelings; needs no special intuition, only attention to how one takes in ideas."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDiscrimination (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node reads discrimination through Ganesha's trunk; here it is defined as going beyond others' models by one's own research and finding what fits one's own feelings."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, The Power Of Discrimination, pp. 32-33; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAInvestigatingWhyAttributionsDiffer a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Investigating why attributions differ"@en, "Untersuchen, warum Zuordnungen abweichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Read several authors on a subject such as runes, note where their attributions differ, and work out why each attribution is given; actively experiment with the material until it becomes personally meaningful."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, The Power Of Discrimination, pp. 32-33; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAcceptingSingleAuthorsViewFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Accepting a single author's view"@en, "Die Sicht eines einzigen Autors übernehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Never looking beyond one author's interpretation means accepting the restriction of that viewpoint and being unable to discriminate between opinions."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of discrimination: whoever never goes beyond one author's reading of a subject has accepted that one viewpoint's limits and cannot tell one opinion from another. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the operator. It concerns pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADiscrimination."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, The Power Of Discrimination, p. 32; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAOwnInvestigationYieldsDiscrimination a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Own investigation yields discrimination"@en, "Eigene Untersuchung ergibt Unterscheidungsvermögen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Finding out the reasons behind attributions enables discrimination between opinions."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAInvestigatingWhyAttributionsDiffer ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADiscrimination ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, The Power Of Discrimination, pp. 32-33; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalModelsOpenQuestionChange a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical models are open to question and change"@en, "Magische Modelle sind fragbar und wandelbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "Models may be elaborated, recognised as limited, or discarded as one questions them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, The Power Of Discrimination, p. 33; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalGlamour a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical glamour"@en, "Magischer Glamour"@de ;
    skos:definition "The aura around a belief system: how adherents present themselves and how the system is seen in wider culture, comprising memes, writing styles, images, buzzwords and sometimes charismatic figureheads; in quasi-religious systems glamours can become faiths. Chaos Magic early acquired an inaccurate 'sinister' glamour."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Magical Glamour, p. 33; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAProjectingGlamours a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Projecting glamours"@en, "Glamour projizieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Skilfully weaving a glamour, such as of shaman or satanist, significantly alters others' reactions; an adept can be seen as both by different groups though neither is true."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Magical Glamour, p. 34; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAOutsiderGlamourCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The Outsider glamour"@en, "Der Außenseiter-Glamour"@de ;
    skos:definition "Seeing oneself as an outsider can excuse failing to get one's act together, goes with lack of direction, poor social skills and resentment, addiction to Being Right and Getting Even, dualistic need for an enemy, and arrogance that hides insecurity."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalGlamour ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, The Dynamics of Sorcery, Magical Glamour, p. 34; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .



#
# Initiation
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAInitiationConsciousTransition a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Initiation as conscious transition"@en, "Initiation als bewusster Übergang"@de ;
    skos:definition "To be initiated is to recognise consciously that one is crossing a threshold of change; the initiate is intensely aware of the condition and rides the wave instead of resisting. Many magicians and pagans mark it with a ritual or magical retirement. It is a period of letting go when habits, beliefs and identifications loosen."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCThresholdRecognitionKey (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node makes recognition of the threshold the key; here the initiate is also said to mark the period by ritual or magical retirement and to ride the wave of letting go."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, p. 35; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcALossCertaintyInitiationCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Loss of certainty in initiation"@en, "Verlust der Gewissheit in der Initiation"@de ;
    skos:definition "One may lose one's hold on what is normal for a time, and the confrontation with oneself can be hard."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAInitiationConsciousTransition ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, p. 35; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAFleeingAdeptFantasiesFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fleeing into adept fantasies"@en, "Flucht in Adeptenphantasien"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some never go the distance through initiation and instead adopt fantasies of being mighty adepts rather than accepting their humanity with humility."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of initiation: some never go the distance and retreat into fantasies of being mighty adepts instead of accepting their own humanity. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the operator. It concerns pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAInitiationConsciousTransition."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, p. 35; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAReAcquaintanceSelf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Re-acquaintance with self"@en, "Wiederbegegnung mit sich selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "A core by-product of initiation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, p. 35; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAConfidenceLettingGo a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Confidence of letting go"@en, "Zuversicht des Loslassens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Confidence springing from the ability to relinquish control when it is no longer viable, to make mistakes freely, admit not knowing, and meet an uncertain world smiling; others' truths no longer threaten one's own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, p. 35; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASenseMagicalProgress a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sense of magical progress"@en, "Gefühl magischen Fortschritts"@de ;
    skos:definition "The feeling of being on the path does not come automatically but creeps up; where one is going depends on one's own, changing idea of progress and on one's company."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, p. 36; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASystemsInitiationMagicalGrades a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Systems of initiation and Magical Grades"@en, "Initiationssysteme und magische Grade"@de ;
    skos:definition "Psychocosms are often used to cut magical progress into discrete steps called grades, each with its own experiences and methods, so the magician can focus on a single thing at a time and interpret experiences within a framework; Hine adds 'that's the theory, anyway'."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, pp. 36-37; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAReadyMadeVersusSelfMadeInitiation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ready-made versus self-made initiation systems"@en, "Fertige gegenüber selbstgeschaffenen Initiationssystemen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some argue for following orders' or teachers' systems, others for building one's own; having done both, Hine finds each has pros and cons, and how far one goes is a matter of preference and changing needs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, p. 37; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAGoldenDawnGrades a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Golden Dawn grades"@en, "Grade des Golden Dawn"@de ;
    skos:definition "Neophyte, Zelator, Practicus and further grades, each with particular magical aims and characteristic mystical experiences."@en ;
    skos:note "Golden Dawn, reported by Hine; only the first three grades are named, the rest are left as etc., and no consequence of skipping is named."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcANeophyte ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAZelator ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPracticus ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Hine gives the Golden Dawn grades as the best-known example of magical grades, naming Neophyte, Zelator and Practicus in that order and breaking off; each grade is said to carry its own aims and experiences, so a grade's work is read from its place in the run." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, p. 37; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcANeophyte a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Neophyte (Golden Dawn grade)"@en, "Neophyt (Grad der Golden Dawn)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first of the Golden Dawn grades Hine names; like each grade it is said to have had its own magical aims and characteristic mystical experiences."@en ;
    skos:note "Golden Dawn, reported by Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, p. 37; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAZelator a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Zelator (Golden Dawn grade)"@en, "Zelator (Grad der Golden Dawn)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The second of the Golden Dawn grades Hine names, with its own aims and experiences that the text does not specify."@en ;
    skos:note "Golden Dawn, reported by Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, p. 37; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPracticus a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Practicus (Golden Dawn grade)"@en, "Practicus (Grad der Golden Dawn)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The third of the Golden Dawn grades Hine names before breaking off the list, with its own aims and experiences that the text does not specify."@en ;
    skos:note "Golden Dawn, reported by Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, p. 37; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAGradeSystemsBreedAbusiveHierarchyEgoCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Grade systems breed abusive hierarchy and ego inflation"@en, "Gradsysteme fördern missbräuchliche Hierarchie und Ego-Aufblähung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Grading lends itself to abusive authority in groups and ego-inflation in solo magicians; a claimed grade means little unless others recognise it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAGoldenDawnGrades ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, p. 37; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATwoTypesInitiationRitual a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two types of initiation ritual"@en, "Zwei Arten von Initiationsritualen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine divides initiation rituals into self-initiation and group initiation."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Prime Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, p. 37; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAGroupInitiationRecognitionMembership a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Group initiation as recognition of membership"@en, "Gruppeninitiation als Anerkennung der Mitgliedschaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "In groups the rite chiefly marks the end of apprenticeship and full acceptance; triggering inner change may be secondary, though such rites can effectively start a personal initiatory cycle depending on the candidate's treatment before, during and after."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 37; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAYearDayProbationTrainingRegimen a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Year-and-a-day probation with training regimen"@en, "Probezeit von Jahr und Tag mit Übungsprogramm"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before coven initiation the candidate waits a year and a day while group and candidate assess each other, keeping a magical diary and following meditation, yoga, banishing rituals, divination practice and a weekly visit to a natural setting."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine's own Wiccan coven, c. 17 years earlier; common in groups and orders."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, pp. 37-38; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcACovenInitiationRite a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Coven initiation rite (Golden Dawn-based)"@en, "Coven-Initiationsritus (nach Golden-Dawn-Vorlage)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The candidate is led naked and blindfolded into the room, meets a dagger point at the breast, makes symbolic commitments to the coven, the goddess tradition and his own development, receives a magical name for ritual use, and is welcomed with a party after closing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 38; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAStagedRejectionInitiatoryTrial a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Staged rejection as initiatory trial"@en, "Inszenierte Zurückweisung als Initiationsprüfung"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the rite the coven, coldly, told the candidate he was unsuited to magic, would go mad if he continued, and must stop all magical work; nearly two years later he was invited back and reinstated. The real trial was being denied his chosen path by a trusted authority."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine says it was exactly what he needed and that he returned with much more perspective: an anecdote that the working worked."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, pp. 38-39; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAStagedRejectionYieldsPerspective a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Staged rejection yields perspective"@en, "Inszenierte Zurückweisung ergibt Perspektive"@de ;
    skos:definition "The coven's deliberate rejection produced an initiatory crisis from which Hine emerged with perspective."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAStagedRejectionInitiatoryTrial ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPerspectiveGainedThroughInitiatoryCrisis ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 39; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPerspectiveGainedThroughInitiatoryCrisis a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Perspective gained through initiatory crisis"@en, "Durch Initiationskrise gewonnene Perspektive"@de ;
    skos:definition "A good deal of perspective on magic and oneself, gained by being plunged into an initiatory crisis and then left alone to come through."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 39; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAEnduringPainWithoutCryingOut a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Enduring pain without crying out"@en, "Schmerz ertragen ohne aufzuschreien"@de ;
    skos:definition "In some tribal cultures the candidate must endure pain silently; pain is itself a route into gnosis."@en ;
    skos:note "Tribal initiation practice reported generally."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 39; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEnduringPainWithoutYieldsGnosis a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Enduring pain without crying out yields gnosis"@en, "Schmerz ertragen ohne aufzuschreien: Ertrag Gnosis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Enduring pain without crying out is said to yield gnosis."@en ;
    skos:note "Written by the integrator from the link pass A recorded between this practice and capacity; the source states the effect at the practice."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAEnduringPainWithoutCryingOut ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAGnosis ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 39; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAEleusinianDescent a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Eleusinian descent"@en, "Eleusinischer Abstieg"@de ;
    skos:definition "A celebrant readied by fasting and hallucinogens might be lowered into caves where beast-masked priests enacted gods and spirits."@en ;
    skos:note "Eleusinian Mysteries, reported."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 39; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAWildernessMisdirectionTrial a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Wilderness misdirection trial"@en, "Prüfung durch Irreführung in der Wildnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lead and misdirect the candidate across wild country until he stumbles on the chosen spot where the rite culminates."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 39; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAHoldingPlaceAgainstTemptationFear a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Holding a place against temptation or fear"@en, "Einen Ort gegen Versuchung oder Furcht halten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ask the candidate to guard a spot or not to leave it whatever temptations or fears arise."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, pp. 39-40; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAConfrontingTabooSurrenderingAttachment a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Confronting a taboo or surrendering an attachment"@en, "Ein Tabu konfrontieren oder eine Bindung aufgeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The trial makes the candidate face a personal taboo directly or give up a major attachment, e.g. shaving the head."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 40; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcATestSelflessSacrifice a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Test of selfless sacrifice (Moonchild)"@en, "Prüfung selbstloser Opferbereitschaft (Moonchild)"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Crowley's novel Moonchild a protagonist surrenders her freedom believing she aids another woman's escape from a supposedly cruel Order; the test is of selfless sacrifice."@en ;
    skos:note "Aleister Crowley, Moonchild (fiction)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 40; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAForcedChoiceTestIndividualSpirit a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Forced-choice test of individual spirit"@en, "Wahlzwang-Prüfung des eigenen Geistes"@de ;
    skos:definition "The candidate must show commitment by choosing among several courses all involving submission or unpleasantness; refusing all of them despite pressure can count as passing a test of individual spirit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 40; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASurpriseVersusSharedStructureInitiation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Surprise versus shared structure in initiation"@en, "Überraschung gegenüber gemeinsamer Struktur in der Initiation"@de ;
    skos:definition "One school repeats the same rite for every candidate to build shared experience and 'we-ness'; another holds that initiation needs risk, few cues and rites tailored to each candidate, so that heightened awareness lets it strike deep (e.g. no S&M trappings for someone already into S&M)."@en ;
    skos:note "Unnamed schools of thought."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 40; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAHeightenedAwarenessEnablingDeepImpact a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heightened awareness enabling deep impact"@en, "Gesteigerte Wachheit für tiefe Wirkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "A candidate with few cues is in heightened awareness, making it likelier the rite affects him at a deep level."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 40; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAFosteringApprehensionCandidate a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Fostering apprehension in the candidate"@en, "Beklommenheit des Kandidaten fördern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Build apprehension through the group's pre-ritual behaviour; heighten it in the rite with blindfolds, earplugs or other sensory-blocking props and by officers distancing themselves, e.g. addressing the candidate in the third person."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 40; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAFosteringApprehensionCandidateYieldsHeightenedAwarenessEnabling a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Fostering apprehension in the candidate yields heightened awareness enabling deep impact"@en, "Beklommenheit des Kandidaten fördern: Ertrag Gesteigerte Wachheit für tiefe Wirkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fostering apprehension in the candidate is said to yield heightened awareness enabling deep impact."@en ;
    skos:note "Written by the integrator from the link pass A recorded between this practice and capacity; the source states the effect at the practice."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAFosteringApprehensionCandidate ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAHeightenedAwarenessEnablingDeepImpact ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 40; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAClosingWarmWelcomeMutualCommitment a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Closing with warm welcome and mutual commitment"@en, "Abschluss mit herzlichem Empfang und gegenseitiger Verpflichtung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Include elements where candidate and group pledge commitment to each other; at the close celebrants greet the initiate with warmth previously withheld, switching from polite distance to joking and rough-and-tumble."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 41; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABondTrustTriggeringInitiatoryCrisisPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Bond of trust for triggering initiatory crisis"@en, "Vertrauensband zur Auslösung einer Initiationskrise"@de ;
    skos:definition "For a group rite to trigger a personal initiatory crisis there must be trust between candidate and initiator, and the initiator must have observed how the candidate behaves under stress and what event suits him."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABondTrustBetweenCandidateInitiator ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATriggeringPersonalInitiatoryCrisisGroupRite ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Hine sets the bond of trust as a condition of the rite succeeding in setting off a personal initiatory crisis, so without it the rite is not expected to do so; he hedges this with I feel."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 41; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABondTrustBetweenCandidateInitiator a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bond of trust between candidate and initiator"@en, "Vertrauensband zwischen Kandidat und Initiator"@de ;
    skos:definition "Trust between the candidate and whoever orchestrates the initiation, resting on the initiator having watched how the candidate behaves under stress and what event would suit him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 41; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATriggeringPersonalInitiatoryCrisisGroupRite a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Triggering a personal initiatory crisis by a group rite"@en, "Auslösen einer persönlichen Initiationskrise durch ein Gruppenritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "A group initiation rite succeeding in setting off a personal initiatory crisis in the candidate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 41; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADepressionNeurosisInitiatoryCyclesCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Depression and neurosis in initiatory cycles"@en, "Depression und Neurose in Initiationszyklen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Personal initiatory cycles often show depression, uncertainty and degrees of neurosis; trust is especially important after a rite meant to trigger a crisis."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATriggeringPersonalInitiatoryCrisisGroupRite ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 41; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAConfidantThroughInitiatoryCrisis a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Confidant through the initiatory crisis"@en, "Vertrauensperson in der Initiationskrise"@de ;
    skos:definition "Have a trustworthy person, ideally one who has been through the crisis-cycle often, with whom to discuss feelings and perceptions so the initiate finds his own way out."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 41; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAComingSuccessfullyThroughInitiatoryCrisis a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Coming successfully through an initiatory crisis"@en, "Erfolgreiches Durchstehen einer Initiationskrise"@de ;
    skos:definition "Getting through the crisis period, said to be more likely with a trusted confidant."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 41; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAConfidantSupportYieldsPassageThroughCrisis a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Confidant support yields passage through crisis"@en, "Begleitung ergibt Durchgang durch die Krise"@de ;
    skos:definition "A trusted, experienced confidant makes successful passage more likely."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAConfidantThroughInitiatoryCrisis ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAComingSuccessfullyThroughInitiatoryCrisis ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Initiation by a Group, p. 41; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASelfInitiationCentral a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-initiation is central"@en, "Selbstinitiation ist zentral"@de ;
    skos:definition "At some stage the would-be magician must willingly expose himself to initiatory crisis and be ready to undergo such trials repeatedly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Self-Initiation, p. 41; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADedicationRitualMistakenSelfInitiationCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Dedication ritual mistaken for self-initiation"@en, "Weiheritual mit Selbstinitiation verwechselt"@de ;
    skos:definition "A dedication rite can serve as statement of intent, recognition of entering the cycle, or closure, but self-initiation is intense self-discovery requiring hard work, unlikely in Hine's opinion to be settled by a half-hour ritual."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASelfInitiationCentral ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Self-Initiation, pp. 41-42; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAInitiatoryInsightsNotPermanentCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Initiatory insights are not permanent"@en, "Initiatorische Einsichten sind nicht dauerhaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dark-night lows and highs of oneness or ego-loss are normal but transitory; it is a misconception that changes gained in a trial are fixed forever."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASelfInitiationCentral ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Self-Initiation, p. 42; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAActingInsightsThroughSmallChanges a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Acting on insights through small changes"@en, "Einsichten in kleinen Schritten umsetzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Act on insights from initiatory highs and lows and understand them gradually, through minor changes in thinking, speech and action rather than sweeping declarations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Self-Initiation, p. 42; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAgainstLineageGroupInitiationSuperiorDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against lineage and group initiation as superior"@en, "Gegen Abstammungslinie und Gruppeninitiation als höherwertig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine rejects the idea that self-initiation is second-rate or that one is no proper magician or witch outside a group, and questions some modern Wiccans' concern with tracing initiatory lines to an authority: lineage gives continuity but no extra validity; a group can at most point a direction."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the occultists and modern Wiccans he answers are not named or quoted."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Self-Initiation, pp. 42-43; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAGroupsRefugeSelfInitiationCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Groups as refuge from self-initiation"@en, "Gruppen als Zuflucht vor Selbstinitiation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Group membership can suit those unwilling to initiate themselves, who prefer fantasies of power to the labour of appraising and accepting oneself."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASelfInitiationCentral ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Self-Initiation, p. 43; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASignsFirstInitiatoryCrisis a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Signs of the first initiatory crisis"@en, "Anzeichen der ersten Initiationskrise"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first crisis from magical work may show as feeling one's practice leads nowhere, the drying up of early success after a few months, the wish to abandon all exercises, existential doubt and fears of madness; it is elusive and not enjoyable."@en ;
    skos:note "Signs that resemble failure but are read as onset of initiation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Steps Towards Self-Initiation, p. 43; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASensingOnsetInitiatoryCrises a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sensing the onset of initiatory crises"@en, "Das Nahen von Initiationskrisen spüren"@de ;
    skos:definition "With experience one gradually senses crises coming, amplified by dreams, intuition and omens, provided one can read one's personal signs correctly."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInitiatoryCycles (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node is recognising one's own cycles; here the onset is said to be sensed through dream, intuition and omen once one can read one's personal signs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Steps Towards Self-Initiation, p. 43; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcADedicatingMagicalProjectOnesInitiation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dedicating a magical project to one's initiation"@en, "Ein magisches Projekt der eigenen Initiation widmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since any intense magical work is held to lead to initiation, any particular project can be dedicated to furthering it."@en ;
    skos:note "View of some magicians."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Steps Towards Self-Initiation, p. 43; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalRetirementSelfDiscovery a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical retirement for self-discovery"@en, "Magischer Rückzug zur Selbsterkundung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Construct a retirement applying magical techniques intensely to uncover a particular aspect of self, for example creating one's own Alphabet of Desire, or identifying one's demon-horde and binding it."@en ;
    skos:note "Some magicians."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Steps Towards Self-Initiation, pp. 43-44; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPsychoanalysisBeforeSeriousMagicPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Psychoanalysis before serious magic (Regardie)"@en, "Psychoanalyse vor ernsthafter Magie (Regardie)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Regardie recommended psychoanalysis before serious magical practice, and for a time it was a requirement in a Golden Dawn-style order he assisted."@en ;
    skos:note "Israel Regardie; Hine refers to Rebels & Devils."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAPsychoanalysisBeforeSeriousMagic ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASeriousMagicalPractice ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Steps Towards Self-Initiation, p. 44; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAPsychoanalysisBeforeSeriousMagic a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Psychoanalysis before serious magic"@en, "Psychoanalyse vor ernsthafter Magie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Undergo psychoanalysis before taking up serious magical practice."@en ;
    skos:note "Recommended by Israel Regardie, and for a time required in a Golden Dawn-style order he assisted; Hine points to Rebels & Devils."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Steps Towards Self-Initiation, p. 44; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASeriousMagicalPractice a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Serious magical practice"@en, "Ernsthafte magische Praxis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Serious magical practice, which Regardie wanted prefaced by psychoanalysis."@en ;
    skos:note "Israel Regardie, reported by Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Steps Towards Self-Initiation, p. 44; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAEgoMagicChallengingSelfIdentifications a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ego Magic: challenging self-identifications"@en, "Ego-Magie: Selbstidentifikationen herausfordern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Intensely challenge one's own self-identifications, values, beliefs and habits of thought and action to provoke an intrapsychic crisis; must be done authentically, not as an intellectual exercise."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Steps Towards Self-Initiation, p. 44; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAWaitingInitiationPreventsFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Waiting for initiation prevents it"@en, "Auf Initiation warten verhindert sie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unless the aim of initiation is absorbed into the details of practice, one is forever watching for it, whereas it tends to strike only once forgotten."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of self-initiation: unless the aim of initiation is folded into the details of practice, one keeps watching for it, and it tends to arrive only once forgotten. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the operator's attitude. It concerns pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASelfInitiationCentral."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Steps Towards Self-Initiation, p. 44; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcANoTechniqueGuaranteesInitiation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No technique guarantees initiation"@en, "Keine Technik garantiert Initiation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Seekers rush for the most powerful methods to guarantee enlightenment now, but no single practice guarantees successful initiation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Steps Towards Self-Initiation, p. 44; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAExploitationInitiatoryVulnerabilityCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Exploitation of initiatory vulnerability"@en, "Ausnutzung initiatorischer Verletzlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "A guide or friend to talk with helps, but people with agendas, e.g. religious cults recruiting students, use a person's vulnerability to plant their own truths."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAConfidantThroughInitiatoryCrisis ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Steps Towards Self-Initiation, p. 44; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAGuideComeThroughInitiationPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "A guide to come through initiation (view of some magicians)"@en, "Ein Führer, um durch die Initiation zu kommen (Ansicht mancher Magier)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because initiation is so amorphous, some magicians hold that a guide, be it teacher, group or open-minded friends, is needed to get through its periods; Hine grants that a confidant is very helpful."@en ;
    skos:note "Unnamed magicians; no consequence of going without is stated."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAConfidantThroughInitiatoryCrisis ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAComingSuccessfullyThroughInitiatoryCrisis ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Initiation, Steps Towards Self-Initiation, p. 44; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .



#
# Experiments in Belief
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABeliefStructuresRealityBeliefsTools a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Belief structures reality; beliefs as tools"@en, "Glaube strukturiert Wirklichkeit; Überzeugungen als Werkzeuge"@de ;
    skos:definition "A central Chaos Magic assertion is that belief shapes reality and that beliefs serve as tools or conceptual weapons to be drawn on as needed rather than fixed perspectives; a magician-healer can accept both spirits and the allopathic view of an illness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, p. 45; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASeeingFaeries a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing faeries"@en, "Feen sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Believing in faeries is said to make one much more likely to manage to see them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, p. 45; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEgoParamountReality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ego and Paramount Reality"@en, "Ego und vorherrschende Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ego is maintained by dividing what it is from what it is not; attitudes and allegiances reinforce it and sustain an embedded 'Paramount Reality' experienced unreflectively as self-evident truth, built from routines and the expectation that nothing will interrupt; experimenting with beliefs therefore involves other people."@en ;
    skos:note "Term 'Paramount Reality' from Berger & Luckmann."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, pp. 45-46; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAHabitBreakingExercises a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Habit-breaking exercises"@en, "Gewohnheitsbrechende Übungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When routine feels oppressive, write with the non-dominant hand, speak backwards, or delete one habit and replace it with another; eat without TV attending only to sensations and flavours; listen to someone with a blank mind and full attention instead of preparing a reply."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Habits & Routines, p. 46; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAHabitBreakingYieldsConsciousReflection a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Habit-breaking yields conscious reflection"@en, "Gewohnheitsbruch ergibt bewusste Reflexion"@de ;
    skos:definition "The exercises introduce reflection into automatic behaviour."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAHabitBreakingExercises ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAConsciousReflectionAutomaticActs ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Habits & Routines, p. 46; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAConsciousReflectionAutomaticActs a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Conscious reflection in automatic acts"@en, "Bewusste Reflexion in automatischen Handlungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bringing conscious awareness into actions previously done more or less automatically."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Habits & Routines, p. 46; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAHabitBreakingNewGuiltHabitCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Habit-breaking as a new guilt habit"@en, "Gewohnheitsbruch als neue Schuldgewohnheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not treat the gambits as obligatory and feel guilty when forgetting; habits have uses, freeing attention for what matters."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAHabitBreakingExercises ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Habits & Routines, p. 46; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcABreachingSocialRoutine a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Breaching social routine (guest in one's own home)"@en, "Bruch sozialer Routine (Gast im eigenen Zuhause)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Behave at home as though a guest, politely asking permission to use the bathroom or retire; in the reported study parents complained angrily, showing that small changes in social behaviour have far-reaching effects."@en ;
    skos:note "Unnamed American sociologist, 1970s."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Habits & Routines, p. 47; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcALooseEgoComplexAdaptivityTolerance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Loose ego-complex: adaptivity and tolerance"@en, "Lockerer Ich-Komplex: Anpassungsfähigkeit und Toleranz"@de ;
    skos:definition "A looser ego-complex makes one more adaptive and tolerant of new ideas and change, able to understand others' views and to interact across a broad social range without needing consensus; rigid egos suppress, deny or attack dissonance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Habits & Routines, p. 47; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAParadigmShiftChaoteVersion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Paradigm shift (Kuhn) and the chaote version"@en, "Paradigmenwechsel (Kuhn) und die Chaos-Fassung"@de ;
    skos:definition "For Kuhn a paradigm is an exemplary case setting norms for a field and a shift occurs when a new one handles problems better; chaos magicians equate paradigm with world-view and mean by paradigm shift intentional shifts of belief and behaviour into a world-view linked to a lifestyle or belief system."@en ;
    skos:note "Thomas Kuhn, The Structure of Scientific Revolutions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Paradigm Shift, p. 47; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcABeliefShift a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Belief Shift"@en, "Glaubenswechsel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deliberately adopt a world-view and enact it fully in social space: change clothes, speech, self-affirmations, time-sense, habits and social circles, with total involvement in its beliefs and behaviours, like an undercover agent; allow time to settle in, to experience consensus reality wholly within it, and to withdraw and evaluate."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCBeliefShifting (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node is the ability to shift beliefs in feeling and action; here the practice is spelled out as enacting a world-view in social space, with clothes, speech, habits and company, in three stretches of time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Paradigm Shift, pp. 47-48; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABeliefShiftYieldsEmpathyEgoRemoulding a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Belief Shift yields empathy, ego-remoulding and relativity of belief"@en, "Glaubenswechsel ergibt Einfühlung, Ego-Umformung und Relativität des Glaubens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Enacted belief shifts produce empathy, ego-fracturing and, cumulatively, the listed capacities."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcABeliefShift ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEmpathy, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEgoFracturingRemoulding, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcACumulativeEffectsBeliefShifting ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Paradigm Shift, p. 48; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEgoFracturingRemoulding a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ego-fracturing and remoulding"@en, "Aufbrechen und Neuformen des Ego"@de ;
    skos:definition "A deliberate change across several strata of life breaks and reshapes the ego, loosening one's web of beliefs and making one more adaptive."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Paradigm Shift, p. 48; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABeliefPlayOnlyHeadFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Belief play only in the head"@en, "Glaubensspiel nur im Kopf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Toying with beliefs only within one's own head is mere mental masturbation; belief shifts rarely work unless fully enacted within the shared reality of a social setting."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of the Belief Shift: playing with beliefs only inside one's own head is called mental masturbation, and shifts rarely work unless fully enacted in a social space. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the operator. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicPrcABeliefShift."@en, "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCBeliefShiftingTakesTime (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node cautions that belief shifting takes time and is too easy in the head; here enactment in a social space is the condition without which shifts rarely work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Paradigm Shift, p. 48; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAReactionsFriendsPeersCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Reactions of friends and peers"@en, "Reaktionen von Freunden und Gleichgesinnten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The hardest part of a belief shift may be coping with friends' and peers' reactions; one may also find oneself emotionally engaged in the role rather than merely playing it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcABeliefShift ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Paradigm Shift, p. 48; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPhasesEnteringWorldView a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Phases of entering a world-view"@en, "Phasen des Eintritts in eine Weltsicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Establishing oneself comfortably in the world-view; experiencing consensus reality wholly within it; withdrawing and evaluating the experience."@en ;
    skos:note "The stages belong to the Belief Shift (see the practice of that name); no consequence of skipping a stage is named."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:ChaosMagicPrcASettlingWorldView ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:ChaosMagicPrcALivingConsensusRealityWithinWorldView ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAWithdrawingWorldViewEvaluating ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Hine says entering a world-view takes time in three stretches, each named in turn: settling in comfortably, living consensus reality wholly within it, and withdrawing to evaluate; evaluation has its sense only after the world-view has been lived in." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Paradigm Shift, p. 48; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcASettlingWorldView a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Settling into a world-view"@en, "Sich in einer Weltsicht einrichten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first stretch of time in a Belief Shift: establishing oneself comfortably within the chosen world-view."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Paradigm Shift, p. 48; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcALivingConsensusRealityWithinWorldView a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Living consensus reality within the world-view"@en, "Konsensrealität ganz in der Weltsicht erleben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The second stretch of time in a Belief Shift: experiencing consensus reality wholly from inside the adopted world-view."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Paradigm Shift, p. 48; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAWithdrawingWorldViewEvaluating a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Withdrawing from the world-view and evaluating"@en, "Rückzug aus der Weltsicht und Auswertung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The last stretch of time in a Belief Shift: withdrawing from the world-view and evaluating the experience."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Paradigm Shift, p. 48; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAQuestioningSelfEvidentTruthsFirstStagePrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Questioning self-evident truths as first stage"@en, "Infragestellen der Selbstverständlichkeiten als erste Stufe"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first stage of a belief shift is beginning to question self-evident truths and experience consensus reality as fragile, one's own beliefs as props like others'."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAExperiencingConsensusRealityFragile ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcABeliefShift ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Paradigm Shift, pp. 48-49; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAExperiencingConsensusRealityFragile a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Experiencing consensus reality as fragile"@en, "Konsensrealität als brüchig erfahren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Questioning the self-evident truths of one's world and experiencing consensus reality as fragile, one's own beliefs as much a prop as anyone else's."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Paradigm Shift, pp. 48-49; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAnxietyQuestioningCultRecruitmentCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Anxiety of questioning and cult recruitment"@en, "Angst des Infragestellens und Sektenwerbung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Questioning consensus reality brings anxiety and alienation; many resolve it by adopting an ideology of false solid ground, and religious and quasi-magical cults deliberately target such people."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAExperiencingConsensusRealityFragile ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Paradigm Shift, p. 49; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEgoMappingBeforeBeliefShiftPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Ego Mapping before Belief Shift"@en, "Ego-Kartierung vor Glaubenswechsel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Preparing to storm the fortress of one's identity, a ground plan (ego map) is useful first."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAEgoMapping ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcABeliefShift ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Ego Mapping, p. 49; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAEgoMapping a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ego Mapping"@en, "Ego-Kartierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before a belief shift, articulate one's beliefs, attitudes, attractive and repellent ideologies, strengths, weaknesses, fears, ego-propping fantasies, desires, dreams and nightmares; write an account of oneself as one is, as one would like to be and as others see one; trawl personal history for turning points, successes, failures, embarrassments, traumas and ecstasies; optionally write in the third person or an obituary set now or ten years ahead."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Ego Mapping, p. 49; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASeeingOnesWorldViewAmongMany a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing one's world-view as one among many"@en, "Die eigene Weltsicht als eine unter vielen sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Understanding that the world-view tacitly taken as true is just one among many in a complex culture."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Ego Mapping, p. 49; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEgoMappingYieldsRelativisedWorldView a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Ego Mapping yields relativised world-view"@en, "Ego-Kartierung ergibt relativierte Weltsicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "As mapping gains momentum one grasps one's world-view as one of many."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAEgoMapping ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASeeingOnesWorldViewAmongMany ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Ego Mapping, p. 49; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAShiftOpposedWorldView a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Shift into an opposed world-view"@en, "Wechsel in eine gegnerische Weltsicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "As a first belief shift, move into a world-view diametrically opposed to one heavily invested in, e.g. a change of political ideology, becoming one of the stereotyped 'others' to challenge one's former truth."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Ego Mapping, p. 49; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAOpposedWorldViewShiftRiskyCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Opposed-world-view shift is risky"@en, "Wechsel in gegnerische Weltsicht ist riskant"@de ;
    skos:definition "Such a shift is risky since it affects all of one's lifestyle, especially relations with family, friends and peers."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAShiftOpposedWorldView ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Ego Mapping, p. 49; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcASubBeliefShiftsBetweenMagicalSystems a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sub-Belief Shifts between magical systems"@en, "Teil-Glaubenswechsel zwischen magischen Systemen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Within a specific context, enter a magical perspective (e.g. witchcraft, Theosophy, Voudoun), work within its parameters until they feel true, then move to another; done over time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Sub-Belief Shifts, p. 50; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASubBeliefShiftsYieldsMagicalModelsTools a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Sub-Belief Shifts between magical systems yields magical models as tools"@en, "Teil-Glaubenswechsel zwischen magischen Systemen: Ertrag Magische Modelle als Werkzeuge"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sub-Belief Shifts between magical systems is said to yield magical models as tools."@en ;
    skos:note "Written by the integrator from the link pass A recorded between this practice and capacity; the source states the effect at the practice."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcASubBeliefShiftsBetweenMagicalSystems ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalModelsTools ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Sub-Belief Shifts, p. 50; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalModelsTools a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical models as tools"@en, "Magische Modelle als Werkzeuge"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recognition that magical belief systems are structures for organising and integrating experience rather than true descriptions, so they become tools; Chaos magicians favour a broad range of conceptual weapons."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Sub-Belief Shifts, p. 50; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAWorkingSystemOverTimePrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Working a system over time"@en, "Ein System über Zeit bearbeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reaching the view of models as tools successfully requires working with a chosen system over time."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcASubBeliefShiftsBetweenMagicalSystems ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalModelsTools ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Sub-Belief Shifts, p. 50; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAChaosDrawsAnyFieldBuildsNew a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Chaos draws on any field and builds new perspectives"@en, "Chaos schöpft aus jedem Gebiet und schafft neue Perspektiven"@de ;
    skos:definition "Chaos magic takes inspiration from any human endeavour (cybernetics, science fiction, biology, non-linear dynamics) and creates perspectives from current ideas and possible futures instead of recycling the past."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Sub-Belief Shifts, pp. 50-51; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcACumulativeEffectsBeliefShifting a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cumulative effects of Belief Shifting"@en, "Kumulative Wirkungen des Glaubenswechsels"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deep grasp of the relativity of all beliefs; ability to adopt a stance consciously and weave a projective glamour from it for self and others; accepting new ideas without feeling threatened; living comfortably in many roles and selves; being wrong or contradictory without serious ego damage."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Sub-Belief Shifts, p. 51; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABeliefShiftingYieldsExoCentricBehaviour a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Belief Shifting yields exo-centric behaviour"@en, "Glaubenswechsel ergibt exozentrisches Verhalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Belief Shifting practised on every level is said to bring the transition from ego-centric to exo-centric behaviour."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcABeliefShift ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEgoToExo ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Sub-Belief Shifts, p. 51; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABoundDemonSelvesRoutesPower a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bound demon-selves as routes into power"@en, "Gebundene Dämonen-Selbste als Zugänge zur Macht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Identifying and accepting what one found fearful, distasteful or unacceptable in oneself; once faced and bound, these demon-selves become routes into power."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Sub-Belief Shifts, p. 51; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAFacingDemonSelvesExoCentricShiftPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Facing the demon-selves for the exo-centric shift"@en, "Begegnung mit den Dämonen-Selbsten für den exozentrischen Wechsel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The move to exo-centric behaviour is said further to require identifying and accepting what one has found fearful, distasteful and unacceptable in oneself."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABoundDemonSelvesRoutesPower ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEgoToExo ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Sub-Belief Shifts, p. 51; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASocialMobilitySelfReassessmentBeliefShiftingPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Social mobility and self-reassessment for belief shifting"@en, "Soziale Beweglichkeit und Selbstprüfung für Glaubenswechsel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The practice requires moving without constraint in one's Social World and continually reassessing one's Personal World."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMovingFreelyOnesSocialWorld ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcABeliefShift ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Sub-Belief Shifts, p. 51; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMovingFreelyOnesSocialWorld a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Moving freely in one's social world"@en, "Sich frei in der eigenen sozialen Welt bewegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to move without constraint in one's Social World while continually reassessing one's Personal World."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Sub-Belief Shifts, p. 51; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAGoingAway a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Going Away"@en, "Fortgehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Travel to adopt belief shifts where few people know one's 'normal' identity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Useful Gambits, Going Away, p. 51; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcASelfObservation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-Observation"@en, "Selbstbeobachtung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Observe oneself dispassionately to see how one creates, projects and maintains an identity, as a continual meditation; watch how others react to willed identity projection and how they maintain their own identities."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Useful Gambits, Self-Observation, pp. 51-52; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAwarenessIdentityMaintenanceBeforeAlteringPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Awareness of identity maintenance before altering it"@en, "Bewusstsein der Identitätserhaltung vor ihrer Veränderung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Awareness of how identity is maintained is called essential for altering one's projection at will."@en ;
    skos:note "Called essential, but no consequence of lacking it is stated."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcASelfObservation ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAlteringIdentityProjectionWill ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Useful Gambits, Self-Observation, p. 51; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAlteringIdentityProjectionWill a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Altering identity projection at will"@en, "Identitätsprojektion willentlich verändern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ability to change the identity one projects deliberately."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Useful Gambits, Self-Observation, pp. 51-52; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAShockTactics a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Shock Tactics"@en, "Schocktaktik"@de ;
    skos:definition "Exploit people's tendency to attribute others' behaviour to personality: when someone has labelled you (e.g. as liberal), choose the right moment to voice the opposite view, giving them a considerable shock."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Useful Gambits, Shock Tactics, p. 52; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAShockTacticsYieldsEnhancedPersonalPower a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Shock Tactics yields enhanced personal power and hidden-agenda collusion"@en, "Schocktaktik: Ertrag Gesteigerte persönliche Macht und Scheinbündnis mit verdeckter Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shock Tactics is said to yield enhanced personal power and hidden-agenda collusion."@en ;
    skos:note "Written by the integrator from the link pass A recorded between this practice and capacity; the source states the effect at the practice."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAShockTactics ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEnhancedPersonalPowerHiddenAgendaCollusion ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Useful Gambits, Shock Tactics, p. 52; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEnhancedPersonalPowerHiddenAgendaCollusion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Enhanced personal power and hidden-agenda collusion"@en, "Gesteigerte persönliche Macht und Scheinbündnis mit verdeckter Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shock tactics may be used to increase personal power or to seem to collude with someone while keeping a hidden agenda."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Useful Gambits, Shock Tactics, p. 52; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPersonalBeliefWebChaosMagicNot a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Personal belief-web; Chaos Magic not an overall belief system"@en, "Persönliches Glaubensnetz; Chaosmagie kein Gesamtglaubenssystem"@de ;
    skos:definition "Belief shifting gradually builds a web of personally meaningful beliefs, ethical stances and a mobile identity, expected to change; Chaos magicians can simultaneously identify with other systems (Hine with free-form shamanism and Tantra)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Useful Gambits, pp. 52-53; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASelfPresentedAcrossLifeWorlds a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self as presented across life-worlds"@en, "Das Selbst als Darstellung über Lebenswelten hinweg"@de ;
    skos:definition "The 'real me' is shown to varying degrees in all the life-worlds we inhabit but fully realised in none; status comes from social constructions while identity comes from resisting total participation in them."@en ;
    skos:note "Paraphrase of Erving Goffman."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Identity & Self, p. 53; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMultiplicitySelves a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Multiplicity of selves"@en, "Vielheit der Selbste"@de ;
    skos:definition "A notion favoured by some Chaos magicians: there is no one self but a cluster of selves, and instead of fixing the 'fiction' of a true self one gives free rein to the many; Bandler and Grinder (NLP) say we are all multiple personalities."@en ;
    skos:note "Bandler & Grinder; Lacan's term 'fiction' of the true self."@en, "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCLegionOfSelves (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node puts the self as a multiplicity of identities in Hine's voice with a Tantric image; here it is reported as a notion of some Chaos magicians, taken further by Bandler and Grinder."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Identity & Self, p. 53; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcANoCoreBehindMasksPlayBeliefs a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No core behind the masks: play with beliefs and identities"@en, "Kein Kern hinter den Masken: Spiel mit Überzeugungen und Identitäten"@de ;
    skos:definition "If selfhood emerges from movement through social zones with no core behind the masks, one is freed from asserting oneself against others; the radical Chaos stance is to stop seeking truth, have fun with beliefs and enjoy many identities, and to transform everyday life by re-injecting the marvellous rather than transcending it. The slogan that nothing is true and all is permitted can be read as pessimism or, after Burroughs, as a call to life as art and play."@en ;
    skos:note "Burroughs cited for the second reading; Crowley given as model."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Identity & Self, p. 54; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcACrowleyModelWhollyMagicalLife a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Crowley as model of a wholly magical life"@en, "Crowley als Vorbild eines ganz magischen Lebens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine praises Crowley for making his entire life magical by casting himself in grand roles against a pale backdrop of normality, for refusing definition, total engagement and uncompromising choice of the life he wanted."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Identity & Self, pp. 54-56; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcACrowleyWannabesCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Crowley-wannabes"@en, "Crowley-Nachahmer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imitators who copy Crowley's heroin habit and deception of the weak, too weak to find out who they are, live in his shadow; Crowley also demanded total surrender from followers and madness and suicide followed him."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcACrowleyModelWhollyMagicalLife ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Identity & Self, p. 55; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMultipleSelvesAgainstNeoplatonicTrueSelfDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Multiple selves against the Neoplatonic True Self"@en, "Vielheit der Selbste gegen das neuplatonische wahre Selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "The multiple-selves view contrasts with the Neoplatonic idea of a part of us sharing in the Absolute, on which much magical theory rests; without a True Self, True Will and the Holy Guardian Angel are questioned, and Carroll and Dave Lee have argued the HGA is nearing obsolescence from the Chaos perspective."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: Neoplatonic theory is characterised, not quoted, and Carroll and Lee are cited for the obsolescence of the Holy Guardian Angel without their words."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Identity & Self, p. 56; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAHolyGuardianAngelMaskVoidNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Holy Guardian Angel as Mask of the Void"@en, "Heiliger Schutzengel als Maske der Leere"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine does not treat the HGA as a distinct being but as a passing mask of the Void, a gateway to inspiration and illumination whose form changes with his interests."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBHolyGuardianAngelNaming (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node gives the traditional view of the HGA as an aspect of the Lamp; here Hine treats it as a passing mask of the Void, not a distinct being."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Holy Guardian Angel (HGA)" ;
    pm:nameRole "temporary mask of the Void; gateway to inspiration" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The HGA, Mask of the Void, pp. 56-57; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAInnerGeniusThroughSelfNegation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner genius through self-negation (Moonchild)"@en, "Inneres Genie durch Selbstnegation (Moonchild)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Crowley in Moonchild suggests a man makes himself a negative and lets his genius come through as it will; Hine relates the HGA to this."@en ;
    skos:note "Aleister Crowley, Moonchild, loosely recalled."@en, "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPersonalGenius (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node lists names for the creative wellspring and calls Moonchild the most useful reference; here the Moonchild remark on making oneself a negative is given as the key to the HGA."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The HGA, Mask of the Void, p. 56; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAzooraNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Azoora"@en, "Azoora"@de ;
    skos:definition "For a time Hine's HGA took the character of a shadowy woman named Azoora; this changed as his magical interests shifted."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Azoora" ;
    pm:nameRole "temporary personification of Hine's HGA" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The HGA, Mask of the Void, p. 57; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAContactsHigherEntitiesDevolveObsessionCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Contacts with higher entities devolve into obsession"@en, "Kontakte mit höheren Wesen entarten zur Besessenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine has seen contact with so-called higher entities turn fast into pathological obsession, degrading the information received, and so keeps his idea of the HGA deliberately ephemeral."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAHolyGuardianAngelMaskVoidNaming ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The HGA, Mask of the Void, p. 57; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcALAMNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "LAM"@en, "LAM"@de ;
    skos:definition "Crowley's entity LAM, called 'the voice of the silence', which Hine finds an apt image of the HGA as a voice of many forms and tongues."@en ;
    skos:note "Crowley's portrait of LAM."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "LAM" ;
    pm:nameRole "voice of the silence; image of the HGA" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The HGA, Mask of the Void, p. 57; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcACreatingMagicalSelf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating a Magical Self"@en, "Erschaffung eines magischen Selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Decide which qualities, abilities and skills you want to acquire and create a role encapsulating them; wear this persona-mask at every act of magic, linked to a symbol, adornment or garment; each act reinforces the role. Design it for qualities you lack, not those you already have in abundance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Magical Self: An Exercise in Empowerment, p. 57; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalSelfYieldsEmpowerment a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Magical Self yields empowerment"@en, "Magisches Selbst ergibt Ermächtigung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wearing the Magical Self invokes the desired future qualities."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcACreatingMagicalSelf, pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAAdoptingMagicalName ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEmpowermentTowardFutureSelf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Magical Self: An Exercise in Empowerment, p. 57; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAAdoptingMagicalName a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Adopting a magical name"@en, "Annahme eines magischen Namens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Choose a name or motto associated with magical concepts reflecting one's aspirations and identify with it, thereby invoking the Magical Self; the name may change as one develops. Example: PACHAD, Hebrew 'Fear', a title of Geburah (Mars), for a magician seeking a martial current."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Magical Self: An Exercise in Empowerment, p. 57; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPersonaReinforcingExistingQualitiesFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Persona reinforcing existing qualities"@en, "Persona, die vorhandene Eigenschaften verstärkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "There is little point designing a magical persona that only reinforces qualities one already has in abundance."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of the Magical Self: a persona that only reinforces qualities one already has in abundance is of little point. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the operator's design. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicPrcACreatingMagicalSelf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Magical Self: An Exercise in Empowerment, p. 57; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEmpowermentTowardFutureSelf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Empowerment toward a future self"@en, "Ermächtigung zu einem künftigen Selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Invocation of a future otherness: developing abilities and powers one senses the need for but lacks."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Magical Self: An Exercise in Empowerment, p. 57; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASecretMagicianPersonaVersusMagicalWhole a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Secret magician-persona versus magical whole life"@en, "Geheime Magier-Persona gegenüber ganz magischem Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Classical theory keeps the magician-persona apart as a secret life revealed only to initiates; if magic is a thread through all of life, the distinct Magician Self blurs without weakening, as the whole life becomes magical. The Magical Self is a heuristic device."@en ;
    skos:note "Classical magical theory reported."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Magical Self: An Exercise in Empowerment, pp. 57-58; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAGraduatedProgressionMagicalIdentity a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Graduated progression of magical identity"@en, "Stufenweise Entwicklung magischer Identität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magic as something one is interested in; something one is engrossed by; being a magician practically full time."@en ;
    skos:note "The progression goes with a shift from Ego to Exo and with a shrinking social group that reinforces the identity; no consequence of skipping a step is named."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicInterest ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEngrossedMagic ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABeingMagicianAlmostFullTime ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Working within a magical psychocosm, Hine says identity moves by a graduated progression from magic as an interest, to being engrossed by it, to being a full-time magician in all but name; each step marks how far identity has become interwoven with magic." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Magical Self: An Exercise in Empowerment, p. 58; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicInterest a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magic as an interest"@en, "Magie als Interesse"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first step of the progression of magical identity: magic as something one is interested in."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Magical Self, p. 58; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEngrossedMagic a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Engrossed by magic"@en, "Von Magie gefesselt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The middle step of the progression of magical identity: magic as something that engrosses one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Magical Self, p. 58; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABeingMagicianAlmostFullTime a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being a magician almost full time"@en, "Fast ganz Magier sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The last step of the progression of magical identity: being a magician nearly all the time, with identity interwoven with one's magic."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, The Magical Self, p. 58; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEscapeRoutesDeadEndsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Escape routes are dead ends"@en, "Fluchtwege sind Sackgassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drugs, sex, fantasy, ideologies, therapies, utopias and even 'revolutionary' routes including magic offer escape from consensus reality but prove dead ends that feed the illusion of escape and are recuperated into fashion."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEscapeRoutes (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node calls magic the great escape route; here magical endeavour is listed among the revolutionary escape routes that prove dead ends, while the Chaos approach turns consensus reality into a playground."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSelfLove ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Self Love, p. 59; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcABringingShardsPandaemonaeonEarth a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bringing shards of the Pandaemonaeon to earth"@en, "Splitter des Pandaemonaeon auf die Erde bringen"@de ;
    skos:definition "From Self Love, treating consensus reality as a playground for manifesting will and desire, the magician can begin bringing to earth whatever parts of the Pandaemonaeon, and beyond, engage his attention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Experiments in Belief, Self Love, p. 59; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .



#
# Microaeonics
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAOccultistsFabricatedHistoriesCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Occultists' fabricated histories"@en, "Erfundene Geschichtsbilder der Okkultisten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Occultists commonly edit selectively and sometimes fabricate historical evidence to support their models; results are biased though sometimes useful pointers."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine applies the warning to his own tour, calling its results incomplete and biased but sometimes useful."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMicroaeonics ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, p. 60; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMicroaeonicSuccessionMagicalParadigms a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Microaeonic succession of magical paradigms"@en, "Mikroäonische Abfolge magischer Paradigmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tribal shamanic aeon (otherworld fused with landscape, participation mystique); Pagan aeon (priesthood mediates, pantheons supplant elder gods); Monotheist aeon (personal soul, three worlds pushed apart, heresy); Modernist phase (Crowley as Faustian avatar); Postmodernism with its magical ethos, Chaos Magic; the projected Fifth Aeon, the Pandemonaeon."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine's own tour, explicitly selective. Pages 62-63 are missing from the text layer, so the passage from monotheism to the Modernist phase is partly unread; the text calls the Pandemonaeon the Fifth Aeon, which this list of six named stages does not reconcile. No consequence of skipping is named."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATribalShamanicOtherworld ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPaganAeon ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMonotheistAeon ;
    rdf:_4 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAModernistPhase ;
    rdf:_5 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPostmodernismMagicalEthosChaosMagic ;
    rdf:_6 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPandemonaeon ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Hine's brief tour through the aeons runs from the tribal shamanic otherworld through the Pagan Aeon and monotheism to the Modernist phase, then to Postmodernism with Chaos Magic as its ethos, and on to the projected Pandemonaeon; each stage is read from its place as a further step in how far the personal, social and mythic worlds are pushed apart." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, pp. 60-67; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMicroaeonics a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Microaeonics (Hine's aeon model)"@en, "Mikroäonik (Hines Äonenmodell)"@de ;
    skos:definition "An author-made model relating each social stage to the relation of individual and society and to the dominant magical paradigm, from tribal shamanism to the Pandemonaeon."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Prime Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, p. 60; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATribalShamanicOtherworld a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tribal shamanic otherworld"@en, "Stammesschamanische Anderwelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first stage of Hine's tour: early tribal societies with an otherworld interpenetrating the local landscape and tied to hunting, gathering, ancestors, local spirits and taboo; personal, social and mythic worlds are fused in participation mystique."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, p. 60; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPaganAeon a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pagan Aeon"@en, "Heidnisches Äon"@de ;
    skos:definition "The second stage: with agriculture, cities and trade a specialised priesthood mediates the otherworld, state myths split from older lore, and new pantheons supplant or demonise older ones, as the Olympians did the Titans; the worlds of experience still overlap closely."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, p. 60; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMonotheistAeon a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Monotheist aeon"@en, "Monotheistisches Äon"@de ;
    skos:definition "The third stage: the move to monotheism separates the personal, social and mythic worlds as the priesthood regulates mythic experience, the personal soul rises, transgressions become heresies, and private confession replaces communal penance."@en ;
    skos:note "Its passage into the modern era falls partly in pages 62-63, which are missing from the text layer read."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, pp. 60-61; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAModernistPhase a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Modernist phase"@en, "Moderne Phase"@de ;
    skos:definition "The stage of the early twentieth century, summed up for occultists by Crowley as the Faustian figure of the Modernist world, destroying old values to build anew; it runs through the inter-war search for a total myth to the Second World War."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, p. 64; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAWarningAgainstSingleTotalVisionCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Warning against a single total vision"@en, "Warnung vor einer einzigen Gesamtvision"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Modernist vision's demonic face (machine rationalism fused with total myth in National Socialism) warns against building one overall vision and realising it at any cost; utopian futures remain a powerful glamour."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAModernistPhase ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, p. 64; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPostmodernismMagicalEthosChaosMagic a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Postmodernism and its magical ethos, Chaos Magic"@en, "Postmoderne und ihr magisches Ethos, die Chaosmagie"@de ;
    skos:definition "The current stage: a multi-cultural, collage-like culture without overall narrative, whose emergent magical ethos is Chaos Magic and whose fitting slogan is Mutate and Survive."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, pp. 65-66; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPostmodernAgeWhichMagicMayThrive a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Postmodern age in which magic may thrive"@en, "Postmodernes Zeitalter, in dem Magie gedeihen kann"@de ;
    skos:definition "Postmodernism is a fragmentary, collage-like culture without overall narrative; scientific glamours for magic can be seen as passing language games or tactics to make free areas for manipulating belief and image; the slogan of the age is Mutate and Survive, and magic becomes a survival approach."@en ;
    skos:note "Cites an unnamed speaker at a ley-line conference: stop seeking facts, believe what you like, have fun."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, pp. 65-66; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPandemonaeon a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Pandemonaeon"@en, "Das Pandemonaeon"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Fifth Aeon projected by some Chaos magicians, different for every individual who projects himself into it, embracing rather than resisting the modern condition, probably itself transitory; some find it useful for going beyond accepted definitions of the magical, and later magi may discard it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Approaching the PandemonAeon, p. 67; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicalFunctionsNewAeon a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical functions of a new aeon"@en, "Magische Funktionen eines neuen Äons"@de ;
    skos:definition "A new-aeon concept serves as a filter for examining and influencing social trends; as an Ideosphere for developing ideas beyond present Achievable Reality; and as a meta-aim unifying groups and helping design possible futures."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Approaching the PandemonAeon, p. 67; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAWorkingIdeosphere a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Working from the Ideosphere"@en, "Arbeiten aus der Ideosphäre"@de ;
    skos:definition "Adopt an attitude open to inspiration from any incoming information (news, cartoons, media images, jargon, acronyms, overheard phrases), rejecting nothing however absurd; seize ideas or store them; immerse in mass media until sated, then withdraw into silence to digest and create new forms."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Ideospheres, p. 68; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcANewParadigmsTechniques a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "New paradigms and techniques"@en, "Neue Paradigmen und Techniken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fresh perspectives on existing models, new paradigms for ordering magical processes, and from them new techniques and applications."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Ideospheres, p. 68; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAIdeosphereYieldsNewParadigms a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Ideosphere yields new paradigms"@en, "Ideosphäre ergibt neue Paradigmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Latching onto ideas from the Ideosphere produces new perspectives and techniques."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAWorkingIdeosphere ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcANewParadigmsTechniques ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Ideospheres, p. 68; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAVirusSystems a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Virus systems"@en, "Virensysteme"@de ;
    skos:definition "A virus is an instruction set that invades a larger system, makes it replicate the virus and alters the host; this holds for computer, biological and word viruses (memes), and opens new magical understanding and applications."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Virus Systems, p. 68; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMemesPerformanceValuePropagationQuotient a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Memes, Performance Value and Propagation Quotient"@en, "Meme, Leistungswert und Verbreitungsquotient"@de ;
    skos:definition "Memes replicate, recombine and mutate, competing for attention; their success depends on Performance Value (the change they bring, e.g. cohesion and confidence) and Propagation Quotient; the most successful reduce anxiety by giving purpose or place. Complexes of memes are Schemes, e.g. religions, which become the host's world; alienated people are ripe hosts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, The Word Virus, pp. 69-70; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAControlCommands a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Control Commands"@en, "Steuerbefehle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Understanding meme spread leads to Control Commands, automatic responses locked into language and thought; Pandemonaeonic magicians design new ways of conceptualising and meta-languages to escape old habits of thinking."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, The Word Virus, p. 70; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcADeletingSemanticTraps a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Deleting semantic traps (THE, IS, EITHER/OR)"@en, "Semantische Fallen tilgen (DER, IST, ENTWEDER/ODER)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Remove from one's language the definite article, the 'is' of identity that fixes labels, and either/or thinking, so that many possibilities open none of which need be right or wrong."@en ;
    skos:note "William S. Burroughs' targets."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, The Word Virus, p. 70; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcADeletingIOnesLanguage a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Deleting 'I' from one's language"@en, "'Ich' aus der eigenen Sprache streichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Eliminate the word 'I' from speech so that without a dominant I a legion of selves can appear."@en ;
    skos:note "Crowley urged this on his students; Hine endorses it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, The Word Virus, p. 70; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADeletingSemanticTrapsYieldsFreedThinking a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Deleting semantic traps yields freed thinking"@en, "Tilgen semantischer Fallen ergibt befreites Denken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dropping 'I', 'the', 'is' and either/or opens multiple selves and possibilities."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcADeletingSemanticTraps, pmp:ChaosMagicPrcADeletingIOnesLanguage ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEscapingHabitualThoughtLoosingDaemons ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, The Word Virus, p. 70; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEscapingHabitualThoughtLoosingDaemons a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Escaping habitual thought; loosing the daemons"@en, "Gewohntem Denken entkommen; die Dämonen entfesseln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Release from narrow language-bound thinking, letting a legion of selves and a myriad of possibilities emerge."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, The Word Virus, p. 70; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAViralTextsEnemyGroupMessagesCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Viral texts and enemy-group messages"@en, "Virale Texte und Feindgruppen-Botschaften"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beware anyone who seriously acts on viral messages of the type 'group x is doing y to z', which demand concern and action and rely on hosts needing an enemy; once rooted they let in the memes of Getting Even and Being Right, which are sources of destructive behaviour. Chain letters are the simplest form."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMemesPerformanceValuePropagationQuotient ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Viral Texts, pp. 70-71; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAgainstOrthodoxInsistenceUniqueMagicalObjectsDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against orthodox insistence on unique magical objects"@en, "Gegen das orthodoxe Beharren auf einzigartigen magischen Gegenständen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Orthodox magic prizes unique talismans, virgin parchment and purpose-made objects; Hine counters that mass production also holds power."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: orthodox magic is characterised, not quoted from a named work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Replicants, p. 71; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAChaospheresGateways a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Chaospheres as gateways"@en, "Chaossphären als Tore"@de ;
    skos:definition "By a shift of perception, treat every mass-reproduced chaosphere (on books, jewellery, posters, jackets) as a gateway through which magical power flows in and out."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Replicants, p. 71; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAChaospheresGatewaysYieldsMassProducedImages a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Chaospheres as gateways yields mass-produced images as power gateways"@en, "Chaossphären als Tore: Ertrag Massenbilder als Machttore"@de ;
    skos:definition "Chaospheres as gateways is said to yield mass-produced images as power gateways."@en ;
    skos:note "Written by the integrator from the link pass A recorded between this practice and capacity; the source states the effect at the practice."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAChaospheresGateways ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMassProducedImagesPowerGateways ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Replicants, p. 71; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMassProducedImagesPowerGateways a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mass-produced images as power gateways"@en, "Massenbilder als Machttore"@de ;
    skos:definition "Thousands of reproduced glyphs become channels for magical power."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Replicants, p. 71; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAGonkSpirit a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Gonk-spirit"@en, "Gonk-Geist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take a mass-produced figure (a small plastic 'Gonk') as receptacle, enchant upon it so that by structural similarity all Gonks receive the information, creating a Gonk-spirit embodying the marketed image; one's own Gonk becomes the controller."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Replicants, p. 71; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPrincipleStructuralSimilarity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Principle of Structural-Similarity"@en, "Prinzip der strukturellen Ähnlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Enchanting one object transmits the information to all objects of similar structure; any object becomes magical once the magician defines it so, combining image, associations and will."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Replicants, pp. 71-72; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAGonkEnchantmentYieldsReplicaPower a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Gonk enchantment yields replica power"@en, "Gonk-Verzauberung ergibt Kopienkraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Empowering one Gonk empowers all and lets the controller draw on them."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAGonkSpirit ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADrawingPowerAllReplicas ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Replicants, p. 71; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADrawingPowerAllReplicas a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Drawing power from all replicas"@en, "Kraft aus allen Kopien ziehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In need, the sorcerer can draw the power of all the other Gonks through his own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Replicants, p. 71; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAPhotocopiedSigilDispersal a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Photocopied sigil dispersal"@en, "Fotokopierte Sigillen verstreuen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sigilise a desire; instead of destroying the sigil, photocopy it and disperse the copies at random."@en ;
    skos:note "Example given: a young man seeking a lover; lovers appeared from all directions (reported outcome, success)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Replicants, p. 71; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAttractingLovers a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Attracting lovers"@en, "Liebhaber anziehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drawing lovers, said in the example to arrive from all directions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Replicants, p. 71; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADispersedSigilYieldsLovers a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dispersed sigil yields lovers"@en, "Verstreute Sigille ergibt Liebhaber"@de ;
    skos:definition "Random dispersal of copied sigils brought lovers."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAPhotocopiedSigilDispersal ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAttractingLovers ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Replicants, p. 71; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAViralServitors a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Viral servitors"@en, "Virale Servitoren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Servitors able to replicate, mutate and recombine, reported to be propagating in virtual space performing healing, protection, and the seeding of ideas into the meme-pool."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBViralSelfReplicatingServitors (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 practice instructs a servitor to multiply; here viral servitors are reported as already propagating in virtual space, healing, protecting and seeding ideas."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Viral Servitors, p. 72; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAProjectingCHAOSVirus a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Projecting the CHAOS Virus"@en, "Projektion des C.H.A.O.S.-Virus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Project the virus using the chaosphere as icon and gateway; thereafter every chaosphere (astral, image or object), and by structural similarity anything like a circle crossed by eight vectors, transmits it; it can be reinforced by seeded memes, image projections, enchantments or sonic sorcery."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, The C.H.A.O.S Virus, pp. 72-73; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAWeakenedEgoResistanceChange a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Weakened ego-resistance to change"@en, "Geschwächter Ich-Widerstand gegen Wandel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The virus stimulates selves desiring change, pleasure, new ideas, adaptability, intelligence and fun, copying itself each time one stirs; over time it weakens ego resistance, and its cells combine in eights into virtual shadows of selves yet to be."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, The C.H.A.O.S Virus, p. 72; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcACHAOSVirusYieldsOpennessChange a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "CHAOS Virus yields openness to change"@en, "C.H.A.O.S.-Virus ergibt Offenheit für Wandel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The projected virus weakens ego-resistance and seeds new selves."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAProjectingCHAOSVirus ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAWeakenedEgoResistanceChange ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, The C.H.A.O.S Virus, p. 72; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAJargonBarrierCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Jargon as barrier"@en, "Fachsprache als Barriere"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magical technical language, like any specialist terminology, can become so opaque that it shuts out everyone outside the group."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMetaLanguagesPrecision ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Meta-Languages, p. 73; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMetaLanguagesPrecision a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Meta-languages for precision"@en, "Metasprachen für Genauigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magicians are said to create meta-languages both as tools for acts of magic and to reach nuances of experience that current language describes poorly, aiming at greater precision of communication."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Meta-Languages, p. 73; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATelepathicAstralCommunication a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Telepathic and astral communication"@en, "Telepathische und astrale Verständigung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Transmitting images, colours and pictographs between people in dream or astral space; experiments are said to suggest these pass more easily than words."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Meta-Languages, p. 73; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAWordlessCommunicationSystemsDreamAstralWork a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Wordless communication systems for dream and astral work"@en, "Wortlose Kommunikationssysteme für Traum- und Astralarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Build communication codes from colours, spatial perspectives, contextual imagery and settings for telepathy experiments, shared dreaming or linking awareness in astral space."@en ;
    skos:note "Attempts by unnamed magicians."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Meta-Languages, p. 73; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAWordlessCommunicationSystemsYieldsTelepathicAstralCommunication a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Wordless communication systems for dream and astral work yields telepathic and astral communication"@en, "Wortlose Kommunikationssysteme für Traum- und Astralarbeit: Ertrag Telepathische und astrale Verständigung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wordless communication systems for dream and astral work is said to yield telepathic and astral communication."@en ;
    skos:note "Written by the integrator from the link pass A recorded between this practice and capacity; the source states the effect at the practice."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAWordlessCommunicationSystemsDreamAstralWork ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATelepathicAstralCommunication ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Meta-Languages, p. 73; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEnhancedVisualisationViaComputerImagery a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Enhanced visualisation via computer imagery"@en, "Verbesserte Visualisierung durch Computerbilder"@de ;
    skos:definition "It has been observed that computer games and work with computer-generated imagery can enhance some people's ability to visualise objects, locations and events."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Simulation-Visualisation, p. 73; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAStopMotionVisualisationSpecialEffects a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Stop-motion visualisation and special effects"@en, "Stop-Motion-Visualisierung und Spezialeffekte"@de ;
    skos:definition "If visualising is hard, build a complex image slowly as a sequence of stop-motion frames; borrow computer effects, e.g. zoom in on a visualised entity or visualise it growing from a cell containing sigil-DNA into a being with nervous system and chosen organs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Simulation-Visualisation, p. 74; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAStopMotionVisualisationYieldsEnhancedVisualisationVia a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Stop-motion visualisation and special effects yields enhanced visualisation via computer imagery"@en, "Stop-Motion-Visualisierung und Spezialeffekte: Ertrag Verbesserte Visualisierung durch Computerbilder"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stop-motion visualisation and special effects is said to yield enhanced visualisation via computer imagery."@en ;
    skos:note "Written by the integrator from the link pass A recorded between this practice and capacity; the source states the effect at the practice."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAStopMotionVisualisationSpecialEffects ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEnhancedVisualisationViaComputerImagery ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Simulation-Visualisation, p. 74; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEnchantingLowProbabilityEventsUnlikelyInspiration a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Enchanting for low-probability events and unlikely inspiration"@en, "Verzauberung für unwahrscheinliche Ereignisse und Inspiration"@de ;
    skos:definition "Enchanting toward events outside one's currently perceived options, e.g. fresh inspiration from areas one would not normally look at."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Probability Scattering, p. 74; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAProbabilityScatteringYieldsUnlikelyInspiration a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Probability Scattering yields unlikely inspiration"@en, "Wahrscheinlichkeitsstreuung ergibt unwahrscheinliche Inspiration"@de ;
    skos:definition "The method enchants toward low-probability outcomes."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAProbabilityScattering ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEnchantingLowProbabilityEventsUnlikelyInspiration ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Probability Scattering, p. 74; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAThreeBandsProbability a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three bands of probability"@en, "Drei Wahrscheinlichkeitsbänder"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's diagram: outer band of low-probability, unmanifested events; middle band of higher-probability conscious but not yet coherent possibilities; inner band of high-probability events already unfolding."@en ;
    skos:note "Diagram not present in the text layer."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Prime Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Probability Scattering, p. 75; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAProbabilityScattering a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Probability Scattering"@en, "Wahrscheinlichkeitsstreuung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use the band diagram as free area; state a general intent (e.g. to take inspiration from improbable quarters); enter gnosis by whatever route; cast runes across the bands; scan them from the outer band inward assessing trends; link the runes, outer to inner, into a barbarous word and vibrate it with full force; banish at once."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Probability Scattering, Method, p. 75; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcACircumventingLustResultEgoDecisionMaking a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Circumventing lust of result and ego decision-making"@en, "Umgehung der Ergebnisgier und der Ich-Entscheidung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Probability Scattering combines divination and enchantment; lacking a specific statement of intent it partly avoids lust of result and bypasses the decision-making of the ego-complex."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Probability Scattering, Method, p. 75; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAIdeasSparkedPreviouslyIgnoredSourcesSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ideas sparked from previously ignored sources"@en, "Ideen aus bisher beachteten Quellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In enchantments for inspiration, results tend to appear as creative ideas kindled by sources the magician had ignored through lack of interest or prejudice."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of Probability Scattering worked for inspiration: results tend to show as creative ideas sparked by sources one had ignored from lack of interest or prejudice. Announced in advance, no rate or deadline given. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAProbabilityScattering."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Probability Scattering, Method, p. 75; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAMagicTakesPlaceOutsideTime a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magic takes place outside Time"@en, "Magie geschieht außerhalb der Zeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Consensus reality locks one into past-present-future; every magical act is a script for a momentary slip through the fabric; magic's secrets lie in plain view and what is hidden is our own resistance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Cut-Ups as Sorcery, p. 75; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcACutUpYieldsTangentialDeliriumsSyncretic a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Cut-up yields Tangential Deliriums and syncretic Gnosis"@en, "Cut-up ergibt tangentiale Delirien und synkretische Gnosis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Disrupting textual sequence produces new messages and gnosis."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcATextCutUp ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATangentialDeliriums, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASyncreticGnosisCollapsedSequence ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Cut-Ups as Sorcery, pp. 75-76; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASyncreticGnosisCollapsedSequence a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Syncretic Gnosis from collapsed sequence"@en, "Synkretische Gnosis aus aufgehobener Abfolge"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cut-up lets the magician fold sequential experience into syncretic gnosis."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Cut-Ups as Sorcery, p. 75; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcATextCutUp a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Text cut-up"@en, "Text-Cut-up"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cut a page of text into four sections and re-paste them so fresh lines and messages emerge; cut up magical texts, or The Book of the Law, to discover new magic or new chapters."@en ;
    skos:note "Technique a literary method first developed by Brion Gysin."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Cut-Ups as Sorcery, pp. 75-76; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATangentialDeliriums a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tangential Deliriums"@en, "Tangentiale Delirien"@de ;
    skos:definition "New messages arising from juxtaposed words and the derangement of associations they provoke."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Cut-Ups as Sorcery, p. 76; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcACuttingUpBelief a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Cutting up belief"@en, "Glauben zerschneiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shuffle beliefs by holding on purpose two belief systems that contradict each other at once and making meaning from nonsensical beliefs, to understand belief's dynamics."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine also likens sigils to cut-ups of desire and divination to cutting a subject into image blocks."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Cut-Ups as Sorcery, p. 76; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAThirdMindTape a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Third Mind tape"@en, "Third-Mind-Band"@de ;
    skos:definition "Record two different conversations, re-record them onto one tape, intercut with street noise, TV fragments and readings from books and newspapers; record, play back and intercut again."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Third Mind, p. 76; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAThirdMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Third Mind"@en, "Der Dritte Geist"@de ;
    skos:definition "An 'absent' source of information that slides into the listener's awareness through the time disorientation induced by the tape."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Third Mind, p. 76; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAIntercutTapeYieldsThirdMind a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Intercut tape yields the Third Mind"@en, "Verschnittenes Band ergibt den Dritten Geist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Listening to the intercut recording produces the Third Mind."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAThirdMindTape ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAThirdMind ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Third Mind, p. 76; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATimeDisorientationDislocatesEgo a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Time disorientation dislocates the Ego"@en, "Zeitdesorientierung verrückt das Ego"@de ;
    skos:definition "All routes to gnosis temporarily dislocate the ego, which needs sequence to uphold the fiction of a single identity; creativity is associative, and any stimulus strong enough to stir emotion and memory (smell above all) pushes awareness out of sequential time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Third Mind, p. 76; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcADayMontageTapeDivination a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Day-montage tape for divination"@en, "Tagesmontage-Band zur Divination"@de ;
    skos:definition "Capture a day of the week (e.g. Monday) on tape; intercut verbal messages you associate with it, street noises and random conversations; intercut and play back; use as a platform for oracular voyages or as backdrop for scrying or dream control."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Practical Applications, 1. Divination, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEntryOracularSpace a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Entry into oracular space"@en, "Eintritt in den orakelhaften Raum"@de ;
    skos:definition "A launching platform for journeys into oracular space, from which sounds, images and associations arise."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Practical Applications, 1. Divination, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADayMontageYieldsOracularSpace a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Day-montage yields oracular space"@en, "Tagesmontage ergibt orakelhaften Raum"@de ;
    skos:definition "The assembled tape opens oracular space."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcADayMontageTapeDivination ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEntryOracularSpace ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Practical Applications, 1. Divination, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAUnrecordedSoundsLaterEchoesSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unrecorded sounds and later echoes"@en, "Nicht aufgenommene Klänge und spätere Echos"@de ;
    skos:definition "One may hear on the tape sounds one was unaware of recording; days later hearing the same sound (e.g. a truck) in the street jolts one into oracular time."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of the day-montage tape: one may hear on it sounds one did not know one had recorded, and on meeting such a sound in the street days later be thrown into oracular time. Announced in advance, no rate or deadline given. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicPrcADayMontageTapeDivination."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Practical Applications, 1. Divination, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcASoundscapeEnchantment a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Soundscape enchantment"@en, "Klanglandschafts-Verzauberung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Treat enchantment as collage: assemble a soundscape relating to the target, recording the target space (as a bottle traps a spirit); take the recording away, alter it, return it to the original location and replay it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Practical Applications, 2. Enchantment, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAffectingTargetSpaceSoundCollage a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Affecting a target space by sound collage"@en, "Einen Zielraum durch Klangcollage beeinflussen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rearranging recorded elements of a target place to affect it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Practical Applications, 2. Enchantment, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcASoundscapeEnchantmentYieldsEffectTarget a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Soundscape enchantment yields effect on target"@en, "Klanglandschaft ergibt Wirkung auf das Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Altered and replayed recordings act on the captured space."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcASoundscapeEnchantment ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAAffectingTargetSpaceSoundCollage ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Practical Applications, 2. Enchantment, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAThreeTracksEmotion a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three tracks of emotion"@en, "Drei Spuren der Emotion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Emotion deconstructed into physiological arousal, cognitive association and patterns of behaviour, treated as separate mixing-desk tracks that can be remixed."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Prime Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Practical Applications, 3. Emotional Engineering, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAEmotionalEngineering a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Emotional Engineering"@en, "Emotionale Technik"@de ;
    skos:definition "In extreme arousal (anger, sorrow, tension) first experience the physiological track alone: drop identification with the emotion's source, still inner dialogue and fantasy, feel sensation without words or images. To re-engineer, experience the arousal as ecstasy, run the word/image track dispassionately and adjust it, identify and remodel behaviour patterns, name the selves, record their inner dialogues, intercut and play back."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondCEmotionalEngineering (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 practice has four steps toward undefined sensation; here emotion is split into three tracks to be remixed, arousal is re-experienced as ecstasy and the selves' dialogues are recorded and intercut."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Practical Applications, 3. Emotional Engineering, pp. 77-78; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAPhysiologicalTrackFirstPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Physiological track first"@en, "Zuerst die physiologische Spur"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first step in extreme arousal is to feel the physiological track separately from behaviour and cognition before re-engineering."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATimeDislocatedPureSensationBaseAny ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAReEngineeredEmotions ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Practical Applications, 3. Emotional Engineering, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAEmotionalEngineeringYieldsTimeDislocatedState a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Emotional Engineering yields time-dislocated state and remixed emotions"@en, "Emotionale Technik ergibt zeitentrückten Zustand und neu gemischte Gefühle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Isolating and remixing the tracks gives a state for magic and reshaped emotions."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEmotionalEngineeringYieldsFreeEmotion (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 yield is Free Emotion and disempowered demons; here the yield is a time-dislocated state for magic and remixed emotions."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcAEmotionalEngineering ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATimeDislocatedPureSensationBaseAny, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAReEngineeredEmotions ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Practical Applications, 3. Emotional Engineering, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcATimeDislocatedPureSensationBaseAny a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Time-dislocated pure sensation as base for any magic"@en, "Zeitentrückte reine Empfindung als Grundlage jeder Magie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pure sensation without identification, dislocated in time, in which any magical act can be done."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Practical Applications, 3. Emotional Engineering, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAReEngineeredEmotions a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Re-engineered emotions"@en, "Umgebaute Emotionen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Remixing arousal, cognition and behaviour into new arrangements, e.g. arousal experienced as ecstasy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Practical Applications, 3. Emotional Engineering, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcACutUpAidedRecordsWideAwareness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cut-up aided by records and wide awareness"@en, "Cut-up gestützt durch Aufzeichnungen und weite Aufmerksamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cut-up work is helped by diaries, scrapbooks and recordings and above all by awareness of what happens beyond the narrow field one is attending to."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part I Chaos Is Everywhere, Microaeonics, Practical Applications, p. 78; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Introduction
#
pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAimRitualUnionMicrocosmMacrocosm a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Aim of ritual as union of microcosm and macrocosm"@en, "Ziel des Rituals als Vereinigung von Mikro- und Makrokosmos"@de ;
    skos:definition "Crowley is cited as defining the objective of ritual as uniting microcosm with macrocosm; Hindu doctrine is cited as holding that ritual contacts gods via harmonic correspondence between worlds, drawing operator and deity nearer."@en ;
    skos:note "Crowley; Hindu magical doctrine (reported)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Introduction, p. 80; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualFocusesAwarenessPowerLies a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual focuses awareness; power lies in the ritualist"@en, "Ritual bündelt Aufmerksamkeit; Kraft liegt im Ritualisten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ritual aims to direct participants' awareness according to a pre-defined schema; improvisation may be as effective as full ceremonial, because power, born of skill, sits in the practitioner rather than in words, gestures or symbols."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Introduction, p. 80; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSuspensionNormalLimitsRitualSpace a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Suspension of normal limits in ritual space"@en, "Aufhebung gewöhnlicher Grenzen im Ritualraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Performing ritual is said to open a space where ordinary limits on the possible fall away and one may plot with gods or dance among demons."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Introduction, p. 80; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBRepetitiveLockReducesRitualEffectivenessCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Repetitive lock-in reduces ritual effectiveness"@en, "Festgefahrene Wiederholung mindert Ritualwirkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ritual loses much of its force when the practitioner gets stuck in one repeated pattern or approach."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualSkillMoreThanSum ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Introduction, Are Rituals Necessary?, p. 81; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEmptyHandedMagic a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Empty-Handed magic"@en, "Magie mit leeren Händen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magical results can be brought about without ritual procedures; rituals can also be enacted on the astral without physical props."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBEmptyHandedGesture (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos makes the Empty-Handed Gesture the sign of an advanced sorcerer working without objects; here Empty-Handed magic is named as one side of the argument over whether ritual is needed, beside ritual enacted on the astral."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Introduction, Are Rituals Necessary?, p. 81; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAstralOnlyMagicDriftsDelusionCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Astral-only magic drifts into delusion of being a mighty magus"@en, "Rein astrale Magie driftet in Wahn eines mächtigen Magus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine warns that if magical work has few connections to physical circumstances, it is easy to drift into an astral dream of grandeur; doing magic only in the head may reflect contempt for physical experience."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEmptyHandedMagic ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Introduction, Are Rituals Necessary?, p. 81; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualSkillMoreThanSum a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual as skill, more than sum of its parts"@en, "Ritual als Fertigkeit, mehr als Summe seiner Teile"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ritual can be analysed into sensory cues, voice, gesture, movement, visualisation, symbolism, trance induction and role-shifting, but is more than these and not merely psychodrama; it creates a space where something mysterious may happen."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Introduction, Are Rituals Necessary?, p. 81; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFocusingAttentionThroughDeliberateAction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Focusing attention through deliberate action"@en, "Aufmerksamkeitsbündelung durch bewusste Handlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Any action done deliberately and with emphasis feels different and becomes ritual, shifting awareness toward an aim; performed by a group it builds a particular atmosphere."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Introduction, What Constitutes A Ritual?, p. 82; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBDrinkVersusFormalToastExercise a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Drink versus formal toast exercise"@en, "Übung: Trinken versus förmlicher Trinkspruch"@de ;
    skos:definition "1) Simply take a drink from a cup. 2) Repeat the same action as a formal, deliberate toast, attending to the deliberateness of movement. 3) For group ritual: everyone first drinks normally, then each in turn makes a formal toast; note how the action feels different and how group performance adds distinctiveness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Introduction, What Constitutes A Ritual?, p. 82; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBToastExerciseYieldsAwarenessDeliberateness a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Toast exercise yields awareness of deliberateness"@en, "Trinkspruch-Übung erzeugt Bewusstsein für Absichtlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The drink/toast exercise produces direct experience of how deliberate action shifts awareness and builds group atmosphere."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBDrinkVersusFormalToastExercise ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFocusingAttentionThroughDeliberateAction ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Introduction, What Constitutes A Ritual?, p. 82; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSequenceRepetitionRitualOpeningClosing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sequence and repetition in ritual; opening/closing sub-ritual"@en, "Abfolge und Wiederholung im Ritual; Eröffnungs-/Schlussritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rituals follow pre-defined sequences (at minimum beginning, middle, end) and use repetition; because ritual has a distinct quality of experience, transitions into and out of it need attention, commonly marked by a self-contained banishing sub-ritual."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Introduction, What Constitutes A Ritual?, pp. 82-83; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBListUsesRitualMagic a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "List of uses of ritual magic"@en, "Liste der Anwendungen ritueller Magie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine lists uses of ritual magic: self-change, sorcery, insight, meditation, celebration, psychodrama, demonstration of technique, brief suspension of embedded rules, deity work, grounding oneself, focusing on a specific pattern; declared non-exhaustive."@en ;
    skos:note "Last items partly garbled in OCR (i, k)."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Prime Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Introduction, What can be done with ritual?, p. 83; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .



#
# Core Elements of Ritual
#
pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBUnderstandingRitualProcessDesignOnes a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Understanding ritual process to design one's own"@en, "Ritualprozess verstehen, um eigene Rituale zu gestalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rituals are processes whose elements combine to make the Free Area in which magic comes alive; understanding the process lets the magician create rituals instead of slavishly following others' scripts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, p. 83; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFamiliarityVersusRiskRitual a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Familiarity versus risk in ritual"@en, "Vertrautheit versus Risiko im Ritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rituals combine familiar elements (banishing, known techniques) and risk elements (new material, improvisation); a script only goes so far, after which participants must respond to each moment. Learning ritual requires challenging the familiar with risk; risk is part of ritual's glamour and power."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, 1. Familiarity v. Risk, pp. 83-85; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBChosenVehicleFailsAchieveInvokedFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Chosen vehicle fails to achieve invoked state"@en, "Gewähltes Gefäß erreicht den Invokationszustand nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "In a ritual to invoke a deity into a chosen person, that vehicle may not reach the required state while another participant does; a group unable to leave its script struggles on unaware, whereas a responsive group improvises."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the person chosen as vehicle for an invoked deity does not reach the required state, while another participant may. Cause: chance within the ritual process, not a fault of the vehicle; the group that cannot leave its script compounds it. No deadline; the text gives a rate in words only (by no means uncommon). It concerns the invocation of a deity into a chosen person."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, 1. Familiarity v. Risk, p. 84; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBRigidScriptBoundGroupsMissCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Rigid script-bound groups miss what happens"@en, "Skriptgebundene Gruppen übersehen das Geschehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Groups unable to depart from their script tend to plod on, blind to what is actually unfolding in the rite."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFamiliarityVersusRiskRitual ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, 1. Familiarity v. Risk, p. 84; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBComplacencyAfterManyRepetitionsRiskyCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Complacency after many repetitions is risky"@en, "Selbstzufriedenheit nach vielen Wiederholungen ist riskant"@de ;
    skos:definition "A first performance carries fear of doing it wrong; after a hundred performances one may become complacent, which is equally risky because strange things happen whether expected or not."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFamiliarityVersusRiskRitual ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, 1. Familiarity v. Risk, pp. 84-85; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBeliefGovernsRitualPower a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Belief governs ritual power"@en, "Glaube formt die Kraft des Rituals"@de ;
    skos:definition "Genuine belief is foundational to ritual magic; the basic conviction that magic is effective only becomes embedded through experience, and how far magic can work depends on one's dominant explanation of it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, 2. Belief Shapes the Power of Ritual, p. 85; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEnergyModel a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Energy Model"@en, "Energiemodell"@de ;
    skos:definition "Arising with science and Eastern imports such as Tantra, it explains entities as subtle energies that humans clothe in form in order to work with them."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondAEnergyModel (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos describes subtle energies that techniques can manipulate (Vril, prana, orgone); here the model is used to explain entities as energies to which humans give form in order to work with them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, 2. Belief Shapes the Power of Ritual, p. 85; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBCyberneticsModel a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cybernetics Model"@en, "Kybernetisches Modell"@de ;
    skos:definition "Incomplete emerging model from information science: entities as self-organising information systems arising from participation in webs of personal belief, group belief, environment and reality itself."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondACyberneticModel (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos describes the cybernetic model as neural storms causing microscopic fluctuations that grow into macroscopic change; here it is applied to entities, read as self-organising information systems arising from webs of belief and environment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, 2. Belief Shapes the Power of Ritual, p. 86; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBelieveEntitiesRealWithinFree a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Believe entities real within the Free Area; choose the most glamorous model"@en, "Im Freiraum Entitäten für real halten; glanzvollstes Modell wählen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inside the ritual one does best to hold that the gods, spirits or allies are real; choosing the model with the greatest glamour produces matching emotional intensity, and an ancient being demands performance with style, respect and awe. Models remain maps, not the territory."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondCActingAsIfGodsReal (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos gives acting as if the gods are real as a practice with the Cthulhu example; here the advice is tied to choosing the explanatory model with the greatest glamour so as to raise emotional intensity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, 2. Belief Shapes the Power of Ritual, p. 86; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualWithoutIntensityMerePlayFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual without intensity is mere play-acting"@en, "Ritual ohne Intensität ist bloßes Theaterspiel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Chaos magicians tend to hold that ritual must be intense, otherwise it is only play-acting."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: ritual without intensity is said to be mere play-acting. Cause: the operator, who has not raised the emotional intensity. No deadline and no rate; reported as the view Chaos Magicians tend to hold."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, 2. Belief Shapes the Power of Ritual, p. 86; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDramaticAwareness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dramatic Awareness"@en, "Dramatisches Bewusstsein"@de ;
    skos:definition "As performers and audience build a shared atmosphere, ritual participants shift collectively toward the mythic arena; heightened senses register micro-changes in voice, posture and body language that shift group awareness. The audience may be non-active participants or the entities stirred forth."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, 3. Dramatic Awareness, pp. 86-87; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBodilySignsPossessionEntitySign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bodily signs of possession by an entity"@en, "Körperliche Zeichen der Besessenheit durch eine Entität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Participants becoming possessed by an entity are observed to show postural change, vocal alteration and subtle facial-muscle changes forming the character associated with that personality; observers' noticing heightens group Dramatic Awareness."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: a participant shows postural change, vocal alteration and a change in the set of the facial muscles toward the character of the entity, read as possession beginning. No deadline or rate; reported as observed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, 3. Dramatic Awareness, p. 87; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBMovingDeliberatenessRitual a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Moving with deliberateness in ritual"@en, "Sich im Ritual mit Absicht bewegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Participants learn to make all movements with deliberate intent to communicate, as actors do toward an audience."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, 3. Dramatic Awareness, p. 87; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBCoordinatingTechniquesRitual a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Coordinating techniques in ritual"@en, "Koordinieren der Techniken im Ritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "Perform several techniques at once (for a traced pentagram: hand movement, visualising, breath and projected colour, with implicit belief that it changes the ritual space), steered by intent toward a specific result, until one recognises through practice the emotional state proper to the action."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, 4. Coordination of Technique, pp. 87-88; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBCoordinatedTechniqueYieldsBeliefShift a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Coordinated technique yields belief shift"@en, "Koordinierte Technik erzeugt Glaubensverschiebung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Coordinated movement, breath and visualisation directed by intent are said to bring the magician into the fitting emotional state, which supports belief and moves it toward the unspoken reality of the rite."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBCoordinatingTechniquesRitual ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBeliefShiftTowardRitualReality ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, 4. Coordination of Technique, p. 88; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBeliefShiftTowardRitualReality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Belief shift toward ritual reality"@en, "Glaubensverschiebung zur Ritualwirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Through coordinated technique the magician learns to recognise the appropriate emotional state and undergoes a tacit belief shift toward the reality of the ritual process."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, 4. Coordination of Technique, p. 88; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFiveStagesRitualProgressionSeries a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Five stages of ritual progression"@en, "Fünf Stufen des Ritualverlaufs"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's basic model for ritual design: first Preparation, then Warm-up, the Core, a Wind-down, and Debriefing last, following the shift toward actualising the intent and back to post-ritual consciousness."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualStage1Preparation ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualStage2WarmUp ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualStage3Core ;
    rdf:_4 pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualStage4WindDown ;
    rdf:_5 pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualStage5Debriefing ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Hine's basic model of ritual design runs through five stages in fixed order, Preparation, Warm-up, Core, Wind-down and Debriefing; the order follows the shift of awareness toward the realisation of the ritual's intent and back out to post-ritual consciousness, so each stage takes its sense from where it stands on that path in and out." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Stages in Ritual Progression, p. 88; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualStage1Preparation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual stage 1: Preparation"@en, "Ritualstufe 1: Vorbereitung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Clean the area, bathe, relax and meditate; optionally fast or give up habits; somatic changes (diet, less sleep, fewer stimulants) are especially effective; within a system assimilate its attributes and symbols; when working with an entity, some or all participants study its behaviour and qualities; brief participants on what is attempted and why."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Stages in Ritual Progression, pp. 88-89; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualStage2WarmUp a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual stage 2: Warm-up"@en, "Ritualstufe 2: Aufwärmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use drumming, dancing, meditation, background music, coordinated breathing or chanting to raise energy and focus; choose tempo to fit the desired mood; the standard warm-up opener is a banishing or centering."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Stages in Ritual Progression, p. 89; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualStage3Core a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual stage 3: Core"@en, "Ritualstufe 3: Kern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Implement the main intention, powered by the energy raised: invocation (calling an entity into participants), evocation (summoning or making a manifestation), projecting an intention into the multiverse, enacting a mythic event, psychodrama for a shift in awareness, or celebration."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Stages in Ritual Progression, pp. 89-90; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualStage4WindDown a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual stage 4: Wind-down"@en, "Ritualstufe 4: Ausklingen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Begin return to everyday awareness, e.g. by banishing again; optionally light-hearted games to discharge tension; shed the magical role and bid the mythic world depart; intense rites need a correspondingly thorough wind-down; observe participants' return from trance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Stages in Ritual Progression, pp. 89-90; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualEnergySpillingEverydayLifeCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual energy spilling into everyday life"@en, "Ritualenergie schwappt in den Alltag"@de ;
    skos:definition "Without the wind-down banishing, the energy and emotions raised can spill over into everyday life."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualStage4WindDown ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Stages in Ritual Progression, p. 89; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBUnevenReturnTranceLingeringEffectsCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Uneven return from trance; lingering effects"@en, "Ungleiche Rückkehr aus Trance; nachwirkende Effekte"@de ;
    skos:definition "People come back from deep trance at different speeds, so careful observation is often needed; intense rituals have effects that linger afterwards."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualStage4WindDown ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Stages in Ritual Progression, p. 90; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBLongTermChangeAwarenessLife a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Long-term change of awareness and life through ritual"@en, "Langfristige Veränderung von Bewusstsein und Leben durch Ritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rituals can produce lasting change in awareness and life, which is one of their aims; magic offers a framework to explore and assimilate such shifts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Stages in Ritual Progression, p. 90; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualStage5Debriefing a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual stage 5: Debriefing"@en, "Ritualstufe 5: Nachbesprechung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Record impressions and insights in the magical diary; assess performance technically, alone or as a group, identifying which parts had most effect and which did not work; accept criticism as part of refining technique."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Stages in Ritual Progression, p. 90; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualImpressionsQuicklyDistortForgottenCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual impressions quickly distort or are forgotten"@en, "Ritualeindrücke verzerren sich schnell oder gehen verloren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Impressions of what happened in ritual distort or vanish surprisingly fast, so diary recording cannot be overstressed."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualStage5Debriefing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Stages in Ritual Progression, p. 90; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMagicalDiaryRequiredSelfAssessmentPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical diary required for self-assessment of progress"@en, "Magisches Tagebuch nötig zur Selbstbewertung des Fortschritts"@de ;
    skos:definition "The magical diary, filled in at debriefing, is called essential for judging one's progress and keeping experiences for later reference; the importance of the record is said to be impossible to overstress."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicOrcDiaryEssential (Oven-Ready Chaos, 1992): Oven-Ready Chaos makes the diary a general necessity for keeping insight; here it is tied to the debriefing stage of a ritual and to the self-assessment of progress."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualStage5Debriefing ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicOrcRetainingAndRecallingInsight ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Impressions of what took place in a ritual are said to become distorted or forgotten surprisingly quickly." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Stages in Ritual Progression, p. 90; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFormalisedRitual a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Formalised ritual"@en, "Formalisiertes Ritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ritual rooted in a tradition, epoch or doctrine (Qabalah, Tantra, Witchcraft, Voudoun, Thelema, Western Esoteric Tradition), whose symbolism and structure follow set criteria."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Formal v. Freestyle, pp. 90-91; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAbsorbSystemsTheorySymbolismBeforePrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Absorb a system's theory and symbolism before getting most from it"@en, "Theorie und Symbolik eines Systems aneignen, um es voll zu nutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "To get the most from a formal system, magicians must absorb its theory, render its symbols personally meaningful and master its ritual forms, often steeping themselves in its culture."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBSteepingOneselfFormalSystem ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFormalisedRitual ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Formal v. Freestyle, p. 91; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBSteepingOneselfFormalSystem a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Steeping oneself in a formal system"@en, "Sich in ein formales System vertiefen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Absorb the theory of a system, make its symbolism personally meaningful and learn its ritual structures, often by immersing oneself in its culture; for Tibetan magic, Hine suggests, this might mean learning a suitable language, studying the Bardo Thodol, hearing the Dalai Lama and researching Tibetan ritual."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Formal v. Freestyle, p. 91; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBFreestyleRitual a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Freestyle ritual"@en, "Freistil-Ritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "Perform ritual not wholly rooted in one doctrine, open-ended and personalised, using broad symbolism and elements not always recognised as occult; Hine dates the growing interest in it from the late 1970s."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine holds that an effective magician can both work within one system and perform freestyle when the occasion suits."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Formal v. Freestyle, p. 91; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAbilityStructureOnesOwnRituals a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ability to structure one's own rituals"@en, "Fähigkeit, eigene Rituale zu strukturieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Freestyle ritual is said to be particularly good for learning to structure rituals oneself rather than following another's method."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Formal v. Freestyle, p. 91; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFreestyleRitualYieldsRitualDesign a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Freestyle ritual yields ritual-design skill"@en, "Freistil-Ritual erzeugt Ritualgestaltungsfähigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Practising freestyle ritual produces the ability to structure rituals oneself."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBFreestyleRitual ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAbilityStructureOnesOwnRituals ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Core Elements of Ritual, Formal v. Freestyle, p. 91; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .



#
# The Components of Ritual
#
pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFourFactorsShapingRitualsComponents a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Four factors shaping a ritual's components"@en, "Vier Faktoren, die die Ritualbestandteile bestimmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "How components are combined depends on: the intention; the style (formal/freestyle); the magical structure or belief system employed; practicalities of time and space."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Prime Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, p. 91; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualTheatreArtaudsPhysicalLanguage a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual as theatre; Artaud's physical language"@en, "Ritual als Theater; Artauds physische Sprache"@de ;
    skos:definition "Artaud is cited for a physical language of theatre independent of speech, provoking unconscious reactions through dance, mime, gesture, lighting, costume and props, requiring careful attention; Hine equates it with the language that builds ritual atmosphere."@en ;
    skos:note "Antonin Artaud, The Theatre and Its Double."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, Ritual as Theatre, p. 92; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBResearchingReconstructedFormalStyleRitual a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Researching a reconstructed formal-style ritual"@en, "Recherche für ein rekonstruiertes Ritual im formalen Stil"@de ;
    skos:definition "When reconstructing a ritual of another culture or epoch, prepare by research, consulting historians and anthropologists as well as occult reconstruction books; treat the style as an opportunity to go all out."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, Style, pp. 92-93; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAgainstBanMixingMagicalSystems a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the ban on mixing magical systems"@en, "Gegen das Verbot, magische Systeme zu mischen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine disputes the school, chiefly champions of the Western Esoteric Tradition and rigid modern witchcraft, which holds mixing systems wrong or dangerous; he answers that the WET is itself a synthesis, and that the problem is how one mixes, not mixing; Tai Chi and Qi Gong movements fit ritual well in his and others' experience."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the opponents are named by type and not quoted. Opponents: Western Esoteric Tradition champions, rigid traditions of modern witchcraft."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, Style, p. 93; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBTimingRitualsAvoidDisturbance a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Timing rituals to avoid disturbance"@en, "Rituale zeitlich so legen, dass man ungestört ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Perform rituals when you will not be disturbed by children, flatmates, neighbours or visitors, rearranging your schedule (rising earlier, retiring later) if needed, which also helps make the ritual special; planetary days/hours and astrological timing are optional."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, Timing, pp. 93-94; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFreeArea a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Free Area"@en, "Freiraum (Free Area)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's term for ritual space, wider than circle or temple: a state of consciousness or any location temporarily established as a zone in which magical reality prevails or is concentrated; e.g. a whole forest until an hour after dawn."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 1. Spatial Elements, a) The Ritual Space as a Free Area, p. 94; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBDemarcatingRitualBoundaries a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Demarcating ritual boundaries"@en, "Ritualgrenzen markieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mark a circle physically (chalk, rope, tape, blankets, floorboards; outdoors brush, ramping or turf) or by visualisation, dance and setting the directions of space with quarter-markers like banners, candles, small altars, statuettes or stangs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 1. Spatial Elements, b) The Demarcation of Boundaries, pp. 94-95; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBoundaryDemarcationYieldsProtectionFocus a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Boundary demarcation yields protection and focus"@en, "Grenzziehung erzeugt Schutz und Fokus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Marking boundaries produces focused attention and control over which influences enter."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBDemarcatingRitualBoundaries ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBoundaryKeepsOutAdmitsUnwanted ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 1. Spatial Elements, b) The Demarcation of Boundaries, p. 95; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBCircleAffirmationDevotion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Circle as affirmation of devotion"@en, "Kreis als Bekräftigung der Hingabe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Crowley is cited (Book Four, ch. 2) as holding the magical circle affirming the magician's dedication to the work."@en ;
    skos:note "Crowley, Book Four."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 1. Spatial Elements, b) The Demarcation of Boundaries, p. 95; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBoundaryKeepsOutAdmitsUnwanted a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Boundary keeps out or admits unwanted influences"@en, "Grenze hält unerwünschte Einflüsse fern oder lädt sie ein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The boundary focuses attention on the working area and bars unwanted or uninvited psychic beings from the circle, or admits them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 1. Spatial Elements, b) The Demarcation of Boundaries, p. 95; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBuildingAltar a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Building an altar"@en, "Einen Altar errichten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Arrange objects of the rite (images, statuettes, incense burner, weapons, mirror) on a cloth-covered table or box in symbolic sequence, placed per a schema such as the quarters and out of the way of movement; select items of core magical and personal significance; it may be minimal or complex; altars may be made for invocations, enchantments (sacrificing a desire on it) or commemorations; a few key items may form a portable altar."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 1. Spatial Elements, c) The Altar, pp. 95-96; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAltarFocusSacredDailyReconnection a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Altar as focus of the sacred and daily reconnection"@en, "Altar als Fokus des Heiligen und tägliche Wiederverbindung"@de ;
    skos:definition "An altar focuses attention toward the sacred, represents what one is and aspires to, serves meditation and reconnection with the magical in everyday life; building one can itself be a powerful act of magic."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 1. Spatial Elements, c) The Altar, pp. 95-96; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAltarBuildingYieldsSacredFocus a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Altar building yields sacred focus"@en, "Altarbau erzeugt sakralen Fokus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Building and tending an altar produces focus and reconnection with the sacred."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBuildingAltar ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAltarFocusSacredDailyReconnection ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 1. Spatial Elements, c) The Altar, p. 96; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBUsingMusicStandRitualProp a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Using a music stand as ritual prop"@en, "Notenständer als Ritualrequisit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Place texts to be read on a music stand, freeing both arms for gesture and allowing attention to posture, voice projection and visualisation; ritually unfold it and remove it before spinning or dancing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 1. Spatial Elements, d) Props & Equipment, p. 96; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPropsUsefulButNotEssential a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Props useful but not essential; collect gradually"@en, "Requisiten nützlich, aber nicht wesentlich; nach und nach sammeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Against the view that a trunk of weapons must come first, Hine holds props arguable as prerequisites, better gathered gradually (second-hand, gifts, handicrafts); chaoist minimalism (coffee mug as chalice) and Lionel Snell's satirical Over The Top Order mark the two poles; Pratchett's headology; do not be tied down by props."@en ;
    skos:note "Lionel Snell (OTTO), Terry Pratchett cited."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 1. Spatial Elements, d) Props & Equipment, pp. 96-97; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBMakingRitualPropsOneself a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Making ritual props oneself"@en, "Ritualrequisiten selbst herstellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Make props through handicrafts (pottery, batik, tie-dye, candle-making, woodwork, masks, incense blending) as preparation for rituals; e.g. carpet tubes turned into qabalistic pillars."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 1. Spatial Elements, d) Props & Equipment, p. 97; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBackdropsIndoorRitualSpace a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Backdrops for indoor ritual space"@en, "Hintergründe für Innenritualraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hang large backdrops: paintings of the invoked deity in the fitting aspect, illusions of space, drapes of suitable colour hiding furnishings; project slides or computer images on walls; use group-made collages as reminders of the group gestalt."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 1. Spatial Elements, e) Backdrops, pp. 97-98; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBVisualisation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Visualisation"@en, "Visualisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The skill of forming mental images and concentrating awareness in them, e.g. via guided visualisation in which another narrates the scene."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBVisualisationProficiency (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos states that some skill at visualising is needed from the start; here visualisation is defined as the skill of forming and focusing awareness into mental images, with guided visualisation as example."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, a) Visualisation, p. 98; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBVisualBiasMagicalExercisesCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Visual bias of magical exercises"@en, "Visuelle Einseitigkeit magischer Übungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Most imaginative exercises favour vision over other senses, though sensory experience is wider and some people are not primarily visual."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBVisualisation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, a) Visualisation, pp. 98-99; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBGoingPlacesExercise a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Going Places exercise"@en, "Übung: Orte aufsuchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Create an imagined place signifying relaxation and calm (past scene, visited or desired place); set a period to visit and explore it, placing yourself in it; after each visit note striking sounds, smells, touch (breeze, sun), emotions or memories; aim to engage hearing, touch, taste and smell, not sight alone."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, Visualisation-Related Exercises, i) Going Places, p. 99; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBGoingPlacesYieldsMultisensoryImagination a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Going Places yields multisensory imagination"@en, "Orte-aufsuchen erzeugt multisensorische Imagination"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Going Places exercise trains multisensory imaginative immersion."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBGoingPlacesExercise ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMultisensoryImaginativeImmersion ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, Visualisation-Related Exercises, i) Going Places, p. 99; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMultisensoryImaginativeImmersion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Multisensory imaginative immersion"@en, "Multisensorisches imaginatives Eintauchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ability to place oneself into an imagined setting with all senses, beyond mere visualisation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, Visualisation-Related Exercises, i) Going Places, p. 99; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBWhatsBoxExercise a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "What's in the Box? exercise"@en, "Übung: Was ist in der Kiste?"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keep a box with a hinged lid; occasionally and casually open it, letting whatever first pops into mind be inside; do not worry about what you find, and do it matter-of-factly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, Visualisation-Related Exercises, ii) What's In the Box?, p. 99; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBUncensoredAccessSpontaneousImages a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Uncensored access to spontaneous images"@en, "Unzensierter Zugang zu spontanen Bildern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being able to find anything in the imagined box without consciously placing it, overcoming the habit of censoring first impressions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, Visualisation-Related Exercises, ii) What's In the Box?, p. 99; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBoxExerciseYieldsUncensoredImagery a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Box exercise yields uncensored imagery"@en, "Kistenübung erzeugt unzensierte Bilder"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeated box-opening trains acceptance of the first image arising."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBWhatsBoxExercise ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBUncensoredAccessSpontaneousImages ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, Visualisation-Related Exercises, ii) What's In the Box?, p. 99; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBUnconsciousSeeing a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Unconscious Seeing"@en, "Unbewusstes Sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Choose a textured everyday object (whitewashed window, brick wall, moss, plant); look at it with a stilled mind, forget what it is, and let forms arise from it. Any sufficiently complex object will do."@en ;
    skos:note "Leonardo da Vinci is said to have called it Eidetic Vision; anecdote of a friend gazing at a spat-upon wall (reported legend)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, Visualisation-Related Exercises, iii) Unconscious Seeing, pp. 99-100; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBUnconsciousSeeingYieldsEideticImages a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Unconscious Seeing yields eidetic images"@en, "Unbewusstes Sehen erzeugt eidetische Bilder"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stilled gazing at complex objects produces arising images."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBUnconsciousSeeing ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEideticVision ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, Visualisation-Related Exercises, iii) Unconscious Seeing, p. 100; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEideticVision a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing meaningful images in phenomena (Eidetic Vision)"@en, "Bedeutsame Bilder in Erscheinungen sehen (Eidetisches Sehen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "An ancient technique is said to let meaningful images arise from flames, bird flight, swarming bees, clouds or textured surfaces."@en ;
    skos:note "Leonardo da Vinci (term); ancient divinatory tradition."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, Visualisation-Related Exercises, iii) Unconscious Seeing, p. 100; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBVoiceRitualTonePaceEmotion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Voice in ritual: tone, pace and emotion over volume"@en, "Stimme im Ritual: Ton, Tempo und Gefühl vor Lautstärke"@de ;
    skos:definition "Voice is used for declarations, statements of intent, extended vowels, mantras and invocations; loudness matters little (a whisper may beat a shout); tone, pacing and emotion, and both content and manner, generate atmosphere."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, p. 100; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBFindingRightTone a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding the Right Tone"@en, "Den richtigen Ton finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Experiment with ways of speaking that convincingly project: reverence, awe, self-confidence, facing slight fear, authority, speaking to a loved one after absence, speaking for the first time to someone admired from afar; observe how others use voice effectively (e.g. Captain Picard's calm command)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, Basic Voice Exercises, i) Finding the Right Tone, pp. 100-101; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBPlanetaryTones a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Planetary Tones"@en, "Planetare Tonlagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "For every one of the eight planets find a tone of voice that stands for one of its aspects (clipped officer-like speech for Mars, slow dreamy speech for the Moon); do this and the previous exercise before a mirror, watching how face and muscles change with the voice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, Basic Voice Exercises, ii) Planetary Tones, p. 101; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBRightToneBeforePlanetaryTonesPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Right Tone before Planetary Tones"@en, "Richtiger Ton vor planetaren Tonlagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Planetary Tones is presented as the next step after Finding the Right Tone."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBFindingRightTone ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBPlanetaryTones ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, ii) Planetary Tones, p. 101; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBUsingVoiceFocusRitualQualities a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Using voice to focus ritual qualities"@en, "Stimme zur Fokussierung ritueller Qualitäten nutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ability to use one's voice to focus on the particular qualities a ritual aims at."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, Basic Voice Exercises, ii) Planetary Tones, p. 101; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBVoiceExercisesYieldRitualVoice a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Voice exercises yield ritual voice control"@en, "Stimmübungen erzeugen rituelle Stimmkontrolle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tone and planetary-tone exercises produce the ability to focus qualities through voice."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBFindingRightTone, pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBPlanetaryTones ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBUsingVoiceFocusRitualQualities ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, p. 101; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBStoryTellingRitual a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Story-telling in ritual"@en, "Geschichtenerzählen im Ritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "Within ritual or its preparation, tell a myth starring the chosen entity, to focus celebrants on its qualities, especially when not all know its aspects; some myths suit ritual re-enactment (Inanna's descent, Bhairava's skull-dance)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, iii) Story-Telling, p. 101; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBGroupFocusEntitysAttributes a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Group focus on an entity's attributes"@en, "Gruppenfokus auf die Attribute einer Entität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Telling the entity's myth focuses other celebrants' attention toward its qualities and attributes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, iii) Story-Telling, p. 101; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBStoryTellingYieldsFocusEntity a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Story-telling yields focus on entity"@en, "Erzählen erzeugt Fokus auf die Entität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Story-telling produces shared focus on the entity's qualities."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBStoryTellingRitual ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBGroupFocusEntitysAttributes ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, iii) Story-Telling, p. 101; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBInannaNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Inanna"@en, "Inanna"@de ;
    skos:definition "Goddess whose descent into the Underworld is named as a myth suitable for ritual re-enactment."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Inanna" ;
    pm:nameRole "goddess who descends to the Underworld" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
