pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBhairavaNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Bhairava"@en, "Bhairava"@de ;
    skos:definition "Named as the wrathful aspect of Shiva, whose skull-dance suits ritual re-enactment."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Bhairava" ;
    pm:nameRole "wrathful aspect of Shiva" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, iii) Story-Telling, p. 101; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBVibrationNames a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Vibration of Names"@en, "Vibration von Namen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Divide the invoked entity's name into syllables (BAPH-O-MET); breathe deeply and intone each syllable, projecting it a few feet ahead so the whole body shakes; with practice extend the felt vibration outward; also usable for barbarous words in invocation and evocation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, iv) The Vibration of Names, pp. 101-102; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBodyShakingVibratedSoundSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Body shaking with the vibrated sound"@en, "Körper bebt vom vibrierten Laut"@de ;
    skos:definition "When vibrating a name correctly one should feel the whole body shaken by the sound's force."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the whole body is felt to shake with the force of the vibrated syllable. Given inside the instruction, no deadline or rate. It concerns A2-0092."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, iv) The Vibration of Names, p. 102; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBWideningVibrationVibratedNameSeries a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Widening vibration of a vibrated name"@en, "Sich ausweitende Vibration eines vibrierten Namens"@de ;
    skos:definition "With practice the felt vibration extends in order: whole body, immediate area, the world, finally the entire multiverse."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBWholeBodyVibratingName ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBImmediateAreaVibratingName ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBWorldVibratingName ;
    rdf:_4 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMultiverseVibratingName ;
    pm:seriesStatement "With practice the felt vibration of an intoned name is said to widen in a fixed order, from the whole body to the immediate area, then the world and at last the entire multiverse; each place names how far the vibration has reached, so a member is read from its position in the widening." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, iv) The Vibration of Names, p. 102; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBWholeBodyVibratingName a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Whole body vibrating with the name"@en, "Ganzer Körper vibriert mit dem Namen"@de ;
    skos:definition "First stage of the widening: the whole body is felt to vibrate as the sound is projected."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, iv) The Vibration of Names, p. 102; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBImmediateAreaVibratingName a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Immediate area vibrating with the name"@en, "Unmittelbare Umgebung vibriert mit dem Namen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Second stage: the surrounding area is felt to vibrate with the sound."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, iv) The Vibration of Names, p. 102; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBWorldVibratingName a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "World vibrating with the name"@en, "Welt vibriert mit dem Namen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Third stage: the world is felt to vibrate with the sound."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, iv) The Vibration of Names, p. 102; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMultiverseVibratingName a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Multiverse vibrating with the name"@en, "Multiversum vibriert mit dem Namen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Last stage: the entire multiverse is felt to vibrate with the sound."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, b) Use of Voice, iv) The Vibration of Names, p. 102; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBPostureSequenceDeliberateChangeConsciousness a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Posture sequence for deliberate change of consciousness"@en, "Haltungsfolge zur bewussten Bewusstseinsänderung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sit upright, tilt head slightly up, fix gaze steadily ahead, hands on thighs, push chest out, and breathe in deeply and slowly; notice the deliberately caused change in consciousness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, c) Posture, Gesture, & Movement, p. 102; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPostureSequenceYieldsAlteredConsciousness a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Posture sequence yields altered consciousness"@en, "Haltungsfolge erzeugt verändertes Bewusstsein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The posture sequence produces a deliberate shift in consciousness."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBPostureSequenceDeliberateChangeConsciousness ;
