    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, c) Posture, Gesture, & Movement, p. 102; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBMakingEveryRitualActionPerformance a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Making every ritual action a performance"@en, "Jede Ritualhandlung zur Darbietung machen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Within ritual space perform each action significantly: raise a toast as if to an audience, visualise light rays entering it, declare you absorb the planet's power by drinking; even consulting a forgotten text is done slowly and deliberately."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, c) Posture, Gesture, & Movement, p. 102; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBodySpaceReflectsProjectsMood a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Body space reflects and projects mood"@en, "Körperraum spiegelt und projiziert Stimmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use of personal space mirrors mood (anxiety contracts toward foetal posture, confidence expands) and can be used on purpose to heighten or project moods; ritual postures have physical and psychological effects beyond symbolism."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, d) Body Space, pp. 102-103; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEnvironmentalAwarenessHardSneakUp a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Environmental awareness: hard to sneak up on"@en, "Umgebungsbewusstsein: schwer zu überrumpeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Legend holds that shamans and sorcerers are very hard to surprise because they are aware of their surroundings."@en ;
    skos:note "legend (unnamed)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, d) Body Space, p. 103; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBlindWalks a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Blind Walks"@en, "Blindgänge"@de ;
    skos:definition "Best in pairs: one leads a blindfolded partner around an area, which heightens other senses; after several tries, the blindfolded person visualises an aura like a bubble or web around the body that senses obstacles before contact."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, d) Body Space, i) Blind Walks, p. 103; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBlindWalksYieldExtendedSensing a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Blind walks yield extended sensing"@en, "Blindgänge erzeugen erweiterte Wahrnehmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Blind walks increase non-visual sensory feedback and train aura-sensing of obstacles."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBlindWalks ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSensingObstaclesThroughAura ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, d) Body Space, i) Blind Walks, p. 103; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSensingObstaclesThroughAura a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sensing obstacles through the aura"@en, "Hindernisse über die Aura spüren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The visualised aura is meant to sense obstacles before physical contact."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, d) Body Space, i) Blind Walks, p. 103; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBFlowingMeditation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Flowing Meditation"@en, "Fließende Meditation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagine space as a fluid, water-like medium; feel each movement make it ripple, push it and shape it with the hands, as a fish in water; attend to spaces between arms and legs as in Tai Chi."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, d) Body Space, ii) Flowing Meditation, pp. 103-104; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFlowingMeditationYieldsSpatialPerception a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Flowing meditation yields spatial perception"@en, "Fließende Meditation erzeugt Raumwahrnehmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagining space as water trains it as a perceptual organ."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBFlowingMeditation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSpaceAdditionalOrganPerception ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, d) Body Space, ii) Flowing Meditation, p. 103; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSpaceAdditionalOrganPerception a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Space as additional organ of perception"@en, "Raum als zusätzliches Wahrnehmungsorgan"@de ;
    skos:definition "Surrounding space can serve as an extra perceptual organ; people, especially women, are said to sense what happens behind their backs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, d) Body Space, ii) Flowing Meditation, pp. 103-104; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualLightingDesign a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual lighting design"@en, "Rituelle Lichtgestaltung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Choose lighting form, symbolism and ambience so it enhances other elements: candles preferred but with enough light to read; alternatives such as head-torches, fairy lights, disco lights, strobes, dream-machines; colour symbolism (scarlet for Mars, green for Venus); form symbolism (brands or spotlights for martial rites, jack-o-lanterns for Hallowe'en); ambience via night-lights inside masks, lit altar with dark periphery, candles stimulating peripheral vision, computer-controlled shifts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, e) Lighting, pp. 104-105; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBInvocationsReducedFarcePoorLightFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Invocations reduced to farce by poor light"@en, "Invokationen durch schlechtes Licht zur Farce"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine has seen many grand invocations become farcical because those declaiming could not see what they were reading."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: grand invocations collapse into farce because those declaiming them cannot see the text. Cause: the operators, through poor lighting. No deadline; Hine reports having seen it in too many rituals, a rate given only in words."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, e) Lighting, p. 104; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFireSafetyCandlesTorchesCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Fire safety with candles and torches"@en, "Brandschutz bei Kerzen und Fackeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take care with candles, torches or other hazards; candle-flame meeting a polyester robe is a drama to avoid."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualLightingDesign ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, e) Lighting, p. 105; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBUsingScentsIncenseRitualTriggers a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Using scents and incense as ritual triggers"@en, "Düfte und Räucherwerk als Ritualauslöser"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use scents with known physiological effects as ritual triggers adding associations to an invocation; raise clouds of incense, itself an ancient form of invocation, to heighten atmosphere."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondCIncenseOffering (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos gives incense and perfume as offerings that build atmosphere and invoke deities; here scents with known physiological effects are used as ritual triggers that add a layer of association to an invocation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, f) Incense & Perfumes, p. 105; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMagicalApparelUniformShiftingState a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical apparel as uniform shifting state"@en, "Magische Kleidung als Uniform zur Zustandsverschiebung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Robes, jewelry, hats and cloaks signal leaving the everyday world; like a doctor's white coat, clothes help focus states of mind and subtle shifts of reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, g) Clothing & Apparel, p. 105; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBMakingWearingRitualHood a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Making and wearing a ritual hood"@en, "Eine Ritualkapuze herstellen und tragen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Get a black pillowcase (dyeing one if needed) and make two eyeholes; wear it for anonymity; optionally decorate with personal symbols or owl/bat eyes; a plain baggy hood is preferred over tight fetish hoods."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, g) Clothing & Apparel, p. 106; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBHoodAnonymityAlteredPerception a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hood: anonymity and altered perception"@en, "Kapuze: Anonymität und veränderte Wahrnehmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "A hood confers anonymity, muffles the voice and subtly changes perception without restricting movement, and looks forbidding."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, g) Clothing & Apparel, p. 106; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBHoodDisguisesIdentityDemons a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hood disguises identity from demons"@en, "Kapuze verbirgt Identität vor Dämonen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A sorceress who introduced Hine to the hood wore one when dealing with demons, saying it disguised her identity so they would not bother her afterwards."@en ;
    skos:note "an unnamed female sorceress, as told to Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, g) Clothing & Apparel, p. 106; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDemonsMayBotherOperatorAfterwardsCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Demons may bother the operator afterwards"@en, "Dämonen könnten den Operator danach belästigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Implied danger, per the sorceress, that demons dealt with could later trouble one who is recognisable."@en ;
    skos:note "unnamed sorceress."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBHoodDisguisesIdentityDemons ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, g) Clothing & Apparel, p. 106; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBHoodWearingYieldsAnonymityPerceptual a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Hood-wearing yields anonymity and perceptual shift"@en, "Kapuzentragen erzeugt Anonymität und Wahrnehmungswechsel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wearing the hood produces anonymity and subtle perceptual changes."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBMakingWearingRitualHood ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBHoodAnonymityAlteredPerception ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, g) Clothing & Apparel, p. 106; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDecoratedHoodEnhancesSeeingOther a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Decorated hood enhances seeing into other places"@en, "Verzierte Kapuze verstärkt das Sehen in andere Orte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some sorcerers decorate hoods with owl or bat eyes to mark that they boost their power to see and travel into other places."@en ;
    skos:note "unnamed sorcerers."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, g) Clothing & Apparel, p. 106; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPreRecordedMusicCarriesDifferentCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Pre-recorded music carries different associations for others"@en, "Aufgenommene Musik trägt für andere andere Assoziationen"@de ;
    skos:definition "An easy pitfall: music apt for oneself may evoke different associations for other participants; Hine uses obscure sources reserved for ritual."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBPreparingRitualMusicTapesCut ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, h) Music, p. 106; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBPreparingRitualMusicTapesCut a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Preparing ritual music tapes and cut-ups"@en, "Ritualmusikbänder und Cut-ups vorbereiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Compile instrumental background tracks from obscure sources kept for ritual use only; prepare cut-up sequences to throw out random inspirations, like the cocktail-party phenomenon."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, h) Music, p. 106; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBRandomInspirationCutUpTapes a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Random inspiration from cut-up tapes"@en, "Zufällige Inspiration durch Cut-up-Bänder"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cut-up sequences are said to throw out random inspirations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 2. BodyMind Components, h) Music, p. 106; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBCutUpTapesYieldRandom a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Cut-up tapes yield random inspiration"@en, "Cut-up-Bänder erzeugen Zufallsinspiration"@de ;
    skos:definition "Playing cut-up sequences produces random inspiration."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBPreparingRitualMusicTapesCut ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBRandomInspirationCutUpTapes ;
