pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMustSymbolismBeAbsorbedBefore a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Must symbolism be absorbed before ritual?"@en, "Muss Symbolik vor dem Ritual verinnerlicht sein?"@de ;
    skos:definition "Against some ritual experts who hold that a ritual's symbolism must be absorbed before it can succeed, Hine allows this only partly: for a Qabalistic ritual prior study helps greatly; for freestyle ritual only personally significant symbolism is needed."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the opponents are named by type and not quoted. Opponents: unnamed experts on ritual magic."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, a) Symbolism, p. 108; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBStudyQabalisticPrinciplesBeforeQabalisticPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Study Qabalistic principles before a Qabalistic ritual"@en, "Qabalistische Prinzipien vor qabalistischem Ritual studieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before performing a ritual structured on Qabalistic principles it helps enormously to have studied them."@en ;
    skos:note "The Qabalistic ritual the text points to is the Geburah invocation given later in the part."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBSteepingOneselfFormalSystem ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBGeburahInvocationMartialPower ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, a) Symbolism, p. 108; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMagicalLink a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical Link"@en, "Magische Verbindung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Connecting one thing with another mentally; it brings the object into one's magical awareness or psychocosm. Examples: wax doll identified with a person, lucky rabbit's foot, talismans linking vessel with inflamed state and symbols."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, b) The Magical Link, pp. 108-109; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBWaxDollEnchantment a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Wax doll enchantment"@en, "Wachspuppen-Verzauberung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take a wax doll, ritually identify it as a specific individual, and use it as focus for beneficial or malefic enchantment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, b) The Magical Link, p. 108; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEnchantingPersonDistance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Enchanting a person at a distance (beneficial or malefic)"@en, "Fernverzauberung einer Person (wohltätig oder schädlich)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Via the identified doll, enchantment is directed at the specific person, for good or ill."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, b) The Magical Link, p. 108; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBWaxDollYieldsEnchantmentPerson a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Wax doll yields enchantment of person"@en, "Wachspuppe erzeugt Verzauberung der Person"@de ;
    skos:definition "The identified doll serves as focus to enchant the person."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBWaxDollEnchantment ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEnchantingPersonDistance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, b) The Magical Link, p. 108; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBCreatingTalismansAmulets a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating talismans and amulets"@en, "Talismane und Amulette herstellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Link a chosen object (vessel) with the state of awareness one has inflamed oneself with during ritual and with the symbolic associations attached to it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, b) The Magical Link, pp. 108-109; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBMagicalToastAbsentFriendsHealth a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical toast to an absent friend's health"@en, "Magischer Trinkspruch auf die Gesundheit eines abwesenden Freundes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take a vessel of fizzy liquid, raise it and strongly visualise the friend's image in its depths; speak his name over it so the sound ripples across; speak your wish aloud, drink, and meditate briefly on inner calm. In an intense Solar invocation, visualise golden sun-rays infusing the liquid at the peak."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, b) The Magical Link, p. 109; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSendingHealthAbsentFriend a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sending health to an absent friend"@en, "Einem abwesenden Freund Gesundheit senden"@de ;
    skos:definition "The magical toast is aimed at an absent friend's health."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, b) The Magical Link, p. 109; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMagicalToastYieldsWishFriends a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Magical toast yields wish for friend's health"@en, "Magischer Trinkspruch erzeugt Gesundheitswunsch"@de ;
    skos:definition "The toast practice directs the wish for the friend's health."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBMagicalToastAbsentFriendsHealth ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSendingHealthAbsentFriend ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, b) The Magical Link, p. 109; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMagicalCorrespondencesTheirLineage a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical correspondences and their lineage"@en, "Magische Entsprechungen und ihre Herkunft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Correspondence tables build associative links between e.g. a planet and symbols and stimuli; many derive from herbals; modern ones follow Crowley, who drew on the Golden Dawn and Agrippa. Use them creatively, add and change links, never dogmatically."@en ;
    skos:note "Crowley, the Golden Dawn order and Cornelius Agrippa named as sources."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, Magical Correspondences, p. 109; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDoNotFollowCorrespondencesDogmaticallyCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not follow correspondences dogmatically"@en, "Entsprechungen nicht dogmatisch befolgen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The key is creative use; getting stuck in dogmatic following is warned against."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMagicalCorrespondencesTheirLineage ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, Magical Correspondences, p. 109; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBHelpfulLists a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Helpful Lists"@en, "Hilfreiche Listen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Head a sheet with the name of each of the eight planets in turn and write down as many associations as come (for Mars a chocolate-bar slogan, Holst, martial arts, red, songs); draw on them for the ritual, its preparation or re-invoking it afterwards."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, Magical Correspondences, i) Helpful Lists, p. 110; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBPostureGestureMoodMemory a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Posture, Gesture, Mood and Memory"@en, "Haltung, Geste, Stimmung und Erinnerung"@de ;
    skos:definition "1) Recall a personal experience linked to a planet (e.g. dentist waiting-room for Saturn). 2) Relive it fully, noting effects on posture, muscles, voice, emotion, scent, sound, taste, colour. 3) Find a posture and gesture recalling that mood and memory. 4) Add a neutral posture/mood/gesture for grounding after exercises. These become personal planetary correspondences, modified with use."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, Magical Correspondences, ii) Posture, Gesture, Mood and Memory, pp. 110-111; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPersonalPlanetaryStatesCue a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Personal planetary states on cue"@en, "Persönliche planetare Zustände auf Abruf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Postures, gestures, moods and memories become the basis of one's own planetary correspondences; a neutral posture aids grounding."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, Magical Correspondences, ii) Posture, Gesture, Mood and Memory, p. 111; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMoodMemoryExerciseYieldsPersonal a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Mood-memory exercise yields personal correspondences"@en, "Stimmungs-Erinnerungs-Übung erzeugt persönliche Entsprechungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The exercise produces cue-able personal planetary states and grounding."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBPostureGestureMoodMemory ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPersonalPlanetaryStatesCue ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, Magical Correspondences, ii), p. 111; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBSillyLists a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Silly Lists"@en, "Alberne Listen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Place everyday categories onto the Tree of Life or planets (Rocky Horror and Star Trek characters, herbal teas, yoghurts, curries, cereals; which tea before a lunar rite, which hat is Saturnian); fun and can yield useful correspondences."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, Magical Correspondences, iii) Silly Lists, p. 111; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMagicalArtefact a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical artefact"@en, "Magisches Artefakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Any physical object with magical associations for the user, from tools (tarot, runes, weapons) to nostalgic reminders; it helps or reminds us of our magical power; artefacts are generic or specific to a rite or system."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, Magical Artefacts, pp. 111-112; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBWandDirectsWill a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wand directs the will"@en, "Stab lenkt den Willen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The wand (rod, pointer) is the general-purpose weapon employed to direct will into the aethyr, a person or an object."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, The Wand, p. 112; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBTraditionalWandCutting a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Traditional wand-cutting"@en, "Traditionelles Schneiden des Stabes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cut ash wood the length of a forearm with a single stroke after asking the tree's permission, at a time fixed by astrology or planetary hours."@en ;
    skos:note "traditional method (unnamed tradition)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, The Wand, p. 112; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBIconoclasticChaosMagiciansVersusTraditional a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Iconoclastic chaos magicians versus traditional wand"@en, "Ikonoklastische Chaosmagier gegen den traditionellen Stab"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first generation of chaos magicians argued one could use a finger or rolled newspaper; Hine grants this in a pinch but defends the traditional hand-made, unique wand as a matter of headology."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the opponents are named by type and not quoted. First-generation chaos magicians (tradition); Pratchett's headology."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, The Wand, p. 112; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBCreatingPersonalWand a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating a personal wand"@en, "Einen persönlichen Stab schaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take a branch from a tree at a place significant to you, visited often across the year until contact with its genius loci; time it astrologically or by a personally significant date; alternatively use bone, or find or be given a suitable object."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, The Wand, pp. 112-113; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBContactGeniusLociBeforeCuttingPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Contact with genius loci before cutting wand"@en, "Kontakt mit dem Genius loci vor dem Schneiden des Stabes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ideally visit the tree's place at different seasons until contact with its spirit is made, then cut."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBVisitingTreesPlaceUntilContact ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBCreatingPersonalWand ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, The Wand, p. 112; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBVisitingTreesPlaceUntilContact a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Visiting a tree's place until contact with its genius loci"@en, "Den Ort eines Baumes aufsuchen bis zum Kontakt mit seinem Genius loci"@de ;
    skos:definition "Return often, at different times of year, to a tree in a place significant to oneself until contact is made with the genius loci, before cutting a branch from it for a wand."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, The Wand, p. 112; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBTransferAnimalAbilitiesViaBone a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Transfer of animal abilities via bone wand"@en, "Übertragung tierischer Fähigkeiten durch Knochenstab"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many magicians prefer bone from an animal whose powers they want to take on; Tibetan Bon shamans are said to fashion weapons from human bone."@en ;
    skos:note "unnamed magicians; Tibetan Bon shamans."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, The Wand, p. 112; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBGlassVajraChandelierLustres a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Glass vajra from chandelier lustres"@en, "Glas-Vajra aus Kronleuchterprismen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Glue two lustres together so each end has a point; use a pendulum to determine positive and negative ends; attribute notches to chakras; use facets for scrying."@en ;
    skos:note "made with an elder magician friend."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, The Wand, p. 113; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPersonalSorceryWeaponScryingFacets a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Personal sorcery weapon; scrying in facets"@en, "Persönliche Zauberwaffe; Scrying in Facetten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The glass vajra became a unique, portable, personally significant sorcery weapon whose facets could be used for scrying."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, The Wand, p. 113; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBVajraMakingYieldsSorceryWeapon a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Vajra making yields sorcery weapon"@en, "Vajra-Herstellung erzeugt Zauberwaffe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Making the lustre vajra produced a personal sorcery weapon."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBGlassVajraChandelierLustres ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPersonalSorceryWeaponScryingFacets ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, The Wand, p. 113; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBIncorporatingWandOnesMagicalUniverse a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Incorporating the wand into one's magical universe"@en, "Den Stab ins eigene magische Universum einbinden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Employ it in every magical act, keep it present in meditation, sleep with it, identify with it in meditation or visualisation; call it astrally to feel its weight and infused power; name it if desired and whisper secrets; keep it wrapped so unwrapping signals unleashing refined will."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, The Wand, p. 113; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBObtainWandMaterialThenIncorporatePrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Obtain wand material, then incorporate it"@en, "Erst Stabmaterial beschaffen, dann einbinden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Getting the material merely starts the process; incorporation follows into the magical universe."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBCreatingPersonalWand ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBIncorporatingWandOnesMagicalUniverse ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, The Wand, p. 113; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBWandIncorporationYieldsWillDirection a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Wand incorporation yields will-direction"@en, "Einbindung des Stabes erzeugt Willenslenkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Incorporating the wand lets one feel its infused power and unleash refined will."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBIncorporatingWandOnesMagicalUniverse ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBWandDirectsWill ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 3. The Interpenetration of Magical Reality, The Wand, p. 113; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPassiveOnlookersGroupRitualGrowCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Passive onlookers in group ritual grow bored"@en, "Passive Zuschauer im Gruppenritual langweilen sich"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one or two act and others watch, ritual becomes boring; Hine has nodded off in long rituals."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBInvolvingEveryoneGroupRitual ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 4. The Division of Roles, p. 113; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBInvolvingEveryoneGroupRitual a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Involving everyone in group ritual"@en, "Alle in das Gruppenritual einbeziehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Give everyone something to do: counter-chants or call-and-response in invocations, dancing the invocation, soundscaping with voice, gesture and movement; swap roles so each performs every part; optionally formal roles such as Incense-Monitor, Exorcist (helps those struggling to enter or leave altered states), Firemaster (fires plus group enthusiasm)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 4. The Division of Roles, pp. 113-114; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFormalGroupRitualRoles a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Formal group ritual roles"@en, "Formale Gruppenritualrollen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some groups define roles: Incense-Monitor, Exorcist, Firemaster, extendable to wider group functions."@en ;
    skos:note "some groups (unnamed)."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Prime Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 4. The Division of Roles, p. 114; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBStartSimpleAddProgressively a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Start simple, add progressively"@en, "Einfach beginnen, schrittweise ergänzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Especially in groups, start from a basic structure and enlarge it working by working rather than plunging people into large cumbersome rites; simplicity beats complexity for its own sake."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, The Components of Ritual, 4. The Division of Roles, p. 114; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .



#
# Example Types of Ritual
#
pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBanishing a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Banishing ritual (general)"@en, "Bannritual (allgemein)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Among the earliest practical exercises a magician learns, also called Centering; performed before (after tidying) and after working, and to clear a room after a bad row or after someone has been ill or depressed there."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBCentering (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos gives centering as a range of exercises with three core steps; here the banishing is given three aims (warm-up into the magician-self, making the space a Free Area, clearing its emotional undercurrents) and uses for rooms after quarrels or illness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Banishing Ritual, pp. 115-116; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBShiftMagicianSelfAxisMundi a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shift into magician-self at the axis mundi"@en, "Wechsel ins Magier-Selbst an der Axis mundi"@de ;
    skos:definition "Banishing acts as warm-up, setting aside everyday thoughts, shifting into the magician-self role and placing oneself at the metaphysical centre of one's magical universe."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicOrcCenteringRitesNullPoint (Oven-Ready Chaos, 1992): Oven-Ready Chaos states that centering rites set the magician at the null-point of his psychocosm as a warm-up; here the warm-up is also said to put aside everyday thoughts and to shift the magician into the role of his magician-self."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Banishing Ritual, p. 115; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBanishingYieldsCentringSacredSpace a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Banishing yields centring, sacred space, cleared atmosphere"@en, "Bannen erzeugt Zentrierung, heiligen Raum, geklärte Atmosphäre"@de ;
    skos:definition "Banishing produces its three aims."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBanishing ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBShiftMagicianSelfAxisMundi, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSacralisingWorkingSpaceFreeArea, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBClearingEmotionalUndercurrentsSpace ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Banishing Ritual, p. 115; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSacralisingWorkingSpaceFreeArea a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sacralising the working space as Free Area"@en, "Arbeitsraum als Freiraum heiligen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Banishing temporarily sets up a loft, bedroom or basement as sacred, a Free Area."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Banishing Ritual, p. 115; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBClearingEmotionalUndercurrentsSpace a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Clearing emotional undercurrents of a space"@en, "Emotionale Unterströmungen eines Raumes klären"@de ;
    skos:definition "Banishing clears the area of emotional undercurrents unconsciously associated with it, including lingering tension after arguments or illness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Banishing Ritual, p. 115; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBanishBeforeFocusedWorkAtmospherePrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Banish before focused work, or atmosphere disturbs the ritual"@en, "Vor fokussierter Arbeit bannen, sonst stört die Atmosphäre"@de ;
    skos:definition "Everyday atmosphere of living spaces should be banished before focused work or it may disturb the ritual; tidying should precede working."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBanishing ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualStage3Core ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "The atmosphere of a room used for everyday living, sensed through unconscious cues, might well disturb the ritual if it is not banished before focused work." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Banishing Ritual, p. 115; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPostWorkingAtmosphereClashesEverydayCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Post-working atmosphere clashes with everyday room use"@en, "Nachwirkende Atmosphäre kollidiert mit Alltagsnutzung des Raumes"@de ;
    skos:definition "After a working the created atmosphere should be dispelled, or it may clash with the room's everyday atmosphere."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBanishing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Banishing Ritual, p. 115; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBOctomanticBanishing a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Octomantic Banishing"@en, "Oktomantisches Bannen"@de ;
    skos:definition "1) Face East (direction of Magic), arms at sides, head slightly up, breathe regularly, clear mind; raise right hand on in-breath, draw it down the body's midline on the out-breath visualising white light through the body; point left and right forming a Tau cross, visualise light across; bring arms forward, visualise a circle of light; fold hands on chest, visualise an expanding sphere of white light. 2) For each of the 8 rays, inhale, snap fingers or clap on exhalation, visualise a chaos thunderbolt and declare its name with a gesture hurling it out: Raw, Death, Wealth, Love, Ego, Sex, Thought, War Magic. 3) Face East, arms in invocation, declare oneself poised at the centre with these weapons of will. Close by running through again, visualising each thunderbolt returning on the in-breath."@en ;
    skos:note "Built on the Chaosphere's eight rays; Hine refers to Peter J. Carroll, Liber Kaos."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Banishing Ritual, Octomantic Banishing, pp. 116-118; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEightRaysChaosphere a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Eight rays of the Chaosphere (eight magics)"@en, "Acht Strahlen der Chaossphäre (acht Magien)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Eight areas of magical activity as facets of self: Raw, War, Death, Thought, Wealth, Sex, Love, Ego Magic."@en ;
    skos:note "Peter J. Carroll, Liber Kaos."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Peter J. Carroll (Liber Kaos), as used by Phil Hine in Prime Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Banishing Ritual, Octomantic Banishing, p. 116; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSuperchargedYetCalmAfterBodyMindSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Supercharged yet calm after BodyMind stage"@en, "Aufgeladen und doch ruhig nach der KörperGeist-Stufe"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the first stage one should feel supercharged with energy, yet calm and prepared to go on."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: feeling charged with energy yet calm and prepared to go on at the end of the first stage of the Octomantic Banishing; given inside the instruction, no deadline or rate. Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBCalmYetSuperchargedSign (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the same sign is there announced for the close of the Lightning Flash; here it closes the BodyMind stage of the Octomantic Banishing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Banishing Ritual, Octomantic Banishing, p. 117; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBElaboratingOctomanticBanishing a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Elaborating the Octomantic Banishing"@en, "Das Oktomantische Bannen ausbauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Give each thunderbolt its colour; let each grow into a chaosphere, or into a servitor personal to you emblematic of that power; develop the form that works best for you."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Banishing Ritual, Octomantic Banishing, p. 118; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMetaphysicalEast a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Metaphysical east"@en, "Metaphysischer Osten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Chaos magicians designate one direction as metaphysical east to begin directional progressions; Hine indoors often takes any wall with a window."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Banishing Ritual, Octomantic Banishing, p. 118; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBDailyBanishingPractice a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Daily banishing practice"@en, "Tägliche Bannpraxis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Perform a chosen banishing daily on waking and before retiring, and to begin and end all magical activity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Banishing Ritual, Practice, p. 118; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBanishingAutopilotDreamsBanishingSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Banishing on autopilot; dreams of banishing"@en, "Bannen auf Autopilot; Träume vom Bannen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In time the ritual runs almost on autopilot with its feelings arising effortlessly; dreaming of banishing is an encouraging sign. Hine reports his dreams always feature the first one he learned, the Lesser Pentagram Rite of the Golden Dawn."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: with time the banishing runs almost on autopilot and its feelings arise without effort, and dreaming of banishing is an encouraging sign. No deadline (in time) and no rate. It concerns A2-0180."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Banishing Ritual, Practice, p. 118; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBMagicalMass a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical Mass"@en, "Magische Messe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Call an entity's power into the Free Area by invoking it into a selected priest or priestess, who becomes it with varying possession; the entity delivers a scripted litany or improvised oracle, may be questioned, may lead participants into acts, or empower a prepared sacrament so all partake of its power."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Mass, pp. 118-119; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSharingEntitysPowerOracleInvoked a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sharing an entity's power; oracle from invoked entity"@en, "Teilhabe an der Macht einer Entität; Orakel der invozierten Entität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Through the mass, all participants share the entity's power and may receive oracular answers from it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Mass, p. 119; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMassYieldsSharedPowerOracle a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Mass yields shared power and oracle"@en, "Messe erzeugt geteilte Macht und Orakel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Performing the mass produces sharing of the entity's power."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBMagicalMass ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSharingEntitysPowerOracleInvoked ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Mass, p. 119; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBEndingDeepPossession a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ending deep possession"@en, "Tiefe Besessenheit beenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Appoint officers prepared to expel the entity from its host; if needed restrain the possessed person, forcefully banish the entity, make the host recall own identity and location; in extreme cases apply a lustration of water."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Mass, p. 119; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEntitiesMayResistLeavingTheirCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Entities may resist leaving their host"@en, "Entitäten können sich weigern, ihren Wirt zu verlassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Entities sometimes resist departing a space they were called into; a deeply possessed person may need restraint, forceful banishing of the entity, and being brought to remember who and where they are; at worst a lustration with water."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBMagicalMass ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Mass, p. 119; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessingEntityRefusesDepartFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Possessing entity refuses to depart"@en, "Besitzende Entität weigert sich zu gehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The possession does not end at will because the entity resists leaving."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the possessing entity resists leaving the host it was called into. Cause: the entity. No deadline; rate in words only (not unknown). It concerns the magical Mass, A2-0182. It concerns the magical Mass (A2-0182)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Mass, p. 119; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBHarpoNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "HARPO (Harpo Marx as avatar of Harpocrates)"@en, "HARPO (Harpo Marx als Avatar des Harpokrates)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Discordians are said to regard Harpo Marx as a present-day avatar of Harpocrates, the Egyptian silence-god; invoked as Lord of Silence, Trickster, Sacred Clown, Sacred Fool, and lord of mute mockery."@en ;
    skos:note "Discordians."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "HARPO; Harpocrates" ;
    pm:nameRole "Lord of Silence, Trickster, Sacred Clown" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Mass, Chaos Mass H, p. 119; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBChaosMassH a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Chaos Mass H"@en, "Chaos-Messe H"@de ;
    skos:definition "Prepare: priest gets wig of wool, top hat and a horn, props on altar. Statement of intent to invoke HARPO so magic's glamours disperse. Priest starts the pomposity; assembly strut and declaim that magic is serious, while priest whirls and leaps with Harpo's gestures and faces, silently invoking HAR-PO until possession; he honks the horn litany; assembly freeze as pompous statues; HARPO plays tricks (feather-duster tickling) to reduce them to laughter; squirts sacrament (milk) from a pricked rubber glove into their mouths; capers until self-importance is banished. Closure: capture and disrobe the priest, coax him into speech; after a few sensible remarks all laugh and cheer."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Mass, Chaos Mass H, pp. 119-121; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPriestSweptHarpoPossessionAssemblySign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Priest swept into Harpo possession; assembly laughs"@en, "Priester von Harpo-Besessenheit erfasst; Versammlung lacht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Signs: the priest feels possession by the avatar take him; the assembly are reduced to laughter."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the priest feels Harpo take possession of him, and the assembly is reduced to laughter. Given inside the rite, no deadline or rate. It concerns A2-0189."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Mass, Chaos Mass H, p. 120; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBChaosMassHYieldsBanished a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Chaos Mass H yields banished pomposity"@en, "Chaos-Messe H erzeugt gebannte Wichtigtuerei"@de ;
    skos:definition "Performing the mass produces temporary release from self-importance."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBChaosMassH ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBanishingSelfImportanceEgoAttachment ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Mass, Chaos Mass H, p. 120; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBanishingSelfImportanceEgoAttachment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Banishing self-importance and ego-attachment"@en, "Bannen von Selbstwichtigkeit und Ego-Anhaftung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mass aims to disperse magic's glamours, let laughing anarchy in, and banish self-importance and ego-attachment, if only temporarily."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Mass, Chaos Mass H, pp. 120-121; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFamiliarityMarxBrothersFilmsWillingPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Familiarity with Marx Brothers films and willing group"@en, "Vertrautheit mit Marx-Brothers-Filmen und bereitwillige Gruppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing the Marx Brothers' films somewhat, and a group willing to play pompous, are named as prerequisites of the rite; no consequence stated."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFamiliarityMarxBrothersFilms ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBChaosMassH ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Mass, Chaos Mass H, Notes, p. 121; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFamiliarityMarxBrothersFilms a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Familiarity with the Marx Brothers' films"@en, "Vertrautheit mit den Filmen der Marx Brothers"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some knowledge of the Marx Brothers' films, named with a group willing to play at pomposity and a recognition of how easily magicians become pompous as what Chaos Mass H requires."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Mass, Chaos Mass H, Notes, p. 121; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMagiciansEasilyBecomePompousCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Magicians easily become pompous"@en, "Magier werden leicht aufgeblasen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine warns how easily magicians become pompous and stresses the need to banish self-importance; silly rites are as important as serious ones."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBanishingSelfImportanceEgoAttachment ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Mass, Chaos Mass H, Notes, p. 121; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBGeburahInvocationMartialPower a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Geburah: Invocation of Martial Power"@en, "Geburah: Invokation martialer Kraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Group rite adaptable to solo. Preparation: altar on scarlet cloth with five scarlet candles, Tower/Adjustment/Emperor cards, weapons, Mars incense, juniper oil, fiery sacrament, red pyramid focus bearing Mars, Fire and planetary spirit/seal/intelligence signs. Officers: Master of the Temple (sword), Priest (sword/dagger), scourge-bearing assistants. Sequence: 1) banishing, celebrants arranged in military ranks; 2) statement of intent to invoke Geburah's powers; 3) purification: inspection, each scourged five times at the altar; 4) invocations: circle, invoke ELOHIM GIBOR visualising a mighty king in a chariot in orange mist; MT invokes KHAMMAEL while all see a vortex send a scarlet beam to the sword tip, closed with Hah; Flashing Power round the circle; third invocation summons the SERAPHIM entwined on the sword, desire-forms visualised, MT spins and projects with Kia while all cry out; closing: banishing, mock drill commands, banish with laughter."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Invocation, Geburah: Invocation of Martial Power, pp. 121-124; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMeditationFivesTowerBeforeGeburahPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Meditation on the Fives and the Tower before Geburah rite"@en, "Meditation über die Fünfen und den Turm vor dem Geburah-Ritus"@de ;
    skos:definition "In its original use the rite was preceded by celebrants meditating on the four Fives of the Tarot and The Tower, linked to Geburah."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBMeditatingFourFivesTower ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBGeburahInvocationMartialPower ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Invocation, p. 121; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBMeditatingFourFivesTower a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Meditating on the four Fives and The Tower"@en, "Meditation über die vier Fünfen und den Turm"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before the Geburah rite, celebrants spend a period meditating on the four Fives of the Tarot and the Major Arcanum The Tower, the cards tied to the action and symbolism of Geburah (Mars)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Invocation, p. 121; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

