pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBElohimGiborNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "ELOHIM GIBOR"@en, "ELOHIM GIBOR"@de ;
    skos:definition "God-name of Geburah, god of strength, imaged as a mighty king in a chariot with chains, shields, spear, scourge and sword, embodying law, power, discipline and strength."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "ELOHIM GIBOR" ;
    pm:nameRole "god-name of Geburah" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Invocation, Geburah, First Invocation, p. 123; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBKhammaelNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "KHAMMAEL"@en, "KHAMMAEL"@de ;
    skos:definition "Archangel of Mars, the Burner, the Wrathful One, who destroys and purifies, cleansing decay and stagnation; embodiment of power, will, purpose, courage, self-scrutiny and discrimination."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "KHAMMAEL" ;
    pm:nameRole "Archangel of Mars" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Invocation, Geburah, Second Invocation, p. 123; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBFlashingPower a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Flashing Power"@en, "Kraft blitzen lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "MT thrusts the charged sword toward his assistant, striking him with the force; the assistant spins deosil and hurls it to the next celebrant on the right; this continues round until the power is projected back to the MT."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Invocation, Geburah, Flashing Power, p. 123; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSeraphimNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "SERAPHIM"@en, "SERAPHIM"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fire-serpents of purifying and correction, summoned to manifest the group's will."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "SERAPHIM" ;
    pm:nameRole "angelic choir of Geburah, fire-serpents" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Invocation, Geburah, Third Invocation, p. 124; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDescentThroughGodArchangelAngelsSeries a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Descent through God, Archangel, Angels in Geburah rite"@en, "Abstieg durch Gott, Erzengel, Engel im Geburah-Ritus"@de ;
    skos:definition "The invocations follow Western Qabalah, drawing power through the spheres of God-name, Archangel and angelic powers in order, letting celebrants identify with these forces."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBElohimGiborNaming ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBKhammaelNaming ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSeraphimNaming ;
    pm:seriesStatement "The Geburah invocations follow Western Qabalah and draw power down through its spheres in order: first the god-name ELOHIM GIBOR, then the archangel KHAMMAEL, then the angelic SERAPHIM; each invocation has its rank from its place in this descent, which lets the celebrants identify with the forces one level at a time." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Invocation, Notes, p. 124; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDistributingEnhancingInvokedForce a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Distributing and enhancing invoked force"@en, "Invozierte Kraft verteilen und verstärken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Turning deosil, participants take the force into themselves and project it outward, enhancing it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Invocation, Notes, p. 124; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFlashingPowerYieldsDistributedForce a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Flashing Power yields distributed force"@en, "Kraftblitzen erzeugt verteilte Kraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Flashing Power distributes Khammael's force among the participants and enhances it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBFlashingPower ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDistributingEnhancingInvokedForce ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Invocation, Notes, p. 124; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBGeburahInvocationYieldsMartialApplications a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Geburah invocation yields martial applications"@en, "Geburah-Invokation erzeugt martiale Anwendungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The rite is offered for the seven listed applications; projected outward into participants' immediate future (e.g. confidence) or into an artefact to charge it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBGeburahInvocationMartialPower ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBIncreaseWillConfidencePurpose, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBInitiatingNewProjects, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEnhancedSexualVitality, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBIncreaseEnergyCourage, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDestructionInternalExternalObstacles, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBChargingTalismans, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBChargingMagicalWeapons ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, Ritual Invocation, Notes, pp. 121-124; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFormalRitualNotNeededEnchantment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Formal ritual not needed for enchantment"@en, "Formales Ritual für Verzauberung nicht nötig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Enchantment does not strictly require formal ritual, but may be desirable in group meetings or theme-centred periods of work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, A Ritual Enchantment, p. 125; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBHammerCast a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The Hammer-Cast"@en, "Der Hammerwurf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Prepare a sigil from a statement of intent, easily recalled as image or mantra. 0) Leader gives statement of intent in parts, all repeat. 1) All adopt leader's posture, nine slow breaths visualising lightning around the body and between the hands. 2) Take the Thurisaz runic posture, focus on the sigil while the leader declaims the litany to Thor; visualise holding Thor's hammer in the right hand charged with the sigil. 3) Vibrate THUR-IZ-AS nine times. 4) With a wordless scream hurl the hammer forth."@en ;
    skos:note "Devised during Hine's six-month working with Thor."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, A Ritual Enchantment, The Hammer-Cast, pp. 125-126; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAchievingDesireThroughGroupEnchantment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Achieving a desire through group enchantment"@en, "Einen Wunsch durch Gruppenverzauberung erlangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "By identifying with Thor's qualities participants hurl forth an enchantment; Mjollnir's return reinforces that they will achieve their desire."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, A Ritual Enchantment, The Hammer-Cast, p. 125; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBHammerCastYieldsAchievedDesire a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Hammer-Cast yields achieved desire"@en, "Hammerwurf erzeugt erreichten Wunsch"@de ;
    skos:definition "The hammer-cast enchants the group's sigilised desire."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBHammerCast ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAchievingDesireThroughGroupEnchantment ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, A Ritual Enchantment, The Hammer-Cast, p. 125; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPrepareSigilBeforeHammerCastPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Prepare the sigil before the Hammer-Cast"@en, "Sigil vor dem Hammerwurf vorbereiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Make the sigil in advance so that it comes readily to mind in the rite."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSigilMagicFullProcess ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBHammerCast ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, A Ritual Enchantment, The Hammer-Cast, p. 125; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBThorNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Thor"@en, "Thor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Norse god invoked as the Thunderer, champion and defender of Asgard, slayer of giants, sky god, judge of men, dwelling in Thrudheim, bearer of Mjollnir, storm-god and son of Earth; his hammer always returns to him."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Thor; the Thunderer" ;
    pm:nameRole "Norse thunder-god" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Example Types of Ritual, A Ritual Enchantment, The Litany, pp. 125-126; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .



