pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEcstasyHeightenedSexualArousalThrough a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ecstasy and heightened sexual arousal through Pan"@en, "Ekstase und gesteigerte sexuelle Erregung durch Pan"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pan may be invoked for ecstasy and heightened arousal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Why Invoke?, p. 127; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPanNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Pan"@en, "Pan"@de ;
    skos:definition "God of ecstasy and heightened sexual arousal."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPanNaming (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos holds Pan to embody sudden illumination and creative derangement; here he is named as the god one invokes for ecstasy and stronger erotic arousal."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Pan" ;
    pm:nameRole "god of ecstasy and arousal" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Why Invoke?, p. 127; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBKnowledgeFutureThroughNornir a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowledge of the future through one of the Nornir"@en, "Wissen um die Zukunft durch eine der Nornen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A Norn may be invoked to gain foreknowledge."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Why Invoke?, p. 127; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBNornirNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Nornir"@en, "Nornen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Norse beings, any one of whom grants knowledge of the future."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Nornir" ;
    pm:nameRole "givers of foreknowledge" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Why Invoke?, p. 127; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBHawksEyeViewThroughRa a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hawk's-eye view through Ra-Hoor-Khuit"@en, "Falkenblick durch Ra-Hoor-Khuit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra-Hoor-Khuit may be invoked for an overview of a situation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Why Invoke?, p. 127; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBConsumingAspectSelfThroughKali a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Consuming an aspect of self through Kali"@en, "Einen Selbstaspekt durch Kali verzehren lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One might invoke Kali to consume an aspect of self one wishes to loosen from the ego-complex."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Why Invoke?, p. 127; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBKaliNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Kali"@en, "Kali"@de ;
    skos:definition "Goddess who consumes aspects of self to be loosened from the ego-complex."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCKaliNaming (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos invokes Kali as goddess of sex and death for the power of attraction; here she is invoked to consume an aspect of self that one wishes to loosen from the ego-complex."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Kali" ;
    pm:nameRole "devourer of ego-aspects" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Why Invoke?, p. 127; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBGeneralGainsInvocation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "General gains of invocation"@en, "Allgemeine Gewinne der Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Through invocation one may modify one's selves, gain inspiration or specific knowledge, develop heightened perception, or feel charged with power for further tasks."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInvocationUses (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos lists bringing a shadow-self to awareness, insight into an entity, a power boost for sorcery and oracular information; here the list is self-modification, inspiration, specific knowledge, heightened perception and a charge of power for further tasks."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Why Invoke?, p. 127; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEcstaticManifestationEntitysQualities a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ecstatic manifestation of the entity's qualities (oracular perception, hidden lore)"@en, "Ekstatische Manifestation der Qualitäten der Entität (orakelhafte Wahrnehmung, verborgenes Wissen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Invocations tend to produce an ecstatic trance in which some quality of the entity shows in the person, e.g. heightened oracular perception or hidden knowledge; anyone practising magic can develop this."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Why Invoke?, p. 127; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBInvokingUponSomeone a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Invoking upon someone"@en, "Auf jemanden invozieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "A practitioner may act as an entity's incarnation at an event, or bring a similar experience about in another person."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Why Invoke?, p. 127; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBTemporaryAbilitiesBeyondNormalCapacity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Temporary abilities beyond normal capacity"@en, "Vorübergehende Fähigkeiten jenseits des Normalen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Invocation heightens dramatic awareness so that the magician gains access to the figure's abilities and temporarily performs acts beyond normal capacities, as actors report singing or feats beyond their range."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Why Invoke?, pp. 127-128; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBuildSymbolFrameworkBeforeInvokingPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Build symbol framework before invoking"@en, "Vor dem Invozieren ein Symbolgerüst aufbauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Building a framework of symbols to focus awareness on the subject of the invocation is called essential and is put first in designing one; no consequence of omitting it is stated."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBuildingSymbolFrameworkInvocation ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInvocation ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Designing Invocations, p. 128; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBuildingSymbolFrameworkInvocation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Building a symbol framework for an invocation"@en, "Ein Symbolgerüst für eine Invokation aufbauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Assemble the symbols, symbolic media and correspondences that will focus awareness on the entity to be invoked, before designing the invocation itself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Designing Invocations, p. 128; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBInvokingMrSpock a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Invoking Mr. Spock"@en, "Mr. Spock invozieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Study the gestures, posture, mannerisms and inscrutability of Spock and adopt them in ritual; devise a pathworking of Spock walking the Enterprise corridors until one feels composed as Spock; then undertake a fitting task such as debugging a program."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondCSpockInvocation (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos reports a colleague invoking Spock for a computer exam by repeating his catchphrase; here the design steps are given: research his mannerisms, devise a pathworking aboard the Enterprise, then take on a task such as debugging."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Designing Invocations, p. 128; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBLogicPatienceCalmTask a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Logic, patience and calm for a task"@en, "Logik, Geduld und Ruhe für eine Aufgabe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Invoking Spock lends unswerving logic, patience and calm, e.g. for debugging."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Designing Invocations, p. 128; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSpockInvocationYieldsLogicCalm a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Spock invocation yields logic and calm"@en, "Spock-Invokation erzeugt Logik und Ruhe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Invoking Spock produces the qualities needed for debugging."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBInvokingMrSpock ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBLogicPatienceCalmTask ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Designing Invocations, p. 128; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBackgroundResearchEntityBeforeInvocation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Background research on an entity before invocation"@en, "Hintergrundrecherche über eine Entität vor der Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use others' material and magical research: meditate on the entity's name; meet it on the astral through mindscaping; divine for information or relate it to tarot cards or runes; dream the entity through dream magic; visit and meditate at an associated locality; read fiction, myths and folk-tales featuring it; heed hunches and synchronicities; build a feel for it even if not verbalisable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Background Research, pp. 128-129; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBKnowSomethingEntityBeforeInvokingPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Know something of the entity before invoking"@en, "Vor dem Invozieren etwas über die Entität wissen"@de ;
    skos:definition "It is generally thought one should know something about the entity before invoking it; some authorities hold that more knowledge makes the invocation more effective, though sometimes only a name is available."@en ;
    skos:note "unnamed authorities."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBackgroundResearchEntityBeforeInvocation ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInvocation ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Background Research, p. 128; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBInvocationGettingRightMood a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Invocation as getting into the right mood"@en, "Invokation als Hineinfinden in die rechte Stimmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Invocation is basically about getting into the right mood for a particular entity; hunches and synchronicities may matter more than literary research."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Background Research, p. 129; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBNonVerbalInvocation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Non-verbal invocation"@en, "Nonverbale Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bringing forth in oneself the mood in which the entity's presence is felt within or around; the mood may well up spontaneously in response to life events."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Non-Verbal Invocation, p. 129; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBImpromptuPujaPasupati a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Impromptu puja to Pasupati"@en, "Spontane Puja an Pasupati"@de ;
    skos:definition "At a crisis of bound loyalties Hine sat under a tree away from a party, improvised a puja and called on Pasupati; overwhelming need gave the emotional intensity for devotion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Non-Verbal Invocation, p. 129; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPasupatiNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Pasupati"@en, "Pasupati"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tantric herdsman-deity whose functions include freeing what is bound; appeared to Hine blazing with white light."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Pasupati" ;
    pm:nameRole "Tantric herdsman-god, remover of bindings" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Non-Verbal Invocation, p. 129; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEmotionalIntensityOpensDevotionUnfamiliar a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Emotional intensity opens devotion to an unfamiliar god"@en, "Emotionale Intensität öffnet die Hingabe an einen unbekannten Gott"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine reports that, though he had never worked with Pasupati, the emotional intensity born of overwhelming need let him reach the fitting state of devotion; the invocation was less a conscious decision than something that felt right at the time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Non-Verbal Invocation, p. 129; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBVisionInvokedDeityStaringBackSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Vision of the invoked deity staring back"@en, "Vision der invozierten Gottheit, die zurückblickt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine reports being astonished to see Pasupati, ablaze in white light, gazing back at him, marking achieved devotion."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: in Hine's own invocation the deity, Pasupati, was seen blazing with white light and staring back at him; the release followed later, not at once. No deadline and no rate; a single first-person case."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Non-Verbal Invocation, p. 129; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBReleaseEntanglingBindings a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Release from entangling bindings"@en, "Befreiung aus verstrickenden Bindungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The intensity of the Pasupati invocation let Hine let go of bindings he felt entangled in; the effect was not immediate but marked the change-point."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Non-Verbal Invocation, p. 129; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPasupatiPujaYieldsRelease a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Pasupati puja yields release (worked)"@en, "Pasupati-Puja erzeugt Befreiung (wirkte)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Firsthand report that the invocation worked, gradually."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBImpromptuPujaPasupati ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBReleaseEntanglingBindings ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Non-Verbal Invocation, p. 129; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBIdentifyingEmotionalStatesEntities a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Identifying emotional states with entities"@en, "Emotionale Zustände mit Entitäten identifizieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Identify recurring emotional states with particular entities (Hine's Pan-mood: urge to go to the country, untroubled horniness; Isis-state: frosty regality) and experience them, optionally intensified by formal ritual."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Non-Verbal Invocation, p. 130; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBIsisNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Isis"@en, "Isis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Goddess whose state Hine experiences as frosty regality."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Isis" ;
    pm:nameRole "goddess of regal state" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Non-Verbal Invocation, p. 130; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBGroupInvocationDanceMusic a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Group invocation by dance and music"@en, "Gruppeninvokation durch Tanz und Musik"@de ;
    skos:definition "One person calls the deity into himself by dancing while others invoke it with dance and music, stylised or free, drawn from traditions or created for the deity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Non-Verbal Invocation, p. 130; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBInvocationRuinedDeadpanDeliveryFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Invocation ruined by deadpan delivery"@en, "Invokation durch monotonen Vortrag ruiniert"@de ;
    skos:definition "A fine invocation is quickly rendered ineffective if read in a deadpan voice punctuated by ers and ums."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a well-written invocation is made ineffective by a deadpan reading broken by hesitations. Cause: the operator's delivery. No deadline and no rate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 130; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDeliveryFeedbackLoopDramaticAwareness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Delivery as feedback loop of dramatic awareness"@en, "Vortrag als Rückkopplungsschleife dramatischen Bewusstseins"@de ;
    skos:definition "Delivery transmits confidence to self and audience; a more gripping speech intensifies dramatic awareness and draws more people in; participants shift between active and passive roles."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 130; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBPacingBreathInvocationDelivery a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Pacing and breath in invocation delivery"@en, "Tempo und Atem im Invokationsvortrag"@de ;
    skos:definition "Explore pacing speech, deliberately breathing louder, and at the climax becoming breathless with a slight tremble; a whisper can beat a shout; learn the speech or improvise rather than read; keep it simple and short."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, pp. 130-131; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDrawingListenersAtmosphereThroughVocal a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Drawing listeners into the atmosphere through vocal emotion"@en, "Zuhörer durch stimmliche Emotion in die Atmosphäre ziehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Successfully projecting awe, reverence or passion makes self and others pick up the emotive undertones and be drawn into the atmosphere."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 131; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBVoicePatternChangesTranceDeepensSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Voice pattern changes as trance deepens"@en, "Stimmmuster ändert sich mit vertiefter Trance"@de ;
    skos:definition "People's voice patterns shift as they pass through trance stages, which others pick up, generating dramatic awareness."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the voice pattern of participants changes as they enter different stages of trance, and others pick it up. No deadline or rate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 131; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBReadingBooksLongSpeechesHamperCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Reading from books and long speeches hamper invocation"@en, "Vorlesen aus Büchern und lange Reden behindern die Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reading textbooks, especially others' writing in the dark or on a windy moor, and long speeches undermine confident delivery."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBPacingBreathInvocationDelivery ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 131; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDeliveryPracticeYieldsAtmosphericDraw a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Delivery practice yields atmospheric draw"@en, "Vortragspraxis erzeugt atmosphärische Sogwirkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Practised delivery produces the drawing-in of listeners."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBPacingBreathInvocationDelivery ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDrawingListenersAtmosphereThroughVocal ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 131; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBStructureRhythmInvocations a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Structure and rhythm of invocations"@en, "Struktur und Rhythmus von Invokationen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Invocations résumé the figure's qualities, energies, legends and deeds; rhythm generates mood and has physiological effects on breath and heartbeat (fast and frenetic for Pan, slow and ponderous for Cronus); an invocation may read poorly yet sound excellent chanted."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 131; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBCronusNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Cronus"@en, "Kronos"@de ;
    skos:definition "God of Time, whose invocation would be slow and ponderous."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Cronus" ;
    pm:nameRole "god of time" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 131; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBThreePartInvocationYieldsAvatarhood a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Three-part invocation yields avatarhood"@en, "Dreiteilige Invokation erzeugt Avatarschaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "The three-part form produces identification with the figure."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCThreePartInvocation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBecomingMythicFiguresAvatarEarth ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 132; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBecomingMythicFiguresAvatarEarth a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming a mythic figure's avatar on earth"@en, "Irdischer Avatar einer mythischen Gestalt werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "For ritual purposes one becomes the figure and can act with its power, from oracle to frenzied dance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 132; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSingleVesselVersusCollectivePossession a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Single vessel versus collective possession"@en, "Einzelnes Gefäß versus kollektive Besessenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the Western Mystery tradition one person is vessel and others celebrants; elsewhere many may be possessed by the same deity at once, e.g. about 300 Haitians possessed by Legba marching on the presidential residence."@en ;
    skos:note "Haitian case (reported)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 132; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBLegbaNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Legba"@en, "Legba"@de ;
    skos:definition "Haitian god said to have possessed some 300 people simultaneously in a political protest march."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Legba" ;
    pm:nameRole "Vodou deity (lwa)" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 132; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBStatusShiftsInvocation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Status shifts in invocation"@en, "Statuswechsel in der Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Borrowed from drama and oratory: social interactions move along a low-high status scale; in invocation one starts as a supplicant looking up to a deity and finishes acting with the deity's status, others treating one accordingly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 132; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBConfusingRitualRoleEverydayPersonCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Confusing ritual role with everyday person"@en, "Ritualrolle mit Alltagsperson verwechseln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Status shifts cause role confusion; a person who is a goddess within ritual should not be so treated once it ends."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBStatusShiftsInvocation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 132; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEgoInflationIdentifyingMythicFiguresCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Ego inflation from identifying with mythic figures"@en, "Ego-Aufblähung durch Identifikation mit mythischen Gestalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The prime danger is blowing up one's ego; continually identifying with a figure that reinforces one's self-image imbalances one toward those tendencies. Hine knew at least three people seriously disturbed after working exclusively with lunar oracular figures that accentuated their tendency to passive oracular trance."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInvocation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, pp. 132-133; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSeriousDisturbanceExclusiveWorkLunarFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Serious disturbance from exclusive work with lunar oracular figures"@en, "Ernste Störung durch ausschließliche Arbeit mit lunaren Orakelgestalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "At least three people became seriously disturbed because exclusive lunar, oracular work accentuated a predisposition to passive trance."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: at least three people Hine knew became seriously disturbed after working only with lunar, oracular figures that strengthened their tendency to passive trance. Cause: the operators, through one-sided identification with figures that reinforce a predisposition. No deadline; three cases are counted."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 133; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBContinualSelfAssessmentWhenInvokingPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Continual self-assessment when invoking"@en, "Ständige Selbstprüfung beim Invozieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Understanding and continually assessing one's strengths, weak points and ego-identifications is needed, above all for teachers and group leaders; skipping it risks the ego inflation and imbalance described."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondASelfAssessment ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInvocation ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "ego inflation and imbalance toward reinforced tendencies, even serious disturbance" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 133; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBIntensityScalesInputHumourRitual a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intensity scales with input; humour in ritual"@en, "Intensität wächst mit dem Einsatz; Humor im Ritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "The more put into an invocation (gesture, lighting, props, smell, taste, music, staging; also silence, grunts, howls) the more intense the effect; humour is an often neglected element."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 133; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBLaughingOnesWayOutSituations a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Laughing one's way out of situations"@en, "Sich aus Situationen herauslachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "An infectious laugh is a useful skill; one can literally laugh one's way out of some situations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 133; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBExperimentingInvocationDelivery a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Experimenting with invocation delivery"@en, "Mit dem Invokationsvortrag experimentieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Collect speeches by others and read them aloud until a delivery feels effective; tape experiments, perhaps for background use; use music; then preferably write and use your own invocations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 133; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBConfidenceCloseContactInvokedFigure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Confidence and close contact with the invoked figure"@en, "Selbstvertrauen und enge Verbindung mit der invozierten Gestalt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Using one's own invocations builds confidence, a feel for what works, and close contact with the figure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 133; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBOwnInvocationsYieldConfidenceContact a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Own invocations yield confidence and contact"@en, "Eigene Invokationen erzeugen Vertrauen und Kontakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Writing one's own invocations produces confidence and closeness to the figure."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBExperimentingInvocationDelivery ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBConfidenceCloseContactInvokedFigure ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 133; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBShapeShiftingAnimalIdentification a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Shape-shifting by animal identification"@en, "Gestaltwandeln durch Tieridentifikation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Observe an animal's characteristic postures, facial expressions, vocalisations and behaviours, and become it by close identification; trance intensity depends on how much abandonment one allows. Human figures are generally easier to invoke than non-human."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, pp. 133-134; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBShapeShifting a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shape-shifting (becoming an animal)"@en, "Gestaltwandel (Tier werden)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Becoming the animal through identification with its characteristics."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 133; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAnimalIdentificationYieldsShapeShifting a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Animal identification yields shape-shifting"@en, "Tieridentifikation erzeugt Gestaltwandel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Observing and identifying with an animal produces the shape-shifting trance."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBShapeShiftingAnimalIdentification ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBShapeShifting ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Verbal Invocations, p. 133; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBOvershadowing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Overshadowing and possession as two extremes"@en, "Überschattung und Besessenheit als zwei Extreme"@de ;
    skos:definition "Invocation yields states between overshadowing (imbued with the figure's power, some detachment, volition retained) and possession (personality almost or wholly submerged, partial or no recollection)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 134; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSignsOvershadowingSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Signs of overshadowing"@en, "Zeichen der Überschattung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Overshadowed persons report a changed sense of body shape and at times a dissonance between what they wanted as the entity and as themselves, with volition kept."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the overshadowed person feels imbued with the figure's power, perceives the body's shape as altered and may notice a dissonance between what he wants as the entity and as himself, keeping volition. No deadline or rate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 134; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPartialNoRecollectionAfterPossessionSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Partial or no recollection after possession"@en, "Teilweise oder keine Erinnerung nach Besessenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "When possession occurs the individual commonly recalls little or nothing of what happened; Maya Deren woke to find Erzulie had ridden her and she had led the ritual."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: after possession the person recalls little or nothing of what happened, as Maya Deren reports of being ridden by Erzulie. No deadline; rate in words only (not uncommon). Source named: Maya Deren, The Voodoo Gods (1953)"@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 134; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBErzulieNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Erzulie"@en, "Erzulie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Voodoo goddess said to have mounted and ridden Maya Deren, who then led the ritual."@en ;
    skos:note "Maya Deren."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Erzulie" ;
    pm:nameRole "Vodou goddess (lwa)" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 134; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFeatsUnderDeepPossessionLoa a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Feats under deep possession by the Loa"@en, "Leistungen unter tiefer Besessenheit durch die Loa"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deeply possessed people are said to do what would normally incapacitate them: those possessed by the Loa hold hot coals in the mouth unburnt, dance manically for hours, drink much rum without drunkenness, and discourse on unknown subjects."@en ;
    skos:note "ethnographic reports on Voodoo."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 134; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBLoaNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Loa"@en, "Loa"@de ;
    skos:definition "Voodoo spirits whose possession of devotees grants feats beyond normal limits."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Loa" ;
    pm:nameRole "Vodou spirits" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 134; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessionWidespreadModeDivineUnion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Possession as widespread mode of divine union"@en, "Besessenheit als verbreitete Form der Vereinigung mit dem Göttlichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Possession is called perhaps the commonest mode of uniting with the divine in history: ancient Egypt, earliest Qabalah, the Delphic oracle, the Theurgists (Proclus defines theurgy as operations of divine possession), Voudoun, Santeria, Macumba, tribal cultures and early Christian speaking in tongues."@en ;
    skos:note "Proclus; historical summary."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, pp. 134-135; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBStPaulManageSpeakingTonguesCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "St Paul: manage speaking in tongues decently and in order"@en, "Paulus: Zungenrede anständig und geordnet handhaben"@de ;
    skos:definition "St Paul, though bearing hallmarks of sudden possession himself, warned the Corinthians that if all speak in tongues outsiders will think them mad, and that all should be done in order."@en ;
    skos:note "St Paul, 1 Corinthians 14."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessionWidespreadModeDivineUnion ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 135; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPhysiognomicIndicatorsPossessionSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Physiognomic indicators of possession"@en, "Physiognomische Anzeichen der Besessenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The possessed person shows changed pitch of voice, facial expression, gesture and posture; facial muscles may re-contract into patterns unlike the person's own; these signal the figure's arrival and heighten group awareness; once one is possessed others may follow more easily."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: altered voice pitch, facial expression, posture and gesture, with the facial muscles setting into patterns unlike the person's own, mark that the invoked figure has arrived. No deadline or rate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 135; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDisinhibitedFeatsPossession a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Disinhibited feats in possession"@en, "Enthemmte Leistungen in der Besessenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Possession lets one drop normal limitations and perform feats normally impossible or socially forbidden."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 135; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessionWestVersusVoodooCultures a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Possession in West versus Voodoo cultures"@en, "Besessenheit im Westen versus Voodoo-Kulturen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Voodoo possession is expected and sanctioned though often unpleasant; in the West such disinhibition is frowned on and seen as demonic, making possession rarer than overshadowing, though increasingly common among chaos magicians."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 135; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBLosingControlKeyPossessionLicence a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Losing control as key to possession; licence to behave out of character"@en, "Kontrollverlust als Schlüssel zur Besessenheit; Erlaubnis, aus der Rolle zu fallen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ability to release inhibitions takes time for many, though some unconfident people let go quickly; possession licenses behaving out of character, sanctioned by officers, celebrants and audience. A voudou celebrant told S. E. Simpson that what one fears to do, one does when possessed."@en ;
    skos:note "S. E. Simpson, Religious Cults of the Caribbean (1970)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, pp. 135-136; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBTranceLostWhenInhibitionsClashFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Trance lost when inhibitions clash with the entity's persona"@en, "Trance geht verloren, wenn Hemmungen mit der Persona der Entität kollidieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine has seen first-time attempters clearly lose trance when their sense of acceptable behaviour conflicted with the persona taken on; built-up expectations are hard to shed even in ritual."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: first-time attempters lose the trance when their sense of proper behaviour clashes with the character they have taken on. Cause: the operator's inhibitions and built-up expectations. No deadline and no rate; observed by Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, pp. 135-136; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBUnclearLimitsPermissionModernPossessionCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Unclear limits of permission in modern possession rites"@en, "Unklare Grenzen der Erlaubnis in modernen Besessenheitsriten"@de ;
    skos:definition "In present-day rites the bounds of allowed behaviour are not always clearly defined, whereas anthropological accounts treat apparent violence as approved and expected play within the ceremony."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBLosingControlKeyPossessionLicence ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 136; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBTeachThatVesselBearsNoPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Teach that the vessel bears no responsibility for the spirit's conduct"@en, "Lehren, dass der Einzelne nicht für das Verhalten des Geistes verantwortlich ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "In teaching possession it is called essential to convey that the person bears no responsibility for how the spirit behaves; once all can separate person from god, the need to cling to one's personality diminishes."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBTeachingThatVesselNotResponsible ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBLosingControlKeyPossessionLicence ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 136; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBTeachingThatVesselNotResponsible a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Teaching that the vessel is not responsible for the spirit"@en, "Lehren, dass das Gefäß nicht für den Geist verantwortlich ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "When teaching others to become possessed, convey that the individual is not answerable for how the spirit acts, so that all present can tell the person apart from the god who is present."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 136; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessionCoCreatedAllPresent a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Possession co-created by all present"@en, "Besessenheit wird von allen Anwesenden miterzeugt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Possession emerges from the whole interplay of performers, audience, officers and Master of Ceremonies; it is partly theatrical, per accounts by Deren, Seabrook and others."@en ;
    skos:note "Maya Deren, William Seabrook."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 136; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMasterCeremoniesIndulgentHighStatus a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Master of Ceremonies as indulgent high-status ringmaster"@en, "Zeremonienmeister als nachsichtiger Zirkusdirektor hohen Status"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keith Johnstone notes Voudou officiating priests hold high status yet are indulgent toward the often childlike possessed; the MC may be seen as a ringmaster coaxing possessees toward gnosis and whipping on the audience."@en ;
    skos:note "Keith Johnstone, Impro (1981)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, pp. 136-137; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRunningPossessionWorkingMc a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Running a possession working as MC"@en, "Eine Besessenheitsarbeit als Zeremonienmeister leiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The MC makes sure the spirit conducts itself (well or badly) as fits and that the audience actively participates in the performance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 137; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPassiveAudienceBeratedSpiritFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Passive audience berated by the spirit"@en, "Passives Publikum vom Geist getadelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine has often seen audiences in possession workings stand uneasily around the possessee and sometimes be berated by the spirit for not participating."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the audience stands uneasily round the possessed person and is at times berated by the spirit for not taking part. Cause: the audience and, by implication, a Master of Ceremonies who fails to draw it in. No deadline; rate in words only (all too often)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 137; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEvokedSpiritsAppearanceDependsRitual a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evoked spirit's appearance depends on ritual space"@en, "Erscheinen des evozierten Geistes hängt vom Ritualraum ab"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine finds that whether an evoked goetic spirit appears successfully depends largely on the ritual space and appropriate props; invocatory and evocatory rites are context-derived."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 137; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBClearSharedContextPossessionWorkingPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Clear shared context for possession working"@en, "Klarer gemeinsamer Kontext für Besessenheitsarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Good possession working requires a context known and understood by all; as with evoked goetic spirits whose appearance depends on ritual space and props."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBClearContextKnownAllParticipants ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRunningPossessionWorkingMc ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "conflicting expectations give results at variance with participants' intentions" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 137; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBClearContextKnownAllParticipants a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Clear context known to all participants"@en, "Klarer, allen Teilnehmern bekannter Kontext"@de ;
    skos:definition "A possession working is said to need a context that every participant knows and understands, as an evoked goetic spirit needs the fitting ritual space and props; where everyone present already expects a known character of the entity the issue does not arise."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 137; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBGhedeNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Ghede"@en, "Ghede"@de ;
    skos:definition "A loa reputed to be especially sexually active; William Sargant reports two Haitian girls simultaneously possessed by Ghede, enacting a symbolic rape and collapsing, with no memory afterwards."@en ;
    skos:note "William Sargant."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Ghede" ;
    pm:nameRole "sexually active loa" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 137; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessedPersonsCannotBeFaulted a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Possessed persons cannot be faulted"@en, "Besessene sind nicht schuldfähig"@de ;
    skos:definition "In many possession cults whatever the possessed do is the indwelling entity's act and cannot be faulted, and afterwards nobody tells them what they did (Sargant's Ghede account: only the boyfriends were upset and could say nothing)."@en ;
    skos:note "William Sargant."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 137; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBGroupSizeDepthPossessionTrance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Group size and depth of possession trance"@en, "Gruppengröße und Tiefe der Besessenheitstrance"@de ;
    skos:definition "Small close-knit groups build trust conducive to possession; large frenzied workings with strobes, massed dancing and screaming allow deep possession quickly, as the crowd sheds the dominant personality and being the focus of attention triggers fight-flight arousal washing away self-image in adrenaline."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, pp. 137-138; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBInducingPossessionDrumsDanceChant a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Inducing possession: drums, dance, chant, masks"@en, "Besessenheit herbeiführen: Trommeln, Tanz, Gesang, Masken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use rhythmic drumming, dancing and chanting, plus strobes and audio effects; use masks and props; in some cults priests discern the incarnating entity and hand over its props; in Western practice the vehicle visualises or is dressed in the garb and is chosen before the ritual."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 138; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBExcitatoryInductionYieldsPossession a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Excitatory induction yields possession"@en, "Erregende Induktion erzeugt Besessenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drumming, dancing, chanting and props produce possession trance."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBInducingPossessionDrumsDanceChant ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessionTrance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 138; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAnonymityThroughMasks a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Anonymity through masks"@en, "Anonymität durch Masken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Masks confer a degree of anonymity on the wearer."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 138; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSpiritMaskUnfinishedGods a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spirit as mask; unfinished gods"@en, "Geist als Maske; unfertige Götter"@de ;
    skos:definition "Masks particular to a spirit show consistent behaviour whoever wears them; spirits tend to conservatism and can be defined as an arising character shaped by belief and context; this fails for unfinished gods lacking an informing tradition or shared expectation, such as Baphomet."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 138; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBUncriticalBeliefBeyondRitualBecomesCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Uncritical belief beyond ritual becomes dysfunctional"@en, "Unkritischer Glaube über das Ritual hinaus wird dysfunktional"@de ;
    skos:definition "Total belief in possession is important inside ritual, but carrying uncritical belief beyond it may turn dysfunctional; Hine wonders how chaos magicians integrate oracular statements when consensual belief is shed on leaving the temple."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessionTrance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, pp. 138-139; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFourProblemsPossession a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Four problems of possession"@en, "Vier Probleme der Besessenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's list: belief (uncritical belief beyond ritual), knowledge of the entity (unprepared vessel), fixation on a persona, banishing/earthing (lingering possession)."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Prime Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, pp. 138-140; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEntityManifestingUnpreparedVesselCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Entity manifesting in an unprepared vessel"@en, "Entität manifestiert in einem unvorbereiteten Gefäß"@de ;
    skos:definition "A vessel without prior knowledge of the entity's character, myth or behaviour cannot coherently deliver its specialised knowledge (e.g. diagnostic advice through healers); novices may lack skill to deliver messages accurately."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessionTrance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 139; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBIncoherentInaccurateDeliveryPossessedNoviceFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Incoherent or inaccurate delivery by possessed novice"@en, "Unzusammenhängende oder ungenaue Übermittlung durch besessenen Neuling"@de ;
    skos:definition "Even when truly possessed, one lacking knowledge of the spirit's specialism, or new to possession, may fail to deliver a coherent or accurate message."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a possessed vessel with no knowledge of the entity's specialism, or new to possession, cannot give a coherent or accurate delivery even when truly possessed. Cause: the operator's lack of preparation and skill. No deadline and no rate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 139; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFixationSinglePersonaCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Fixation on a single persona"@en, "Fixierung auf eine einzige Persona"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some magicians manifest the same persona whatever the entity; arguably not true possession but ego-reinforcement before an audience, which can lead to obsessional mania as one self dominates; often rooted in insecurity."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessionTrance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 139; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSamePersonaRegardlessEntityNotFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Same persona regardless of entity: not true possession"@en, "Gleiche Persona unabhängig von der Entität: keine echte Besessenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sign that possession did not occur: identical behaviour and persona appear whatever entity is invoked."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the same behaviour and persona appear whatever entity is called, which Hine says is arguably not possession but ego-reinforcement before an audience. Cause: the operator's fixation, often rooted in insecurity. No deadline and no rate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 139; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBLingeringDelayedPossessionAfterRiteCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Lingering or delayed possession after the rite"@en, "Fortdauernde oder verzögerte Besessenheit nach dem Ritus"@de ;
    skos:definition "People may stay possessed after the rite or become spontaneously possessed hours or days later (in religion leading to conversion); psychological models say that if the experience does not end in exhaustion or collapse, its effects may linger."@en ;
    skos:note "unnamed psychological models of possession."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBKeyElementsPossessionWorking ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, pp. 139-140; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessionCanBeLifeChangingCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Possession can be life-changing and painful"@en, "Besessenheit kann lebensverändernd und schmerzhaft sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "A first possession may have far-reaching life-changing consequences, onset sudden or gradual, and some accounts call it agonizingly painful."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessionTrance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 140; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBResistanceIntensifiesPossession a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Resistance intensifies possession"@en, "Widerstand verstärkt die Besessenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sargant notes resisting the onset more, the more intense it becomes; Hine finds that consciously limiting depth made it more intense than expected. Possession is a learned response."@en ;
    skos:note "William Sargant; confirmed firstPerson by Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 140; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessionTrance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Possession trance"@en, "Besessenheitstrance"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state in which an entity incarnates in the vehicle; with practice it can be reached relatively quickly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, pp. 138-140; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBKeyElementsPossessionWorking a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Key elements of a possession working"@en, "Schlüsselelemente einer Besessenheitsarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Warm up with banishing to direct attention toward the entity; use excitatory gnosis (drumming, dancing) to stress the body so awareness inflames with the entity's image; let possession arise spontaneously or direct it into a chosen vehicle; steer the god with mild rather than commanding requests; if the god will not leave, add stress, capture the celebrant if needed and summon them back from trance till the persona leaves."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 140; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessionWorkingYieldsPossessionTrance a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Possession working yields possession trance"@en, "Besessenheitsarbeit erzeugt Besessenheitstrance"@de ;
    skos:definition "The key elements produce possession by the invoked entity."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBKeyElementsPossessionWorking ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessionTrance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 140; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBOnlyInvokedEntitiesManifestGods a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Only invoked entities manifest; gods resent command"@en, "Nur invozierte Entitäten manifestieren; Götter verübeln Befehle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Someone other than the vehicle may be possessed, but entities other than those invoked rarely appear (Sargant: revivalists are not possessed by Kali); gods, being regal, react badly to command yet respond to gentler steering, hence priests' indulgence."@en ;
    skos:note "William Sargant; Keith Johnstone."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 140; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBGodReluctantLeaveVehicleFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "God reluctant to leave the vehicle"@en, "Gott will das Gefäß nicht verlassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Frequently the god resists leaving; modern magic handles it by further stress, capture and calling out of trance."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the god is reluctant to leave the vehicle. Cause: the entity. No deadline; rate in words only (often)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 140; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessionYieldsOracleChargingMythic a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Possession yields oracle, charging, mythic transformation"@en, "Besessenheit erzeugt Orakel, Ladung, mythische Verwandlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Possession work is put to these listed uses."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBKeyElementsPossessionWorking ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBOracularInformationThroughPossession, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBChargingMagicalWeaponsThroughPossession, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSharingEntitysPowerOracleInvoked, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBLivingMythicTransformation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 140; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBOracularInformationThroughPossession a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Oracular information through possession"@en, "Orakelwissen durch Besessenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Possession can yield oracular information, as Greeks and Tibetans did."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 140; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBChargingMagicalWeaponsThroughPossession a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Charging magical weapons through possession"@en, "Magische Waffen durch Besessenheit laden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Possession can be used to charge magical weapons."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 140; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBLivingMythicTransformation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Living a mythic transformation"@en, "Eine mythische Verwandlung durchleben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Possession lets one share the god's power (as in masses) or undergo a specific mythic transformation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, pp. 140-141; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessionMayDevolveHabituatedLimitationCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Possession may devolve into habituated limitation"@en, "Besessenheit kann zur gewohnheitsmäßigen Begrenzung verkommen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Like all techniques its use needs careful analysis and evaluation lest it become a habituated limitation; it can be hair-raising."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBKeyElementsPossessionWorking ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPossessionMustBeExperiencedBe a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Possession must be experienced to be understood"@en, "Besessenheit muss erlebt werden, um verstanden zu werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Care with ingredients and skill in combining them intensify the experience; no theory conveys it; it needs experience and practice; useful to study cultures where possession is defined, and relate it to conversion, hypnosis and abreactive therapy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Overshadowing and Possession, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBCrowleysSevenDevotionalStancesSeries a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Crowley's seven devotional stances (Liber Astarte)"@en, "Crowleys sieben devotionale Haltungen (Liber Astarte)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Address the entity successively as slave to master, vassal to lord, child to parent, priest to deity, sibling to sibling, close friend, and finally lover; requires paradigm and status shifts."@en ;
    skos:note "Crowley, Liber Astarte."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDevotionalStanceSlaveMaster ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDevotionalStanceVassalLord ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDevotionalStanceChildParent ;
    rdf:_4 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDevotionalStancePriestDeity ;
    rdf:_5 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDevotionalStanceSiblingSibling ;
    rdf:_6 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDevotionalStanceCloseFriend ;
    rdf:_7 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDevotionalStanceLover ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Crowley's Liber Astarte, as Hine reports it, has the magician address the invoked entity in seven stances taken in order, as slave to master, vassal to lord, child to parent, priest to deity, sibling to sibling, close friend and at last lover; each stance takes its sense from its place in a progression of paradigm and status shifts toward ever closer intimacy with the entity." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Devotional Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDevotionalStanceSlaveMaster a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Devotional stance: slave to master"@en, "Devotionale Haltung: Sklave zum Herrn"@de ;
    skos:definition "First stance of the Liber Astarte schema: the magician addresses the entity as a slave addressing a master."@en ;
    skos:note "Crowley, Liber Astarte, as reported by Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Devotional Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDevotionalStanceVassalLord a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Devotional stance: vassal to lord"@en, "Devotionale Haltung: Vasall zum Lehnsherrn"@de ;
    skos:definition "Second stance of the Liber Astarte schema: the magician addresses the entity as a vassal addressing his lord."@en ;
    skos:note "Crowley, Liber Astarte, as reported by Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Devotional Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDevotionalStanceChildParent a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Devotional stance: child to parent"@en, "Devotionale Haltung: Kind zum Elternteil"@de ;
    skos:definition "Third stance of the Liber Astarte schema: the magician addresses the entity as a child addressing its parent."@en ;
    skos:note "Crowley, Liber Astarte, as reported by Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Devotional Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDevotionalStancePriestDeity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Devotional stance: priest to deity"@en, "Devotionale Haltung: Priester zur Gottheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fourth stance of the Liber Astarte schema: the magician addresses the entity as a priest addressing a deity."@en ;
    skos:note "Crowley, Liber Astarte, as reported by Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Devotional Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDevotionalStanceSiblingSibling a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Devotional stance: sibling to sibling"@en, "Devotionale Haltung: Geschwister zu Geschwister"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fifth stance of the Liber Astarte schema: the magician addresses the entity as a sibling addressing another."@en ;
    skos:note "Crowley, Liber Astarte, as reported by Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Devotional Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDevotionalStanceCloseFriend a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Devotional stance: close friend"@en, "Devotionale Haltung: Enger Freund"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sixth stance of the Liber Astarte schema: the magician addresses the entity as a close friend."@en ;
    skos:note "Crowley, Liber Astarte, as reported by Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Devotional Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDevotionalStanceLover a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Devotional stance: lover"@en, "Devotionale Haltung: Liebender"@de ;
    skos:definition "Seventh and last stance of the Liber Astarte schema: the magician addresses the entity as a lover."@en ;
    skos:note "Crowley, Liber Astarte, as reported by Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Devotional Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBMagicalRetirement a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical retirement (devotional monasticism)"@en, "Magischer Rückzug (devotionales Mönchtum)"@de ;
    skos:definition "For days, weeks or months invoke one deity progressively each day, e.g. through the seven stances of Liber Astarte."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Devotional Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBKnowledgePersonalRelationshipDeity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowledge of and personal relationship with a deity"@en, "Wissen über eine Gottheit und persönliche Beziehung zu ihr"@de ;
    skos:definition "Progressive invocatory work yields much information on an entity's nature, qualities and aspects and builds a personal relationship with it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Devotional Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMagicalRetirementYieldsKnowledgeRelationship a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Magical retirement yields knowledge and relationship"@en, "Magischer Rückzug erzeugt Wissen und Beziehung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Progressive daily invocation produces knowledge of and relationship with the deity."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBMagicalRetirement, pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBEverydayDevotionalInvocation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBKnowledgePersonalRelationshipDeity ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Devotional Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBEverydayDevotionalInvocation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Everyday devotional invocation"@en, "Alltägliche devotionale Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "(a) behave in daily life as would please the entity; (b) discern its hand stirring everyday events; (c) set up a personal shrine with regular offerings (money, incense, flowers, sweets); (d) devise portable prayers, visualisations, mantras, meditations (Hine kept Ganesha as lord of scribes on his work computer). Genuineness from the heart matters more than formality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Devotional Magic, pp. 141-142; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBGaneshaLordScribesNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Ganesha, lord of scribes"@en, "Ganesha, Herr der Schreiber"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hindu deity depicted as lord of scribes, given devotion by Hine at his workplace computer; also cited for Indian sweets in ritual."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCGaneshaNaming (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos holds Ganesha to be the binder and transformer of obsessional demons and a deity of wealth; here he is depicted as lord of scribes and given unobtrusive devotion at a workplace computer."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Ganesha" ;
    pm:nameRole "lord of scribes" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Invocation, Devotional Magic, p. 142; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .



#
# Evocation
#
pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEvocationYieldsTaskPerformingEntities a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Evocation yields task-performing entities"@en, "Evokation erzeugt aufgabenerfüllende Entitäten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Evocation produces entities able to perform the listed tasks."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBasicTwoPhaseEvocation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEvokedEntitiesHealingProtectionInspiration, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBModifyingOnesOwnBehaviourCognition, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEntitiesGuidesDreamingAstralJourneys, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEntitiesPatrollingGuardingSites ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, p. 143; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEvokedEntitiesHealingProtectionInspiration a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evoked entities for healing, protection, inspiration, offence"@en, "Evozierte Entitäten für Heilung, Schutz, Inspiration, Angriff"@de ;
    skos:definition "Evoked entities may be sent to perform results-oriented tasks such as protection, healing, inspiring, or offensive work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, p. 143; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBModifyingOnesOwnBehaviourCognition a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Modifying one's own behaviour and cognition via evoked entity"@en, "Eigenes Verhalten und Denken durch evozierte Entität verändern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Evoked entities may be used to change one's own patterns of behaviour and cognition."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, p. 143; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEntitiesGuidesDreamingAstralJourneys a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Entities as guides in dreaming and astral journeys"@en, "Entitäten als Führer für Traumarbeit und Astralerkundung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Evoked entities can guide one in dreaming work and astral exploration."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, p. 143; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEntitiesPatrollingGuardingSites a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Entities patrolling and guarding sites"@en, "Entitäten als Patrouille und Wächter von Orten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Entities can patrol one's home, belongings or an outdoor area; a common use is placing them as guardians at environmentally threatened sites."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, p. 143; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBasicTwoPhaseEvocation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Basic two-phase evocation"@en, "Grundlegende zweiphasige Evokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "1) Choose an entity from a grimoire, create one, or contact one via dream-work, trance or scrying. 2) Call it into a defined space per the chosen system: e.g. Lesser Key: triangle with its symbols, command the demons to appear, subjugate and send them; shamanic: psychoactive vision-quest to meet the spirit and learn its name and form, then on return call it into a prepared bottle, crystal, stone or mask."@en ;
    skos:note "Lesser Key of Solomon method reported."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, The Dynamics of Evocation, pp. 143-144; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFourStagesEntityDesign a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Four stages of entity design (after COBOL)"@en, "Vier Stufen des Entitätsentwurfs (nach COBOL)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine orders the design of an evoked entity in four stages, Identification, Environment, Data and Procedure, which he says are taken from the procedure for writing a program in COBOL."@en ;
    skos:note "Derived from COBOL programming procedure. Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBServitorDesignSequence (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos orders servitor design in seven steps from general intent to shape; here the design of any evoked entity is ordered in four stages borrowed from COBOL. Kept as an ordering, not a series, because the stages are named by content and none takes its sense from its place."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Prime Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, The Dynamics of Evocation, pp. 144-145; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBDesigningEvokedEntityFourStages a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Designing an evoked entity in four stages"@en, "Eine evozierte Entität in vier Stufen entwerfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "1) Identification: discover or create name, shape, number, form, persona; treat it as an individual unit for the working, the paradigm providing the belief buffer. 2) Environment: set the paradigm and ritual parameters to establish it, allot its task and send it; choose qualities, symbols or organs suited to the task. 3) Data: isolate variables such as time limit, window of opportunity, optimal conditions, and activation cues (time-periods, conjunctions, moon-phases, command words). 4) Procedure: write the Statement of Intent covering what, when, where and how."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBDesigningServitor (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos gives servitor design in seven steps (general intent, specific intent, symbols, time, name, base, shape); here an evoked entity of any kind is designed through identification, environment, data with activation cues, and a statement of intent."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, The Dynamics of Evocation, pp. 144-145; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEntitySeedingNewIdeasCommand a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Entity seeding new ideas on a command word"@en, "Entität, die auf ein Befehlswort neue Ideen einpflanzt"@de ;
    skos:definition "An entity tasked to plant fresh ideas in the magician can be activated whenever he vibrates a set word or phrase."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, The Dynamics of Evocation, p. 145; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEntityDesignYieldsCueActivated a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Entity design yields cue-activated idea-seeding"@en, "Entitätsentwurf erzeugt durch Signal aktivierte Ideengebung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Specifying a command-word cue in the Data stage produces an on-demand idea-seeding entity."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBDesigningEvokedEntityFourStages ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEntitySeedingNewIdeasCommand ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, The Dynamics of Evocation, p. 145; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEvokedEntityProgramShell a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evoked entity as program shell"@en, "Evozierte Entität als Programmhülle"@de ;
    skos:definition "The entity resembles a program shell having name, identity, functions and variable processing; the operation launches it; the magician is the input device; the world(s) into which it is launched are the output device."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, The Dynamics of Evocation, p. 145; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEvokedEntitiesFollowTheirCreating a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evoked entities follow their creating paradigm"@en, "Evozierte Entitäten folgen ihrem Erzeugungsparadigma"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some evidence is said to support that evoked entities behave in line with the ritual process and underlying paradigm they were created in."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, Servitors, p. 145; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBeliefDangerousDemonsMakesThemFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Belief in dangerous demons makes them uncontrolled"@en, "Glaube an gefährliche Dämonen macht sie unkontrollierbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "A magician in classical Goetia believing its demons dangerous and prone to escape control will likely find them so."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a magician who believes that Goetic demons are dangerous and apt to break control is likely to find them so. Cause: the operator's paradigm, which the entity follows. No deadline and no rate; hedged with some evidence."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, Servitors, p. 145; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBHiddenVariablesBoundEntitiesMayCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Hidden variables; bound entities may become uncontrolled"@en, "Verborgene Variablen; gebundene Entitäten können außer Kontrolle geraten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Any operation has hidden variables needing due care; magical apocrypha tell of bound entities becoming uncontrolled, and despite their anecdotal nature common sense demands care."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBasicTwoPhaseEvocation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, Servitors, p. 145; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBThreePerspectivesNatureSpirits a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three perspectives on the nature of spirits"@en, "Drei Perspektiven auf das Wesen der Geister"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pantheistic (spirits real and independent; religious variant: only our gods real, others demons); Psychological (aspects of psyche, gods as Higher Self, demons as Lower Self); Interactionist."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Prime Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, p. 146; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBInteractionistPerspective a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Interactionist Perspective on spirits"@en, "Interaktionistische Perspektive auf Geister"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spirits partly originate in the psyche yet have independent existence; generated by will or unconsciously, given shape, identity and powers, they can act independently of their makers and over time may become independent and seemingly sentient."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, p. 146; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSpiritsEverywhereHabitsTechnologiesCities a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spirits everywhere: habits, technologies, cities"@en, "Geister überall: Gewohnheiten, Technologien, Städte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magicians relate to spirits as if real; restricting spirits to classical terms is a limiting trap; habits, addictions and obsessing fantasies can be worked with as entities; consider elementals of petrochemicals, electricity, fission, urban spirits, a machine-elemental of computer networks."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, p. 146; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBWorkingHabitsAddictionsEntities a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Working with habits and addictions as entities"@en, "Mit Gewohnheiten und Süchten als Entitäten arbeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Habits, addictions or obsessive fantasies can be treated, and so worked with, as magical entities."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, p. 146; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBImaginationMovieDirectorFacultySeeing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Imagination and the movie-director faculty in seeing spirits"@en, "Imagination und die Regisseursfähigkeit beim Sehen von Geistern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Out of time-sense, belief and imagination the mind's movie-director faculty produces glimpsed effects; once one person sees an entity others become likelier to (UFO and monster flaps); parapsychologists' fictional spirit biographies let test groups receive information from the spirit."@en ;
    skos:note "unnamed parapsychologists."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, pp. 146-147; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBHumanSpiritInteractionEcosystemExperience a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Human-spirit interaction as ecosystem; experience over explanation"@en, "Mensch-Geist-Interaktion als Ökosystem; Erfahrung vor Erklärung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many interwoven factors (electromagnetic shifts, neurotransmitters, belief, place history, local myth, expectation) create the experience; for chaos magicians experience matters more than explanation, models arising from it and opening new areas."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, p. 147; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBFlowchartCybersorcery a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Flowchart cybersorcery"@en, "Flussdiagramm-Cyberzauberei"@de ;
    skos:definition "1) Define the general magical intent for the situation. 2) Analyse intensively to identify variables usable to influence it and how changes may play out, e.g. via SWOT or divination for overview and tweak-points. 3) Design the flowchart with levels of operation (cognition, behaviour patterns, emotions, self-referential statements, wild events, time factors, cues and signals, events beyond the program). Then seal it in an envelope and forget it, or fire it ritually; trigger by any factor (astrological phase, command word, target's behaviour). Assigning spirits to stages (Lesser Key hierarchy, Enochian entities) is optional."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBFlowchartServitorsIFTHEN (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos builds flowcharts in which controlling servitors direct subordinate ones; here experience is said to show that no spirit need be assigned to the stages, since the analysis and the building of the flowchart suffice, and the chart may be sealed away and forgotten or fired by ritual."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, Evocation & Cybersorcery, Flowchart Design Sequence, pp. 147-149; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBNoManifestationPathwayDesireFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No manifestation pathway for the desire"@en, "Kein Manifestationsweg für den Wunsch"@de ;
    skos:definition "There is no point conjuring for something that has no pathway along which to manifest."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: conjuring for something that has no pathway along which to manifest is said to be pointless. Cause: the operator, who has not analysed the situation. No deadline and no rate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, Evocation & Cybersorcery, Flowchart Design Sequence, p. 148; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBOperationGoingWrongMayCompromiseCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Operation going wrong may compromise the operator"@en, "Fehlschlagende Operation kann den Operator kompromittieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Under Threats, consider whether a failed operation could compromise you and how to cope with fast-changing variables and new events."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBFlowchartCybersorcery ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, Evocation & Cybersorcery, Flowchart Design Sequence, p. 148; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAnalysisAloneCreatesSequence a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Analysis alone creates the sequence"@en, "Die Analyse allein erzeugt die Abfolge"@de ;
    skos:definition "Experience is said to show that ritually assigning a spirit to each stage is unnecessary; analysing and building the flowchart is enough."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, Evocation & Cybersorcery, p. 149; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBroaderPerspectiveNovelApproachesSituation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Broader perspective and novel approaches to a situation"@en, "Breitere Perspektive und neuartige Zugänge zu einer Situation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rigorous analysis of hidden variables yields a broader perspective than single-shot enchantment and tends to reveal novel keys to twisting a situation as desired."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, Evocation & Cybersorcery, p. 149; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBEnchantingPromotionWithoutOpenSlotFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Enchanting for promotion without an open slot"@en, "Für Beförderung zaubern ohne freie Stelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "After analysis Hine and a colleague judged that enchanting simply for better promotion chances would likely fail unless a slot opened; they chose to work for a co-worker's promotion first, then for the colleague to become that person's assistant. Outcome not reported."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: after analysis, enchanting simply for better chances of promotion was judged unlikely to work unless a slot in the hierarchy opened, so the work was redirected to promoting a co-worker first. Cause: the circumstances, an absence of a vacancy, not the method. No deadline and no rate; the outcome is not reported."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, Evocation & Cybersorcery, p. 149; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFlowchartSorceryYieldsBroaderPerspective a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Flowchart sorcery yields broader perspective"@en, "Flussdiagramm-Zauberei erzeugt breitere Perspektive"@de ;
    skos:definition "Flowchart analysis produces broader situational perspective and novel approaches."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBFlowchartCybersorcery ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBroaderPerspectiveNovelApproachesSituation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Evocation, Evocation & Cybersorcery, p. 149; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .



#
# Astral Magics
#
pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPopularNotionsAstralPlane a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Popular notions of the astral plane"@en, "Populäre Vorstellungen von der Astralebene"@de ;
    skos:definition "The astral is popularly where the astral body goes in dreams and OBEs, peopled by demons below and angels above, with the dead, allowing travel in time and space, or a region of imagination; explanations range from theosophical planes to scientific; Hine has stopped trying to explain it rationally."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, p. 150; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBCrowleyNoObjectiveRealityPhilosophicalCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Crowley: no objective reality or philosophical validity for astral experience"@en, "Crowley: keine objektive Realität oder philosophische Gültigkeit astraler Erfahrung"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Liber O Crowley warns against treating astral experiences as objectively real or as philosophically valid."@en ;
    skos:note "Crowley, Liber O."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPopularNotionsAstralPlane ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, p. 150; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAstralCoterminousPhysical a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Astral coterminous with physical"@en, "Astralebene deckungsgleich mit der physischen"@de ;
    skos:definition "It is believed each physical thing has an astral double and intentional actions echo there; a visualised pentagram exists on the astral, perceivable by astral entities and clairvoyants; physical ritual also operates astrally."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, p. 150; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBClairvoyantPerceptionAstralForms a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Clairvoyant perception of astral forms"@en, "Hellsichtige Wahrnehmung astraler Formen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Humans with clairvoyant talents are said to perceive astral forms such as a visualised pentagram."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, p. 150; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBVeracityProblemAstralWorkCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Veracity problem in astral work"@en, "Wahrhaftigkeitsproblem in der Astralarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Astral work ranks among the most troublesome fields, not for difficulty or danger, but because the veracity of experiences must be grappled with."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPopularNotionsAstralPlane ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, p. 150; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBShadeLMacGregorMathersNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Shade of S. L. MacGregor Mathers (as claimed contact)"@en, "Schatten von S. L. MacGregor Mathers (behaupteter Kontakt)"@de ;
    skos:definition "A woman claimed astral contact with Mathers' shade, identified by a Scottish accent and signature; Hine notes Mathers was a Hampshire man who visited Scotland once; the shade told her to study Qabalah, and Hine pointed her to Mathers' Kabbalah Unveiled."@en ;
    skos:note "unnamed woman's report to Hine. Reported to Hine by an unnamed woman: the shade, recognised by a Scottish accent and a signature, told her to learn about the Qabalah; Hine notes that Mathers came from Hampshire and visited Scotland once, and sent her to Mathers' The Kabbalah Unveiled. Entered as a naming, not a receiving, because the text does not claim its own wording from the shade."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Samuel Liddell MacGregor Mathers (shade)" ;
    pm:nameRole "Golden Dawn leader encountered as astral spirit; credentials doubted" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, pp. 150-151; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAcceptingSpiritsCredentialsFaceValueCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Accepting a spirit's credentials at face value"@en, "Die Beglaubigung eines Geistes unbesehen hinnehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the Mathers example the spirit presented credentials that were accepted uncritically; this concerns the veracity of experience, distinct from the useful process of being pointed to information."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBShadeLMacGregorMathersNaming ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, p. 151; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAstralFeedsFantasiesEgoInflatingCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Astral feeds fantasies and ego-inflating delusions"@en, "Astralebene nährt Fantasien und ego-aufblähende Wahnvorstellungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Crowley is cited that the astral's danger is offering experiences conforming to one's fantasies and ego-inflating delusions; as a feedback loop, a secret belief in one's greatness yields confirming experiences; take all astral experiences with a pinch of salt."@en ;
    skos:note "Crowley."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBPopularNotionsAstralPlane ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, p. 151; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBLookBeneathSurfaceAstralExperience a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Look beneath the surface of astral experience"@en, "Unter die Oberfläche astraler Erfahrung blicken"@de ;
    skos:definition "The astral is a metaphor for poorly understood experiences; what matters is the dynamics beneath the surface, e.g. that the Mathers contact prompted study of a new branch of magic; we co-create our astral experiences. Hine withdraws his earlier edition's Virtual Magic metaphor as not working well. A Zen master's advice to breathe deeply until a Buddha vision goes away models the helpful attitude."@en ;
    skos:note "Self-correction of first edition; Zen anecdote (traditional)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, pp. 151-152; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBMindscaping a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Mindscaping / guided journey (pathworking)"@en, "Mindscaping / geführte Reise (Pfadarbeit)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use a set of visual or oral cues to focus on a facet of experience then entered as a distinct astral space: read, hear or tape a narrative, with cues for all senses and feelings to feel present; journeys may be passive or interactive; images such as tarot cards may set the scene."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBPathworking (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos describes pathworking as a story the magician steps into until it means something personally, typed by how much narrative is given; here mindscaping is defined by a set of cues that make a facet of experience a discrete astral space, likened to a fantasy role-playing game, with passive and interactive journeys."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, Mindscaping, pp. 152-153; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBRolePlayingGamesVirtualEnclave a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Role-playing games as virtual enclave"@en, "Rollenspiele als virtuelle Enklave"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fantasy role-players transfer attention into a virtual enclave sustained by props as reference points, narrative flow and group collusion; a good session needs supportive narrative plus freedom; playing a role draws on one's own experience."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, Mindscaping, p. 153; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDiscoveringLatentRepressedCapacitiesThrough a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Discovering latent repressed capacities through roles"@en, "Latente verdrängte Fähigkeiten durch Rollen entdecken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Assuming a role outside one's repertoire can reveal unexpected capacities, often latent possibilities rejected as incompatible with self-image."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, Mindscaping, p. 153; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRolePlayingMagicalExerciseGroup a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Role-playing as magical exercise; group mythos"@en, "Rollenspiel als magische Übung; Gruppenmythos"@de ;
    skos:definition "Run a fantasy defined by the group where participants encounter facets of themselves in set situations; use the same dynamics to create a group mythos explored and modified by experience."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondCRolePlayingMythos (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos uses a role-playing game to enter a mythic universe; here the group-defined fantasy is a way for participants to meet aspects of themselves and to build a group mythos that their experiences modify."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, Mindscaping, p. 153; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBRolePlayYieldsDiscoveryLatent a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Role-play yields discovery of latent capacities"@en, "Rollenspiel erzeugt Entdeckung latenter Fähigkeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Role-play exercise produces discovery of latent capacities."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBRolePlayingMagicalExerciseGroup ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDiscoveringLatentRepressedCapacitiesThrough ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, Mindscaping, p. 153; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMindscapingYieldsInsightAnswersSpontaneity a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Mindscaping yields insight, answers, spontaneity"@en, "Mindscaping erzeugt Einsicht, Antworten, Spontaneität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Guided journeys produce card insight, divine answers, reduced anxiety and imaginative spontaneity."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBMindscaping ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBInsightTarotCardThroughJourneying, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBQuestioningDeityJourney, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBReducingAnxietyRehearsingSituations, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBImaginativeSpontaneity ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, Mindscaping, p. 153; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBInsightTarotCardThroughJourneying a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Insight into a tarot card through journeying"@en, "Einsicht in eine Tarotkarte durch Reisen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Journeying into the landscape of e.g. The Tower yields insight into the card's meaning."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, Mindscaping, p. 153; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBQuestioningDeityJourney a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Questioning a deity on a journey"@en, "Eine Gottheit auf einer Reise befragen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A journey to visit Freyja to ask a question may move one and give an answer or a perspective previously missed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, Mindscaping, pp. 153-154; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBFreyjaNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Freyja"@en, "Freyja"@de ;
    skos:definition "Goddess who can be visited on a mindscape journey and asked pertinent questions."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Freyja" ;
    pm:nameRole "goddess consulted in journeying" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, Mindscaping, p. 153; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBReducingAnxietyRehearsingSituations a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reducing anxiety by rehearsing situations"@en, "Angstminderung durch Proben von Situationen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Psychologists have socially nervous people rehearse situations in imagination beforehand to reduce stress and anxiety."@en ;
    skos:note "psychologists (general)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, Mindscaping, p. 153; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBJourneyEvokesConcordantEmotionsInsightsSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Journey evokes concordant emotions, insights, revelations"@en, "Reise ruft passende Gefühle, Einsichten, Offenbarungen hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "If effective, a journey evokes emotions, insights and even revelations concordant with the imagery's theme."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: an effective journey evokes emotions, insights and even revelations in keeping with the theme of its imagery. No deadline or rate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, Mindscaping, pp. 153-154; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBImaginativeSpontaneity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Imaginative spontaneity"@en, "Imaginative Spontaneität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mindscaping helps develop imaginative spontaneity, drawing on the mind's rapid creation of inner virtual realities."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, Mindscaping, p. 154; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBConfabulation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Confabulation"@en, "Konfabulation"@de ;
    skos:definition "A defence mechanism by which the mind quickly constructs detailed, consistent false realities under anxiety; such false memories surface under hypnosis as UFO abductions, past lives or satanic rituals."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, Mindscaping, p. 154; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBCreatingGroupAstralTemple a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating a group astral temple"@en, "Einen Gruppen-Astraltempel erschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "For three people: design a square black room having doors in W, N and S walls each bearing a member's glowing sigil, a circular black mirror in the east wall, a black chaosphere floating from the ceiling as aetheric lamp, and a floor glyph interlocking members' sigils; add sensations (smell, touch, humidity, colour, sound). Each attempts entry at agreed times and records experiences for later comparison. Aids: a group perfume first used in a trust-and-bonding ritual, then as memory enhancer; photographs of members in ritual garb; a shared mantra recorded by each and cut up so all seem to chant together. Entry: visualise the temple sigil, step through one's door seeing others enter theirs, each sends an energy bolt into the chaosphere to activate it."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBBuildingAstralTemple (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos builds a solitary astral temple from perceptual gestalts and kinesthetic memory; here a temple for three is designed with members' sigils, a black mirror and a chaosphere, entered at agreed times, with scent, photographs and cut-up mantra tapes as aids."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, A Group Astral Temple, pp. 154-155; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSharedAstralSpaceGroupMagic a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shared astral space for group magic"@en, "Geteilter Astralraum für Gruppenmagie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Members contribute to a shared dream-space where they can meet and interact non-locally for exploration and group magic."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, A Group Astral Temple, p. 154; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMasterSimpleTempleBeforeElaboratingPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Master the simple temple before elaborating"@en, "Erst den einfachen Tempel beherrschen, dann ausbauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keep the design simple until all members can easily visualise and project into it; only then add rooms, corridors and gateways to other dimensions."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBCreatingGroupAstralTemple ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBElaboratingGroupAstralTemple ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, A Group Astral Temple, p. 154; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBElaboratingGroupAstralTemple a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Elaborating the group astral temple"@en, "Den Gruppen-Astraltempel ausbauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once every member can easily visualise and project into the basic temple, extend it with more rooms, passages and exits into other dimensions, and give the space sensations of smell, touch, humidity, colour and sound."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, A Group Astral Temple, pp. 154-155; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBCommonDetailsMutualSightingsAstralSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Common details and mutual sightings in the astral temple"@en, "Gemeinsame Details und gegenseitiges Sehen im Astraltempel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Common details in members' recorded experiences count as success; initially success is agreed as each reporting entering and seeing the others there."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: common details in the members' separately recorded experiences of the temple, and at first each member reporting having entered and seen the others there. Agreed in advance by the group; no deadline or rate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, A Group Astral Temple, pp. 155-156; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBAstralTemplePracticeYieldsShared a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Astral temple practice yields shared space"@en, "Astraltempel-Praxis erzeugt geteilten Raum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Building and entering the temple produces a shared astral space."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBCreatingGroupAstralTemple ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSharedAstralSpaceGroupMagic ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, A Group Astral Temple, p. 155; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMutualSightingBeforeSignalTelepathyPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Mutual sighting before signal and telepathy tests"@en, "Gegenseitiges Sehen vor Signal- und Telepathietests"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once members reliably see each other in the temple, further conditions are set: giving a gesture signal, telepathically projecting an image or emotion."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBCommonDetailsMutualSightingsAstralSign ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBTelepathicProjectionImageEmotion ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, A Group Astral Temple, p. 155; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBTelepathicProjectionImageEmotion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Telepathic projection of image or emotion"@en, "Telepathische Übertragung von Bild oder Gefühl"@de ;
    skos:definition "Within the astral temple one member may signal others with a gesture or telepathically project an image or emotion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, A Group Astral Temple, p. 156; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBAstralTractorBeamExercise a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Astral Tractor Beam Exercise"@en, "Übung Astraler Traktorstrahl"@de ;
    skos:definition "While one member meditates passively elsewhere: 1) the others start in the temple with the chaosphere charged; 2) state intent to send power to the named person to transfer awareness there; 3) repeat the temple power-mantra projecting octarine energy into the chaosphere until it turns orange (mercurial communication); 4) visualise the target's face and chant that they be here now; 5) visualise an orange beam from the chaosphere striking and drawing the target; 6) concentrate on the door with the target's sigil, chanting their presence, till the person is seen to come through."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, A Group Astral Temple, Astral Tractor Beam Exercise, p. 156; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDrawingAnothersAwarenessAstralTemple a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Drawing another's awareness into the astral temple"@en, "Das Bewusstsein eines anderen in den Astraltempel ziehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Two members aim to draw a passively meditating third member's awareness into the temple."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, A Group Astral Temple, p. 156; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBTractorBeamYieldsDrawnMember a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tractor beam yields drawn-in member"@en, "Traktorstrahl erzeugt hereingezogenes Mitglied"@de ;
    skos:definition "The tractor-beam rite aims to bring the target's awareness into the temple."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBAstralTractorBeamExercise ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBDrawingAnothersAwarenessAstralTemple ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, A Group Astral Temple, p. 156; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBTargetSeenAppearingThroughTheirSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Target seen appearing through their doorway"@en, "Zielperson wird durch ihre Tür eintreten gesehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The chanting continues until participants perceive the person arriving via the door bearing their sigil."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the participants see the drawn-in person appear through the door bearing his sigil. Given inside the exercise; no deadline or rate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, A Group Astral Temple, Astral Tractor Beam Exercise, p. 156; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBProjectingMessengerServitorsAnotherMembers a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Projecting messenger-servitors into another member's dreams"@en, "Boten-Servitoren in die Träume eines anderen Mitglieds senden"@de ;
    skos:definition "A suggested experiment: one member uses the temple's dark mirror first to send messenger-servitors into another member's dreams, and later to project himself into the other's dreams."@en ;
    skos:note "Passage cut at unit end; continuation in next unit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, A Group Astral Temple, p. 156; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBMessengerServitorsBeforeSelfProjectionPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Messenger-servitors before self-projection into dreams"@en, "Boten-Servitoren vor Selbstprojektion in Träume"@de ;
    skos:definition "First attempt projecting messenger-servitors into another's dreams, later projecting oneself."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBProjectingMessengerServitorsAnotherMembers ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBProjectingOneselfAnotherMembersDreams ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, A Group Astral Temple, p. 156; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBProjectingOneselfAnotherMembersDreams a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Projecting oneself into another member's dreams"@en, "Sich selbst in die Träume eines anderen Mitglieds projizieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The later step of the dream experiment: a member uses the temple's dark mirror to project himself into a fellow member's dreams."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part II Dynamic Ritual, Astral Magics, A Group Astral Temple, p. 156; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Introduction
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSocialSupportCrossFertilisationResources a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Social support, cross-fertilisation and resources through group work"@en, "Soziale Unterstützung, Austausch und Ressourcen durch Gruppenarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine states that a group setting supplies social support, lets the individual share in ideas, skills and techniques he could not reach alone, and commands more space, information and materials."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Introduction, p. 158; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCCommunityWhichOnesIdeasValidated a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Community in which one's ideas are validated, tested or challenged"@en, "Gemeinschaft, in der eigene Ideen bestätigt, geprüft oder hinterfragt werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "For Hine the chief gain of group work is a sense of belonging in an accepting setting where his own magical ideas can be confirmed, tested or contested."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Introduction, p. 158; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Introduction (group interview)
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSocialSideBeforeLastingMagicalPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Social side before lasting magical work"@en, "Soziales vor dauerhafter magischer Arbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Member T holds that if a group's social side is good it can work at any time, but if it is unresolved the work will not last in the end."@en ;
    skos:note "Testimony of 'T'."@en ;
    skos:note "The speaker names only the social side and the work; they are read here onto the nodes for cohesiveness and for the performing stage."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCCohesivenessWeNess ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCPerforming ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Unless the social side of the group is sorted out, its work will not last in the end, because of all that stays unresolved."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Introduction (group interview), p. 160; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCUnmetPersonalMattersFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual feels false when members' personal matters are not met"@en, "Ritual wirkt falsch, wenn persönliche Anliegen der Mitglieder nicht aufgefangen werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Member C recalls a former group whose members came with matters that were not part of the ritual; sometimes these could be put aside or picked up at a fitting moment, but when that failed, things felt strange and false and C was uncomfortable."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: ritual feels false when members' personal matters are not met. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the operator (members whose personal concerns were neither set aside nor met)."@en ;
    skos:note "Testimony of C, a member of the friends' group Hine interviewed. Integrator addition."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Introduction (group interview), p. 161; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCControllingMemberSabotagesGroupUntilFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One controlling member sabotages the group until it ends"@en, "Ein kontrollierendes Mitglied sabotiert die Gruppe bis zur Auflösung"@de ;
    skos:definition "In a group interview, member C recalls a working group in which one person kept trying to sabotage it and control the others, so that in the end the group had to stop."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: one controlling member sabotages the group until it ends. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on another party (a group member)."@en ;
    skos:note "Testimony of 'C', a member of a friends' group interviewed by Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Introduction (group interview), p. 161; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupSubsumingIndividualsPowerlessnessCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Group subsuming individuals into powerlessness"@en, "Gruppe, die Einzelne bis zur Ohnmacht vereinnahmt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Member P warns that trouble follows when a group swallows its members so that they feel powerless and unheard."@en ;
    skos:note "Testimony of 'P'."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCCommunityWhichOnesIdeasValidated ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Introduction (group interview), p. 161; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCUnvoicedMistrustMakesEveryWorkingFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unvoiced mistrust makes every working fail"@en, "Unausgesprochenes Misstrauen lässt jede Arbeit scheitern"@de ;
    skos:definition "C reports a group where two members wanted different things and distrusted each other without ever saying so; as a result nothing worked whenever the group tried to act."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: unvoiced mistrust makes every working fail. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the operator (group members' lack of honesty)."@en ;
    skos:note "Testimony of 'C'; lack of honesty said to undermine everything."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Introduction (group interview), p. 161; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCUnclarifiedObjectivesProduceHiddenAgendasFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unclarified objectives produce hidden agendas"@en, "Ungeklärte Ziele erzeugen verdeckte Agenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "When a group does not sort out why it is together, what its aims are and what each member expects, hidden agendas arise that sabotage its work and members leave dissatisfied."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: unclarified objectives produce hidden agendas. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the operator (group)."@en ;
    skos:note "Testimony of 'C'."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Introduction (group interview), p. 162; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Introduction
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCKnowEachOtherGroupCorollary a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Know Each Other as the group corollary of Know Yourself"@en, "Kennt einander als Gruppenentsprechung zu Erkenne dich selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine argues that an effective magical group needs more than people, props and a charter: it requires attention to group dynamics, and mutual knowledge is to the group what self-knowledge is to the lone magician."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Introduction, p. 162; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupSkillsNeverFinishedTransferable a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Group skills are never finished and not transferable by rule"@en, "Gruppenkompetenz ist nie abgeschlossen und nicht schematisch übertragbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "Working in groups needs personal and interpersonal skills; Hine stresses that this learning is never complete, and a method that succeeds in one setting may fail in another."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on the limited fixity of group methods."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Introduction, p. 162; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCOccultLearningDoesConferSocialCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Occult learning does not confer social skill"@en, "Okkultes Wissen verleiht keine soziale Kompetenz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine warns that years of studying Crowley or exploring astral realms may still leave a magician poor at getting along with other people."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCKnowEachOtherGroupCorollary ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Introduction, p. 163; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, What is a Group?
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCFiveFeaturesDistinguishingGroupMere a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Five features distinguishing a group from a mere aggregate of people"@en, "Fünf Merkmale, die eine Gruppe von einer Ansammlung unterscheiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine lists interaction, shared goals, group norms, the development and recognition of roles, and cohesiveness as what marks off a group, each then explained."@en ;
    skos:note "Compiled from group psychology by Hine (pm:Systematizing)."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Prime Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, What is a Group?, p. 163; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, What is a Group?, Common Goals
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCDivergentPerceptionsCommonGoalsBreedCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Divergent perceptions of common goals breed conflict"@en, "Abweichende Wahrnehmung gemeinsamer Ziele erzeugt Konflikt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shared goals are often implicit and perceived differently; in magical groups members' own explorations, agendas, expectations and ability levels frequently clash with the group's direction."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCFiveFeaturesDistinguishingGroupMere ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, What is a Group?, Common Goals, pp. 163-164; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, What is a Group?, Norms
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupNorms a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Group norms"@en, "Gruppennormen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Norms are the mostly implicit, slowly arising rules about proper conduct in a group; an act's meaning derives from its significance to the group, and norms often surface only when someone is felt to have broken them."@en ;
    skos:note "Illustrated by factory production-quota studies."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, What is a Group?, Norms, p. 165; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, What is a Group?, Roles
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCFormalInformalGroupRolesAssigned a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Formal and informal group roles; assigned versus real leader"@en, "Formelle und informelle Gruppenrollen; ernannter und tatsächlicher Leiter"@de ;
    skos:definition "Roles may be formally assigned, as with IOT Pact temple offices (Magister Templi, Archivist, Insubordinate), but most are assumed through interaction; the assigned leader may differ from the real one, and different people may fill task and maintenance leadership."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, What is a Group?, Roles, p. 165; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, What is a Group?, Cohesiveness
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCCohesivenessWeNess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cohesiveness ('we-ness')"@en, "Kohäsion ('Wir-Gefühl')"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shared experience binds members into a 'we'; Hine calls cohesiveness the key to group effectiveness and says it correlates positively with how intensely members interact."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, What is a Group?, Cohesiveness, p. 166; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupShattersWhenTensionsRaisedFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Group shatters when tensions are not raised"@en, "Gruppe zerbricht, wenn Spannungen nicht angesprochen werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "When members avoid bringing up problems, conflicts are nursed by individuals or cliques until they cannot be resolved; members then leave or the group is rendered ineffective, often with back-biting and scapegoating of the group."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: group shatters when tensions are not raised. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the operator (members)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, What is a Group?, Cohesiveness, p. 166; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSafetySelfExplorationCandidCritique a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Safety for self-exploration and candid critique within a cohesive group"@en, "Sicherheit für Selbsterkundung und offene Kritik in einer kohäsiven Gruppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Strong cohesion lets members explore avoided areas, disclose how magic affects them at a deep personal level, take interpersonal risks and criticise techniques or beliefs without it being taken as a slight."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, What is a Group?, Cohesiveness, pp. 166-167; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCInitiationsCelebrationsFosterGroupCohesion a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Initiations and celebrations to foster group cohesion"@en, "Initiationen und Feiern zur Förderung der Gruppenkohäsion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Groups hold initiations as rites of passage or demonstrations of commitment, and celebrate members' births, marriages, deaths and seasonal turning points, so the group shares and honours each person's life outside it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, What is a Group?, Cohesiveness, p. 167; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCCohesionRitesYieldGroupCohesion a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Cohesion rites yield group cohesion"@en, "Kohäsionsriten bewirken Gruppenkohäsion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Initiations and celebrations are said to promote cohesion and the sense of 'we-ness', which in turn makes self-disclosure and critique safe."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCInitiationsCelebrationsFosterGroupCohesion ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSafetySelfExplorationCandidCritique ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, What is a Group?, Cohesiveness, p. 167; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, What is a Magical Group?
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCMagicalGroupPrimaryGroup a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical group as primary group"@en, "Magische Gruppe als Primärgruppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine treats magical groups as primary groups in Cooley's sense, defined by direct face-to-face interaction and psychological unity, because magic requires deep self-exploration and disclosure among members."@en ;
    skos:note "Concept from Charles Cooley (date given as 1965 in text)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, What is a Magical Group?, p. 167; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, The Importance of Self-Disclosure
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAppropriateSelfDisclosureHereNow a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Appropriate self-disclosure: here-and-now, 'story' not 'history'"@en, "Angemessene Selbstoffenbarung: Hier und Jetzt, 'Geschichte' statt 'Historie'"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following social psychologists, Hine says fitting disclosure reacts to what happens in the group now and reveals the present self; 'history' lists facts while hiding the self, 'story' invites dialogue."@en ;
    skos:note "Social psychologists, unnamed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, The Importance of Self-Disclosure, p. 168; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGoodRelationshipsBeforeDeepSelfPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Good relationships before deep self-disclosure"@en, "Gute Beziehungen vor tiefer Selbstoffenbarung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Self-disclosure can only happen once good interpersonal relations exist; since these form gradually, disclosure must also be gradual, and in turn strengthens the relationships."@en ;
    skos:note "Stated as a \"can only\"; no consequence of skipping is named beyond that such disclosure does not take place."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCCohesivenessWeNess ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAppropriateSelfDisclosureHereNow ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, The Importance of Self-Disclosure, p. 168; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCPrematureExcessiveSelfDisclosureCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Premature or excessive self-disclosure"@en, "Verfrühte oder übermäßige Selbstoffenbarung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Too rapid or too much disclosure, like too little, may signal disturbance or exhibitionism; one person's story can set off point-scoring anecdotes until discussion degenerates."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAppropriateSelfDisclosureHereNow ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, The Importance of Self-Disclosure, pp. 168-169; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCMagicalGroupTherapyGroupCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A magical group is no therapy group"@en, "Magische Gruppen sind keine Therapiegruppen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some treat the group as a sounding-board for their own problems instead of contributing; leaders must judge whether disclosure suits the group, while recognising that magic does touch members deeply."@en ;
    skos:note "Remark of an unnamed colleague, endorsed by Hine."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAppropriateSelfDisclosureHereNow ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, The Importance of Self-Disclosure, p. 169; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSelfDisclosureNecessarySelfKnowledgePrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-disclosure necessary for self-knowledge"@en, "Selbstoffenbarung als Bedingung der Selbsterkenntnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine states that self-knowledge needs self-disclosure: those who never reveal themselves lack self-awareness and the feedback for change."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAppropriateSelfDisclosureHereNow ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSelfKnowledgeRealityTestingThrough ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Lack of self-awareness and of feedback for behavioural change."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, The Importance of Self-Disclosure, p. 169; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSelfKnowledgeRealityTestingThrough a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-knowledge and reality testing through self-disclosure"@en, "Selbsterkenntnis und Realitätsprüfung durch Selbstoffenbarung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Disclosing oneself gives valid feedback and reality testing, allows feelings into consciousness to be owned, and supplies the feedback needed for chosen change in attitude, belief or behaviour."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, The Importance of Self-Disclosure, pp. 169-170; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCTestingOnesMagicalWorldView a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Testing one's magical world-view against others in a group"@en, "Realitätsprüfung des eigenen magischen Weltbilds in der Gruppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "A group lets members confront their magical experiences and beliefs with others', which Hine calls an unparalleled chance to test one's magical world-view and know oneself better."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, The Importance of Self-Disclosure, p. 170; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSolitaryMagiciansMagusItisCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Solitary magicians and 'Magus-itis'"@en, "Einzelmagier und 'Magus-itis'"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magicians working entirely alone often fall prey to obsessional fantasies of superiority, believing themselves one ritual from adepthood; continual invocation of a deity that boosts one self over others breeds obsessions that a group would point out."@en ;
    skos:note "Refers to Hine's Condensed Chaos for Magus-itis."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondAMagusItisCautela (Condensed Chaos, 1995): there Magus-itis is described as a syndrome of the self-exalted magician; here Hine names solitary work as its breeding ground and the group as the place where it is pointed out."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCTestingOnesMagicalWorldView ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, The Importance of Self-Disclosure, p. 170; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCMagicalDevelopmentDemandsBehaviouralChange a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical development demands behavioural change"@en, "Magische Entwicklung verlangt Verhaltensänderung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magical development as commonly understood implies and requires behavioural change resulting from practice, which is why feedback in groups matters."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, The Importance of Self-Disclosure, p. 170; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupProblemsRecurResolutionNever a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Group problems recur; resolution is never final"@en, "Gruppenprobleme kehren wieder; keine Lösung ist endgültig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine calls it a common fallacy that a resolved conflict will not return; effective groups accept recurrence and work through issues each time more deeply."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development, pp. 170-171; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCTuckmansStagesGroupDevelopment a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Tuckman's stages of group development"@en, "Tuckmans Phasen der Gruppenentwicklung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Forming, Storming, Norming, Performing, proposed by Bruce Tuckman after a review of group research and adopted by Hine as a guide for magical groups."@en ;
    skos:note "Bruce Tuckman. No consequence of skipping named; Hine notes groups cycle and overlap stages."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCForming ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCStorming ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCNorming ;
    rdf:_4 pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCPerforming ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Tuckman's stages, as Hine adopts them, run forming, storming, norming and performing; each stage takes its sense from its place, since the conflicts over authority and intimacy that mark storming must be resolved before norms and roles emerge in norming, and only then does the group turn wholly to its task in performing. Hine adds that no group passes cleanly between stages and that groups cycle back through them." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development, pp. 170-171; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development, Forming
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCForming a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forming"@en, "Formierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "First stage: members join with varied, partly unconscious motives (confirmation, belonging, enjoyment, achievement), feel uncertain and need acceptance, and keep to formal polite interaction."@en ;
    skos:note "Bruce Tuckman's model."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development, Forming, pp. 171-172; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCNonDirectiveLeadershipHeightensFormingCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Non-directive leadership heightens forming anxiety"@en, "Nicht-direktive Leitung verstärkt Anfangsangst"@de ;
    skos:definition "New members' anxiety is likely to rise if the group lacks direction because the leader takes a non-directive role."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCForming ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development, Forming, p. 171; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCDeepSelfDisclosureDuringFormingCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Deep self-disclosure during forming"@en, "Tiefe Selbstoffenbarung in der Formierungsphase"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deep disclosure is not expected at the forming stage and may frighten others who do not yet feel settled enough to reciprocate."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCForming ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development, Forming, p. 172; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development, Storming
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCStorming a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Storming"@en, "Konfliktphase (Storming)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Members drop politeness, feel vulnerable, discover likes and dislikes and differences; tension between individual and group and hostility to the leader arise, worse when structure is lacking; polarisation may follow."@en ;
    skos:note "Bruce Tuckman's model."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development, Storming, p. 172; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development, Norming
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCNorming a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Norming"@en, "Normierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once authority and intimacy issues settle, members accept each other, norms of tolerance and openness emerge, informal roles are identified and the leader is seen as an equal; cohesion is still fragile and harmony may be kept at all costs."@en ;
    skos:note "Bruce Tuckman's model."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development, Norming, p. 173; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development, Performing
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCPerforming a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Performing"@en, "Leistungsphase (Performing)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The group is oriented to its task, members take roles that serve its activities, accept differences, and can confront and challenge one another positively in mutual respect."@en ;
    skos:note "Bruce Tuckman's model."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development, Performing, p. 173; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCStageModelGuideFixedSequence a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Stage model is a guide, not a fixed sequence"@en, "Phasenmodell als Leitfaden, nicht feste Abfolge"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine says no group shows clean transitions; groups recycle stages with new members or outside changes, and forming and performing coexist in varying proportion; the model's value is as guidance for leaders."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how fixed the model is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development, p. 174; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCInexperiencedLeadersDefensiveReactionEscalatesFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inexperienced leader's defensive reaction escalates conflict"@en, "Defensive Reaktion unerfahrener Leiter verschärft Konflikt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Leaders who take hostility personally and respond by turning non-directive or authoritarian tend to raise tension, causing emotional explosions that damage the group's move toward cohesion."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: inexperienced leader's defensive reaction escalates conflict. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the operator (leader)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development, p. 174; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCIllusionHarmonyExpenseUnderlyingConflictCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Illusion of harmony at the expense of underlying conflict"@en, "Harmonie-Illusion auf Kosten verdeckter Konflikte"@de ;
    skos:definition "If tensions are not acknowledged, they move into cliques, resentments are nursed until shown aggressively or the member leaves, members feel unheard, and those who raise issues get scapegoated."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCNorming ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Stages of Group Development, p. 174; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, The Group and the External Environment
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupExternalEnvironment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Group and external environment"@en, "Gruppe und äußeres Umfeld"@de ;
    skos:definition "Groups are shaped by setting (village or city), by a parent organisation, by their own history, which can harden into rigid tradition, and by members' cross-membership and priorities among groups."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, The Group and the External Environment, p. 174; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCRigidGroupTraditionCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Group tradition hardening into a rigid norm"@en, "Gruppentradition, die zur starren Norm erstarrt"@de ;
    skos:definition "What a group takes to be its tradition can become a rigid norm that blocks adaptation and flexibility, voiced as the view that things have always been done one way."@en ;
    skos:note "Integrator addition."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupExternalEnvironment ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, The Group and the External Environment, p. 175; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCDemandingMembersPutOnesGroupFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Demanding members put one's group first backfires"@en, "Forderung, die eigene Gruppe vorzuziehen, schlägt fehl"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine has seen a leader insist that members prioritise his group; one member promptly reduced his memberships by leaving that very group."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: demanding members put one's group first backfires. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the operator (leader)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, The Group and the External Environment, p. 175; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Glamour Projection
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGlamourProjection a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Glamour projection"@en, "Glamour-Projektion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Groups project an image through symbols (the Chaosphere versus inverted pentagram and goat's head), dress, codes and secret signs, with tension between wide projection and the glamour turning into a fashion detached from the group."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Glamour Projection, p. 175; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Perceptions of Magic
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCTightLooseConsensualBeliefSystems a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tight and loose consensual belief systems"@en, "Enge und lose konsensuelle Glaubenssysteme"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine distinguishes tight systems where all share one belief system (e.g. a Wiccan group) from loose ones like Chaos Magic groups agreeing on few principles; convergent belief aids cohesion, divergent belief demands more explaining and risk."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Perceptions of Magic, p. 176; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, The Challenge of Change
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCBeliefChangeThroughProgressStrainsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Belief change through progress strains the group"@en, "Glaubenswandel durch Fortschritt belastet die Gruppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "As members progress, their beliefs shift gradually or suddenly through revelations, illuminations or initiatory crises such as the 'Dark Night' of St John; this causes conflict, especially in tight-belief groups holding tradition inviolate, and is behind the phrase 'magical differences' for departures."@en ;
    skos:note "'Dark Night of the Soul' attributed to St. John of the Cross."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCTightLooseConsensualBeliefSystems ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, The Challenge of Change, pp. 176-178; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Conflicting Values
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAssumingSharedValuesSorceryProposalsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Assuming shared values in sorcery proposals"@en, "Annahme geteilter Werte bei Zaubereivorschlägen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Members often assume all share their values, e.g. when proposing a healing or cursing working; when challenged, proposers feel slighted and challengers uncomfortable, worse under time pressure, so members may go along with what they dislike."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupSupportedWorking ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Conflicting Values, p. 178; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupSupportedWorking a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Group-supported working proposed by a member (healing or cursing)"@en, "Von einem Mitglied vorgeschlagene, von der Gruppe getragene Arbeit (Heilung oder Fluch)"@de ;
    skos:definition "A member requests the group's backing for a working of his choosing, such as a healing or a cursing operation; Hine says such a request usually implies that the working matters greatly to him."@en ;
    skos:note "Only the working is named; no steps are given. Integrator addition, as the step that the prior discussion of values serves."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Conflicting Values, pp. 178-179; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCBeliefGroupWorkingsOutweighSolo a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Belief that group workings outweigh solo workings"@en, "Glaube, Gruppenarbeiten seien wirksamer als Einzelarbeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine notes as a consensual belief, often treated as fact, that group magic is more powerful than solo magic; because of it, requests for group support imply importance and challenges are taken personally, and 'we all feel' phrases are used to block challenge."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine marks the belief as consensual, not established."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Conflicting Values, pp. 178-179; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCReassuringChallengedMembers a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Reassuring members whose idea is challenged"@en, "Mitglieder beruhigen, deren Idee in Frage gestellt wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since a challenge to a proposed working tests the we-ness the group takes for granted, it needs careful handling: members are reassured that questioning a single idea of theirs does not call into question all they have given the group."@en ;
    skos:note "Integrator addition."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Conflicting Values, p. 178; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCEarlyAiringRotatingExplorationMembers a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Early airing and rotating exploration of members' interests"@en, "Frühe Offenlegung und reihum Erkundung der Interessen der Mitglieder"@de ;
    skos:definition "The leader points out divergent beliefs and interests early and invites discussion; the group spends a period exploring each interest area in turn, each member (with help if needed) leading a session on his own field; values are discussed before related magical work, and the group agrees each may opt out of activities found repugnant."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Conflicting Values, p. 179; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCMutualAppreciationMembersMagicalBackgrounds a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mutual appreciation of members' magical backgrounds and group direction"@en, "Gegenseitiges Verständnis der magischen Hintergründe und der Gruppenrichtung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Members learn each other's magical backgrounds, where each is coming from, and in which directions the group can move."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Conflicting Values, p. 179; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCRotatingInterestSessionsYieldMutual a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Rotating interest sessions yield mutual understanding"@en, "Reihum geführte Interessensitzungen bewirken gegenseitiges Verständnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Exploring each member's interest area in turn is said to give members an appreciation of one another's backgrounds and of possible group directions, provided each is willing to lead a session."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCEarlyAiringRotatingExplorationMembers ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCMutualAppreciationMembersMagicalBackgrounds ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Conflicting Values, p. 179; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCDiscussValuesBeforeValueLadenPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Discuss values before value-laden magical work"@en, "Werte besprechen vor wertbezogener magischer Arbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine recommends that members discuss personal and shared values before engaging in magical work that touches those values."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine calls it useful; no consequence of skipping is named."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCEarlyAiringRotatingExplorationMembers ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupSupportedWorking ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Conflicting Values, p. 179; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCAgreeingEachMembersRightOpt a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Agreeing each member's right to opt out"@en, "Vereinbarung des Rechts jedes Mitglieds auf Nichtteilnahme"@de ;
    skos:definition "The group discusses and adopts a general principle: members are encouraged to support group work, but each may decline any rite or event they find objectionable for reasons of taste, ethics or personal liking, and may say so without feeling they are failing the group or causing trouble."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine presents it as useful alongside prior discussion of values (cf. A3-0051, A3-0046)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Conflicting Values, p. 179; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Contribution to the Group Process/Task
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCOverContributorsExpectingStatusCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Over-contributors expecting status"@en, "Übermäßig Beitragende, die Status erwarten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Members who put in much effort may expect unrealistic appreciation and higher status, become defensive when challenged, and threaten to withdraw while citing past contributions."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCRationalTaskAllocationRotationSeasonal ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Contribution to the Group Process/Task, p. 179; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSelfInitiatedProjectsTangibleContributionFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-initiated projects and tangible-contribution grievances drive members out"@en, "Eigeninitiierte Projekte und Groll über sichtbare Beiträge treiben Mitglieder hinaus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Members who start extra projects (newsletter, archive, props) may discount intangible roles and hold the group at fault for withholding support; such conflict can end in the aggrieved leaving, hard to resolve unless they examine their own motives and drop claims to extra status."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: self-initiated projects and tangible-contribution grievances drive members out. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the operator (aggrieved member)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Contribution to the Group Process/Task, p. 180; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSameFewMembersCarryingAllCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Same few members carrying all the work"@en, "Dieselben wenigen Mitglieder tragen alle Arbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the main contributions always come from the same people they soon tire of supporting the rest, which is unsatisfying for all unless a magician wants mere followers; tasks given out of liking or kept as one person's property also harm the group."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCRationalTaskAllocationRotationSeasonal ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Contribution to the Group Process/Task, p. 181; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCRationalTaskAllocationRotationSeasonal a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Rational task allocation with rotation (seasonal celebration example)"@en, "Rationale Aufgabenverteilung mit Rotation (Beispiel Jahreskreisfest)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Allocate tasks by ability, interest and responsibility; e.g. split a seasonal celebration into finding a site, transport and routes, incense and lighting, props, choosing people for ritual roles, and writing and distributing the ritual format; assign each to a member and rotate them at successive events so everyone learns each task."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Contribution to the Group Process/Task, p. 181; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCTaskRotationYieldsCohesionCommitment a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Task rotation yields cohesion and commitment"@en, "Aufgabenrotation bewirkt Kohäsion und Verbindlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rotating tasks is said to promote cohesiveness and commitment and help friendships form."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCRationalTaskAllocationRotationSeasonal ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCCommitmentFriendshipsBeyondMeeting, pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCCohesivenessWeNess ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Contribution to the Group Process/Task, p. 181; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCCommitmentFriendshipsBeyondMeeting a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Commitment and friendships beyond the meeting"@en, "Verbindlichkeit und Freundschaften über das Treffen hinaus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Members who feel essential to the group's success show more commitment to meetings, and friendships form that extend beyond the meeting place."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Contribution to the Group Process/Task, p. 181; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCFormalOnlyContactHindersIntimacy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Formal-only contact hinders intimacy in group experience"@en, "Nur formeller Kontakt erschwert Nähe in der Gruppenerfahrung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine has found that members who limit contact with others to formal meetings find it harder to take part in the group's more intimate experiences."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Contribution to the Group Process/Task, p. 182; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Challenges to Authority
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCUnverifiableSpiritualAuthorityStarSyndromeCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Unverifiable 'spiritual' authority and the Star Syndrome"@en, "Unüberprüfbare 'spirituelle' Autorität und das Star-Syndrom"@de ;
    skos:definition "Authority may rest on experience, on notoriety or books (Star Syndrome), or on claimed spiritual initiation; the latter is rarely open to inspection, so charismatic people can claim moral superiority and would-be gurus have fooled people for long periods."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAuthorityTwoWayProcess ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Challenges to Authority, p. 182; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAgainstInitiationBasedAuthorityGolden a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against initiation-based authority of Golden Dawn leaders"@en, "Gegen initiationsbegründete Autorität von Golden-Dawn-Leitern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine cites some Golden Dawn leaders and their many imitators as examples of claiming superiority from a higher initiation that cannot be inspected."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the opposing view is reported by him, not quoted from a named work."@en ;
    skos:note "Named tradition: Hermetic Order of the Golden Dawn and imitators."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Challenges to Authority, p. 182; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGodYourSideBreedsAbsolutismCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "'God on your side' breeds absolutism and paranoia"@en, "'Gott auf seiner Seite' erzeugt Absolutismus und Paranoia"@de ;
    skos:definition "Claiming divine mandate tends toward absolutism, and Hine calls paranoia an inevitable result, since any criticism seems to question the authenticity of one's initiation."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAuthorityTwoWayProcess ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Challenges to Authority, p. 182; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAuthorityConflictsEndSchismMagicalFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Authority conflicts end in schism and magical warfare"@en, "Autoritätskonflikte enden in Spaltung und magischem Krieg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Challenges to authorities polarise groups into followers and heretics, leading to departures or schism; ex-members become enemies, bonding the rest in paranoia, followed by psychic attack, magical battles and sniping in the occult press, while internal contradictions are ignored."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: authority conflicts end in schism and magical warfare. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the operator (authority figures and members)."@en ;
    skos:note "Studies of religious cults cited for group resilience of shared belief."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Challenges to Authority, p. 183; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAuthorityTwoWayProcess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Authority as a two-way process"@en, "Autorität als wechselseitiger Prozess"@de ;
    skos:definition "Authority depends as much on members' perception of authority figures as on the self-presentation of those seeking authority."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Challenges to Authority, p. 183; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Transgression of Group Norms
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCUnwittingTransgressionImplicitNormsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Unwitting transgression of implicit norms"@en, "Unbeabsichtigte Verletzung impliziter Normen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine has met people censured for giggling in an invocation or smoking after a meditation; in a magical context such acts get read as disrespect to the Goddess or desecration of the circle, and the offender is often just frozen out."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupNorms ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Transgression of Group Norms, p. 183; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Sexuality in Groups
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSexualExploitationNewMembersUnderCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Sexual exploitation of new members under magical pretext"@en, "Sexuelle Ausbeutung neuer Mitglieder unter magischem Vorwand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some leaders treat newcomers as sexual prospects, offering an immediate higher initiation involving sacred intercourse with the leader or claims of past-life soulmates; sexual conduct is justified as magical so normal feelings supposedly should not apply."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCInitiationsCelebrationsFosterGroupCohesion ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Sexuality in Groups, p. 184; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCPersonalFeelingsPersistInsideCircleCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Personal feelings persist inside the circle"@en, "Persönliche Gefühle bestehen im Kreis fort"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sexual exchanges among members will not go unnoticed, and feelings, fears and inhibitions do not vanish when the circle is cast or temple door shut; what matters is how individuals and group handle them."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupSexualGnosisBoundedSettings ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Sexuality in Groups, p. 184; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupSexualGnosisBoundedSettings a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Group sexual gnosis in bounded settings"@en, "Sexuelle Gnosis in der Gruppe in abgegrenztem Rahmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Group sexual gnosis is used within well-defined spaces and at times when normality is suspended, with careful group management before, during and after, and only among participants who feel emotionally secure and trusting."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Sexuality in Groups, p. 184; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCEcstasyDeConditioningThroughGroup a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ecstasy and (de)conditioning through group sexual gnosis"@en, "Ekstase und (De-)Konditionierung durch sexuelle Gnosis in der Gruppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sex offers a strong path into ecstasy; group sexual gnosis can act as a strong conditioner but also as a strong deconditioner."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Sexuality in Groups, p. 185; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupSexualGnosisYieldsEcstasy a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Group sexual gnosis yields ecstasy and deconditioning"@en, "Sexuelle Gnosis in der Gruppe bewirkt Ekstase und Dekonditionierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bounded group sexual gnosis is presented as a route to ecstasy that may condition or decondition."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupSexualGnosisBoundedSettings ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCEcstasyDeConditioningThroughGroup ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Sexuality in Groups, p. 185; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSexualGnosisMindControlGroupsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Sexual gnosis in mind-control groups; sex-only focus"@en, "Sexuelle Gnosis in Psychokontrollgruppen; reine Sexfixierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sexual gnosis features in mind-control groups as a conditioner, and a group whose behaviour centres entirely on sex tends to lose wider impetus."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupSexualGnosisBoundedSettings ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Sexuality in Groups, p. 185; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCTrustManagementRequiredGroupSexualPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Trust and management required for group sexual gnosis"@en, "Vertrauen und Leitung als Bedingung sexueller Gnosis in der Gruppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Successful use needs careful management before, during and after, and participants must, without exception, feel emotionally safe and trust each other highly."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSafetySelfExplorationCandidCritique ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupSexualGnosisBoundedSettings ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without careful management before, during and after, and without secure mutual trust, the practice is not used successfully; the bounded settings are said to serve to head off conflict and fallout afterwards."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Issues Specific to Magical Groups, Sexuality in Groups, p. 185; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCExamineOnesMotivesBeforeRunningPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Examine one's motives before running a group"@en, "Eigene Motive prüfen, bevor man eine Gruppe leitet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before practical matters Hine puts first the examination of one's own motivation to set up a group."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine names the look at one's own motives as the first thing before practical matters; no consequence of skipping is named. The prior step is read onto the self-assessment practice of Condensed Chaos."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondASelfAssessment ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCDefiningClearSimpleAimsNew ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, p. 185; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCTransferableOrganisationalPeopleSkillsRunning a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Transferable organisational and people skills from running groups"@en, "Übertragbare Organisations- und Personalkompetenz durch Gruppenleitung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Running a group builds a name as an effective organiser and develops organisation, promotion and people-management skills transferable to other life areas; it teaches about oneself, others, group dynamics, management and shared magical experience."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, pp. 185-186; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCImpetusPractiseThroughRunningGroup a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Impetus to practise through running a group"@en, "Antrieb zur Praxis durch Gruppenleitung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine says a main reason he runs groups is that it pushes him to do things he would otherwise not make time for."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, p. 186; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCTeachingBecomesBoringWhenOnlyFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Teaching becomes boring when only the teacher speaks"@en, "Lehren wird langweilig, wenn nur der Lehrer spricht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Teaching magic is boring if one is the only person voicing opinions; it rewards only with lively students who experiment past dogma."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: teaching becomes boring when only the teacher speaks. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on another party (students' passivity)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, p. 187; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCDeeperGraspOnesMaterialThrough a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Deeper grasp of one's own material through teaching"@en, "Vertieftes Verständnis des eigenen Stoffs durch Lehren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Teaching forces revision and, through preparing material in several formats, reveals unnoticed aspects; successful transmission shows confidence, communication and self-organisation, and trains turning feelings into words."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, p. 187; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Aims & Objectives
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCDefiningClearSimpleAimsNew a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Defining clear and simple aims for a new group"@en, "Klare, einfache Ziele für eine neue Gruppe festlegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before starting, define aims and objectives like a Statement of Intent, keep them clear and simple and open to change, and avoid lengthy charters."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Aims & Objectives, p. 187; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCOverElaborateChartersCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Over-elaborate charters"@en, "Überladene Satzungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Huge charters leave members no room to contribute and set the founder up for disappointment, since fixed ideas invite disagreement; vagueness, conversely, looks bad."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCDefiningClearSimpleAimsNew ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Aims & Objectives, p. 187; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Spreading The Word / Points of Contact
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCPublicisingGroupSettingUpContact a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Publicising a group and setting up contact points"@en, "Eine Gruppe bekanntmachen und Kontaktstellen einrichten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spread word by mouth, shop cards, posters, magazine listings or local adverts suited to the target audience; avoid giving home address, think before giving a phone number, prefer a box number (Post Office or British Monomarks) or personal referral."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Spreading The Word / Points of Contact, p. 188; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Points of Contact
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCPrivacyDrawbacksContactMethodsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Privacy drawbacks of contact methods"@en, "Datenschutznachteile von Kontaktwegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Phone numbers are unwise in shared housing; a Post Office box is tied to the nearest sorting office, has tariffs, discloses the holder to official enquiries and may require ID at collection."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCPublicisingGroupSettingUpContact ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Points of Contact, p. 189; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Finding A Venue / Booking Rooms
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCFindingBookingVenue a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding and booking a venue"@en, "Einen Raum finden und buchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Match venue to group type: pub rooms for socials and forums (cultivate the landlord), community or adult education centres, drama or dance studios, rehearsal studios, therapy spaces or outdoors; pay deposits, view the space first, give notice of cancellation and stay on good terms with management."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Finding A Venue / Booking Rooms, p. 189; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Finding A Venue
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCFireAlarmShattersPathworkingSessionFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fire alarm shatters a pathworking session"@en, "Feueralarm zerstört eine Pfadarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "At a centre Hine used, a fire alarm rung shortly before closing once broke the built-up calm of a pathworking session."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: fire alarm shatters a pathworking session. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on chance (venue)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Finding A Venue, p. 190; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCUnsuitableVenuesRehearsalStudiosTherapyCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Unsuitable venues: rehearsal studios and therapy spaces"@en, "Ungeeignete Räume: Proberäume und Therapieräume"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rehearsal studios bring fixed hour-blocks, noise from neighbouring bands and next bookings barging in; therapy spaces are costly and their New Age operators may object to demon summoning."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCFindingBookingVenue ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Finding A Venue, p. 190; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Finding A Venue, Outdoors
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCPlanningOutdoorRitualWork a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Planning outdoor ritual work"@en, "Planung von Ritualarbeit im Freien"@de ;
    skos:definition "Secure privacy from sight and sound, plan travel there and back in the dark, consider weather, gather and hide firewood by day, tidy the site afterwards, and clear a working space."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Finding A Venue, Outdoors, p. 191; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCDrivingHomeWhileStillGnosisCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Driving home while still in gnosis"@en, "Heimfahrt im noch gnostischen Zustand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine has found that whoever drives the group home after a rite usually suffers for it, especially if still somewhat in gnosis; leaving the site untidy also risks lurid press reports."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCPlanningOutdoorRitualWork ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Finding A Venue, Outdoors, p. 191; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCPortableOilDrumFireplace a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Portable oil-drum fireplace"@en, "Tragbare Ölfass-Feuerstelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cut an oil drum in half and make four holes; carry it to the site for the fire, then extinguish it, pass two poles through the holes, immerse the drum in water and carry it home."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Finding A Venue, Outdoors, p. 191; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Nom de Plumes
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCCoverNamesHiredMeetings a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Cover names for hired meetings"@en, "Decknamen für angemietete Treffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When hiring a venue, use a cover name: social forums often use 'Folklore', working groups names with 'Experimental Drama' (e.g. Isle of Thanet Drama Group)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Nom de Plumes, p. 191; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCCoverNameFailsUnlessAllFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cover name fails unless all members know it"@en, "Deckname versagt, wenn ihn nicht alle kennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The cover name only works if every member knows it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure of pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCCoverNamesHiredMeetings: cover name fails unless all members know it. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the operator (group)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Nom de Plumes, p. 192; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, People Management
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCLooseManagementOpenForum a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Loose management of an open social forum"@en, "Lockere Führung eines offenen geselligen Forums"@de ;
    skos:definition "A social forum open to anyone, attended to meet others, may need only light management of the setting, such as the organiser introducing people to one another at the first few meetings."@en ;
    skos:note "Integrator addition."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, People Management, p. 192; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Leadership
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupsNeedLeadersDespitePagan a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Groups need leaders despite Pagan aversion"@en, "Gruppen brauchen Leitung trotz heidnischer Abneigung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Though Pagan and occult circles dislike leaders and prefer terms like facilitator, someone must initiate decisions and see things done, more so in larger groups; a founder is responsible for the group's development and seen as such."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Leadership, p. 192; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAgainstStructurelessConsensusGroup a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the 'structureless' consensus group"@en, "Gegen die 'strukturlose' Konsensgruppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine rejects critics of hierarchical grade systems who offer the leaderless consensus group as remedy: any group meeting over time structures itself, and an unspoken informal structure may invite more abuse than an open hierarchy."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the opposing view is reported by him, not quoted from a named work."@en ;
    skos:note "Disputed position: advocates of structureless/consensus groups (unnamed)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Leadership, pp. 192-193; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCHiddenHierarchiesConnectionsOverRank a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hidden hierarchies; connections over rank"@en, "Verborgene Hierarchien; die richtigen Leute kennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Groups are more than their overt structure: loose networks grow hidden status hierarchies and hierarchies act like networks; Hine finds that knowing the right people matters more than formal rank, and structures change as members move."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Leadership, p. 193; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCUnaccountableCharismaticLeadersCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Unaccountable charismatic leaders"@en, "Nicht rechenschaftspflichtige charismatische Leiter"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magical groups and orders run into trouble when charismatic leaders' influence is not balanced by accountability; members ought to be free to critique the leader without it collapsing into schism."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupsNeedLeadersDespitePagan ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Leadership, p. 193; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGoodMagicianDoesMeanGood a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Good magician does not mean good leader; leadership is learnt live"@en, "Guter Magier heißt nicht guter Leiter; Leitung wird im Vollzug gelernt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine endorses Antero Alli's observation that occultists assume a good magician will be a good leader, implying both are born; research does not support this, and leadership can only be learnt in practice, aided by watching leaders and reading leadership theory."@en ;
    skos:note "Antero Alli."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Leadership, p. 193; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCLeadershipContextualGrantedGroup a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Leadership is contextual and granted by the group"@en, "Leitung ist kontextabhängig und von der Gruppe verliehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The leader role applies only in particular contexts (formal proceedings, not socials); a title alone does not make someone regarded as leader, since the group gives permission to lead."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Leadership, p. 194; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCLeaderPushingSetProgrammeAgainstFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Leader pushing a set programme against group signals"@en, "Leiter zieht festes Programm gegen Gruppensignale durch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Leaders who keep working through a planned series of rituals while overlooking signs it no longer fits lose members' support; imposing will only works while members collude."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: leader pushing a set programme against group signals. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the operator (leader)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Leadership, p. 194; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCReadingGroupMood a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Reading group mood"@en, "Gruppenstimmung lesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rather than asking directly, the leader observes body language and how people say things, distinguishing enthusiastic assent from mere going along, to judge when to keep to the task and when to switch."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Leadership, p. 194; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCLeaderJudgedAgainstInfallibleAdeptCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Leader judged against an infallible-adept standard"@en, "Leiter am Maßstab des unfehlbaren Adepten gemessen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A magical-group leader must be seen as a good magician; if members imagine adepts as wise infallible superhumans, the leader's inevitable errors look like grave transgressions; the leader also draws projections about authority and parents."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCLeadershipContextualGrantedGroup ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Leadership, p. 195; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCDenyingDeFactoLeadershipCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Denying de facto leadership"@en, "Faktische Leitungsrolle leugnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine finds that those who most deny being leaders are still seen as such on account of age, experience or sociability; ignoring this harms the group as much as clutching at leadership."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGroupsNeedLeadersDespitePagan ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Leadership, p. 195; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, The Three Circles Model
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCThreeCirclesModelGroupNeeds a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three Circles Model of group needs"@en, "Drei-Kreise-Modell der Gruppenbedürfnisse"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine presents a diagram of three interdependent areas of need, task, group maintenance and individual; the leader's job is to achieve the task, build and maintain the team, and respect and develop individuals, which requires awareness, understanding of what is needed, and skill to act."@en ;
    skos:note "Model presented without attribution (pm:Systematizing)."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Prime Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, The Three Circles Model, p. 196; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCLeadersEffectivenessShownGroupResponseSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Leader's effectiveness shown by group response"@en, "Wirksamkeit des Leiters zeigt sich an der Gruppenresonanz"@de ;
    skos:definition "The effectiveness of a leader's actions can be judged by how much the group responds."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: leader's effectiveness shown by group response; announced in advance by Hine, with no deadline or rate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, The Three Circles Model, p. 196; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Clarifying
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCTaskClarityBeforeSuccessfulAchievementPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Task clarity before successful achievement"@en, "Aufgabenklarheit vor erfolgreicher Durchführung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine states that a task will only succeed if it is clearly understood; members who cannot relate to a task give it less than whole-hearted support."@en ;
    skos:note "The dependent step is read onto the Three Circles model, whose first need is achieving the task."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCClarifyingCommonTaskBeforeGroup ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCThreeCirclesModelGroupNeeds ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Members who cannot relate to the task give it less than whole-hearted support, and the task is not achieved successfully."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Clarifying, p. 197; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCClarifyingCommonTaskBeforeGroup a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Clarifying the common task before a group ritual"@en, "Klärung der gemeinsamen Aufgabe vor einem Gruppenritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "The leader makes sure the task is meaningful to all, communicates it and checks others' understanding, breaks vague aims into specific steps and explains why; before a ritual with first-time celebrants, everyone is told why it is done, how, what is expected of each, and invited to ask for clarification."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Clarifying, p. 197; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Planning
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCInventedHereResistanceCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "'Not Invented Here' resistance"@en, "'Nicht hier erfunden'-Widerstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "A common resistance rejects ideas not originated by oneself or not part of one's tradition; Hine was surprised how magically open people dismissed ideas from science fiction, dramatherapy or psychology for not looking magical."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCStimulatingIdeaGenerationPlanning ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Planning, p. 198; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCStimulatingIdeaGenerationPlanning a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Stimulating idea generation in planning"@en, "Ideenfindung in der Planung anregen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Besides brainstorming with suspended judgement, the leader invites outside experience, builds on one person's suggestion, weaves members' suggestions into a team plan, and responds positively to every idea, deferring unfeasible ones rather than dismissing them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Planning, p. 198; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCComplexRitualPlansGoAwryFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Complex ritual plans go awry"@en, "Komplexe Ritualpläne misslingen"@de ;
    skos:definition "No plan is perfect; the more complex a ritual plan the likelier things go wrong (a dropped sword scattering incense, a member failing to bring the props), jokingly blamed on Eris watching; plans rarely survive contact with people."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: complex ritual plans go awry. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on chance (jokingly attributed to the goddess Eris) and other people."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Planning, p. 198; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCKeepingPlanBStandExercises a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Keeping a plan B and stand-by exercises"@en, "Einen Plan B und Reserveübungen bereithalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "As he was taught when trained to run groups, Hine keeps a flexible plan with a fallback plan and some reserve exercises in case of last-minute failure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Planning, p. 199; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCPlanningPreRitualBriefing a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Planning the pre-ritual briefing"@en, "Planung der Einweisung vor dem Ritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "Think ahead what to say; keep the message clear, avoid obscure jargon that unsettles newcomers, break complex procedures into points, and convey enthusiasm through vivid wording, body language and jokes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Planning, p. 199; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCPlanningGeneralSkillInfluencingGroup a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Planning as a general skill for influencing group situations"@en, "Planung als allgemeine Fähigkeit zur Beeinflussung von Gruppensituationen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Planning one's communication develops a broadly applicable skill: planning how to affect a group to foster teamwork and creativity or to encourage particular members, learnt only through experience."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Planning, p. 199; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCBriefingPracticeYieldsGeneralPlanning a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Briefing practice yields general planning skill"@en, "Einweisungspraxis bewirkt allgemeine Planungsfähigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Practising planned briefings is said to build confidence and a general skill of planning group influence."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCPlanningPreRitualBriefing ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCPlanningGeneralSkillInfluencingGroup ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Planning, p. 199; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Invisible Leadership
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCInvisibleLeadership a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Invisible leadership"@en, "Unsichtbare Führung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Citing Lao Tzu's verse that the best leader is barely noticed and lets people feel they did it themselves, Hine argues effective groups are largely self-regulating; the clearer the task, the more gently the leader can intervene, with a word or glance."@en ;
    skos:note "Opens with a verse attributed to Lao Tzu."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Invisible Leadership, pp. 199-200; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCQuietSilencingQuietConsensusTesting a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Quiet silencing and quiet consensus testing"@en, "Leises Zum-Schweigen-Bringen und leises Konsensprüfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine commends developing the ability to silence someone quietly but firmly and to test for consensus without fuss, as more useful long-term than being overbearing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Invisible Leadership, p. 200; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Motivating
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCDelegatingMotivatingVolunteers a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Delegating and motivating volunteers"@en, "Delegieren und Freiwillige motivieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ensure delegated tasks get done; check a volunteer has the resources (especially time) and abilities; tell him exactly what the task involves, ideally with a checklist; support him; recognise everyone's achievements equally, e.g. through the Sumble. Hine gives one or two chances, then no more."@en ;
    skos:note "Quotes Ralph Waldo Emerson on trust; refers back to the Sumble discussed earlier in the book."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Motivating, p. 200; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCLeaderEndingUpRunningEverythingCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Leader ending up running everything"@en, "Leiter macht am Ende alles selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "It is easy for a leader to end up doing everything himself when volunteers take on jobs without thinking them through."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCDelegatingMotivatingVolunteers ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Motivating, p. 200; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCTaskUndoneBecauseContentWasFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Task undone because its content was never explained"@en, "Aufgabe unerledigt, weil ihr Inhalt nie erklärt wurde"@de ;
    skos:definition "Managers often hand out a job without saying what it involves and then complain it was not done to their liking."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: task undone because its content was never explained. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the operator (leader)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Motivating, p. 200; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Self-Assessment
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCLeadersSelfAssessment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Leader's self-assessment"@en, "Selbsteinschätzung des Leiters"@de ;
    skos:definition "Leaders must be able to assess their own performance; self-assessment of feelings, experiences, behaviour and ideas is central to magical development and doubly so for group leaders, grown into over time rather than learnt overnight."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Self-Assessment, p. 201; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Bringing People Into the Group
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCAssessingCandidatesInterviewLetter a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Assessing candidates by interview and letter"@en, "Kandidatenprüfung durch Gespräch und Brief"@de ;
    skos:definition "Interview candidates, one-to-one or by a panel, in a public place; a no-show is read as a message about sincerity; examine first letters for an SAE, legibility and how the person presents himself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Bringing People Into the Group, pp. 201-202; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Bringing People Into the Group, What Next?
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCBringingCandidateGroup a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Bringing a candidate into the group"@en, "Einen Kandidaten in die Gruppe aufnehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "After first assessment, invite the candidate to a meeting and then gather members' comments, or admit him for a trial period like the Wiccan year-and-a-day before initiation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Bringing People Into the Group, What Next?, p. 202; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCYearDayBeforeWiccanInitiationPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Year-and-a-day before Wiccan initiation"@en, "Jahr und Tag vor der Wicca-Initiation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine cites the Wiccan custom of a period of a year and a day spent working with a coven before full initiation."@en ;
    skos:note "Wiccan coven practice."@en ;
    skos:note "Wiccan coven custom reported by Hine; no consequence of skipping is named."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCBringingCandidateGroup ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCInitiationsCelebrationsFosterGroupCohesion ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Bringing People Into the Group, What Next?, p. 202; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCBypassingInductionSexualReasonsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Bypassing induction for sexual reasons"@en, "Umgehung der Aufnahme aus sexuellen Motiven"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine condemns fast-tracking attractive candidates to high degrees; posing as a Magister to get sex is pathetic."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCBringingCandidateGroup ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Bringing People Into the Group, What Next?, p. 202; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Bringing People Into the Group, Who Gets In
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCHinesCriteriaAdmittingCandidates a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hine's criteria for admitting candidates"@en, "Hines Kriterien für die Aufnahme von Kandidaten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's list: do you get along with them as people; are they interesting with something to offer; what skills and resources they bring; what they say in interview (avoid head-nodders); prior magical experience and adaptability; whether to admit only known people; optimum size."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine's own compiled checklist (pm:Systematizing)."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Prime Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Bringing People Into the Group, Who Gets In, p. 203; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCNonWellReadNewcomersInnovate a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Non-well-read newcomers innovate"@en, "Wenig belesene Neulinge sind innovativ"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine finds that people not widely read in magic often devise innovative practices because they do not know any better; knowing Liber 777 by heart is no substitute for getting on with people."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Bringing People Into the Group, Who Gets In, p. 203; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCExperiencedCandidatesWhoInsistGroupCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Experienced candidates who insist the group is wrong"@en, "Erfahrene Kandidaten, die die Gruppe für falsch halten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Prior experience helps only if the candidate can adapt to the group's style rather than declaring its methods wrong on his former guru's authority."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCHinesCriteriaAdmittingCandidates ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Bringing People Into the Group, Who Gets In, p. 203; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAdmittingFriendsRisksFriendshipCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Admitting friends risks the friendship"@en, "Freunde aufzunehmen gefährdet die Freundschaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Even with friends a formal chat is advised; if things fail one may have to ask them to leave, which can damage the personal relationship."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCHinesCriteriaAdmittingCandidates ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Bringing People Into the Group, Who Gets In, p. 204; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Bringing People Into the Group, Does Size Matter?
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCOptimumSizeSmallMagicalGroup a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Optimum size of a small magical group"@en, "Optimale Größe einer kleinen magischen Gruppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "It is generally agreed that 8-12 people is optimal for a small magical group; other groups are limited by venue size."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Bringing People Into the Group, Does Size Matter?, p. 204; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Refusals
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCHandlingRefusalsComplaintsFirmlyFairly a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Handling refusals and complaints firmly and fairly"@en, "Ablehnungen und Beschwerden fest und fair behandeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Refuse firmly and fairly with a good, preferably truthful reason; when others complain about someone the leader likes, treat it as the leader's problem and handle it objectively so members see all views considered."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine has heard of groups declared single-sex to exclude one disruptive person."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Refusals, p. 204; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCBadlyHandledRefusalBreedsMaliciousFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Badly handled refusal breeds malicious rumours"@en, "Schlecht gehandhabte Ablehnung erzeugt üble Gerüchte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Handled poorly, refused people are likelier to become embittered and spread malicious rumours about leader and group."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: badly handled refusal breeds malicious rumours. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the operator (leader)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Refusals, p. 204; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, The Lemming Effect
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCLemmingEffectFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Lemming Effect"@en, "Der Lemming-Effekt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unhappy members vote with their feet and their friends may follow, often without explanation; Hine once lost four members of an open group in two weeks and learnt only later it was because of another member's offhand remark."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the Lemming Effect. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on another party (a remaining member's remark)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, The Lemming Effect, p. 205; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Expulsions
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCExpellingMember a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Expelling a member"@en, "Ein Mitglied ausschließen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Expulsion is a last resort, never done in desperation: give the person due awareness of the problem (Hine and a colleague gave three verbal warnings), then call a meeting with all members present so it is clearly a group decision, with the coordinators delivering the judgement honestly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Expulsions, pp. 205-206; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCDueWarningBeforeExpulsion a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Due warning before expulsion"@en, "Gebührende Verwarnung vor dem Ausschluss"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before expelling someone, make him duly aware of the problem; Hine and a colleague gave a persistently late member three verbal warnings first."@en ;
    skos:note "Split out of the expulsion procedure so that the order Hine sets can be carried."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Expulsions, pp. 205-206; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCWarningsBeforeExpulsionPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Warnings before expulsion"@en, "Verwarnungen vor dem Ausschluss"@de ;
    skos:definition "If expulsion is prefaced by making the offender aware and he makes no effort to change, he cannot really complain."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine adds that an offender warned in this way who has made no effort cannot really complain; that is a consequence of keeping the order, not of skipping it."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCDueWarningBeforeExpulsion ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCExpellingMember ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part III Group Effects, Running Groups, Expulsions, pp. 205-206; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, All Hail Discordia!
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCDiscordianismSocialStance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Discordianism as social stance"@en, "Diskordianismus als soziale Haltung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Discordianism, popularised by Wilson and Shea's Illuminatus! and the Principia Discordia of Malaclypse the Younger, looks like a religion of Eris; anyone can declare themselves a Discordian Pope, but it is chiefly a social perspective of sacred clowning, mocking authority and fusing humour with seriousness via Surrealist, Dada, Pataphysical and Situationist techniques, rooted in postwar paranoia and conspiracy culture."@en ;
    skos:note "Sources: R.A. Wilson & R. Shea, Illuminatus!; Malaclypse the Younger, Principia Discordia."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicOrcEveryoneAGenuinePope (Oven-Ready Chaos, 1992): there the Pope tactic is given as how the movement spreads; here Discordianism is read as a social stance of sacred clowning with its techniques and history."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, All Hail Discordia!, pp. 207-208; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCErissMessageFoundersDiscordianismReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "Eris's message to the founders of Discordianism"@en, "Botschaft der Eris an die Gründer des Diskordianismus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Principia Discordia relates that around the start of the 1950s Eris showed herself to a pair of young Californians, who thereupon became Omar Ravenhurst and Malaclypse the Younger; she named them Keepers of the Sacred Chao, charging them to tell humankind that rules exist only where people choose to make them."@en ;
    skos:note "Principia Discordia (Malaclypse the Younger)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondAErisMessageReceiving (Condensed Chaos, 1995): there the appearance is dated to the late 1950s; here, citing Principia Discordia, Hine dates it to the early 1950s and adds that Omar and Mal then declared each other High Priest and formed a Society of Discordia."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "A pair of young Californians who thereby became Omar Ravenhurst KSC and Malaclypse the Younger, as Principia Discordia relates and Hine retells" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "Eris" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "An appearance of the goddess in the early 1950s, in which she appointed the two Keepers of the Sacred Chao; no state, witness or record is described." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, All Hail Discordia!, p. 207; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCDangerTakingOneselfTooSeriouslyCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Danger of taking oneself too seriously"@en, "Gefahr, sich selbst zu ernst zu nehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "From a magical angle, Discordian touches serve to expose the risk of excessive seriousness about oneself or one's work."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCDiscordianismSocialStance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, All Hail Discordia!, p. 208; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Sacred Weapons of Power, Dice
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCDiceMagic a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dice magic"@en, "Würfelmagie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pick six possible actions or behaviours and let a roll of the die decide which to carry out; rolling is also a moment to ask Eris for favour. Hine took this up after Luke Rhinehart's novel The Diceman."@en ;
    skos:note "Inspired by Luke Rhinehart (spelled Rheinhardt in text), The Diceman."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDiceManCaution (Condensed Chaos, 1995): there Rhinehart's novel is cited for a caution about the effects of deconditioning on others; here the dice method itself is given."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Sacred Weapons of Power, Dice, pp. 208-209; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Sacred Weapons of Power, The Ego-Hammer
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCEgoHammer a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The Ego-Hammer"@en, "Der Ego-Hammer"@de ;
    skos:definition "A brightly coloured inflatable hammer (originally a lump-hammer) is applied to someone ranting or pontificating, while uttering 'Bonk' or 'Biff' as power-mantras, with a mocking litany."@en ;
    skos:note "Humorous Erisian weapon."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Sacred Weapons of Power, The Ego-Hammer, p. 209; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Sacred Weapons of Power, The Chaos Grenade
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCChaosGrenade a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The Chaos Grenade"@en, "Die Chaos-Granate"@de ;
    skos:definition "Compress Murphy's Law, the Uncertainty Principle or anything else into an etheric ball; to use, hold it, mime pulling its pin, then throw it into a space or group; to use on oneself, hold the ball and throw away the pin."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Sacred Weapons of Power, The Chaos Grenade, p. 209; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCInjectionErisianWackinessSelfIllumination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Injection of Erisian wackiness; self-illumination (hedged)"@en, "Einspritzung erisischer Verrücktheit; Selbsterleuchtung (eingeschränkt)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The grenade is said to inject Erisian chaos into a space or group, and used on oneself to illuminate, with Hine's ironic rider that it may not."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Sacred Weapons of Power, The Chaos Grenade, p. 209; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCChaosGrenadeYieldsErisianDisruption a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Chaos Grenade yields Erisian disruption/illumination"@en, "Chaos-Granate bewirkt erisische Störung/Erleuchtung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Throwing the grenade yields wackiness in the target; throwing the pin yields (perhaps) illumination."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCChaosGrenade ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCInjectionErisianWackinessSelfIllumination ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Sacred Weapons of Power, The Chaos Grenade, p. 209; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Smartie Servitor
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCSmartieServitorRitual a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Smartie Servitor ritual"@en, "Smartie-Servitor-Ritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "(1) State the intent to make one's town more fun, optionally visualising a Discordian Chaosphere; (2) perform the Airburst visualisation; (3) when the leader judges it established, chant the names of the four avatars of Chaos while visualising waves expanding the column into a wobbly sphere, with a slow drumbeat; (4) speed chant and drum, count down from ten, shout 'Blast off', and visualise billions of Smarties marked FUN raining over the town; banish with laughter."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Smartie Servitor, pp. 209-210; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCRaisingTownsNiceWeirdness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Raising a town's 'nice weirdness'"@en, "Steigerung der 'netten Seltsamkeit' in einer Stadt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Smartie Servitor aims to increase pleasant weirdness and fun in one's town, people radiating a glow of magical possibility."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Smartie Servitor, p. 209; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSmartieServitorYieldsTownWide a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Smartie Servitor yields town-wide nice weirdness"@en, "Smartie-Servitor bewirkt stadtweite nette Seltsamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ritual is aimed at making the town more fun."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCSmartieServitorRitual ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCRaisingTownsNiceWeirdness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Smartie Servitor, p. 209; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCDiscordianChaosphere a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Discordian Chaosphere"@en, "Diskordianische Chaossphäre"@de ;
    skos:definition "A Chaosphere with a smiley face at its centre and wobbly arrows, representing the happiness of accepting chaos and recognising Eris's hand in all that happens."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Smartie Servitor, p. 209; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCAirburstGroupVisualisation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "'Airburst' group visualisation"@en, "'Airburst'-Gruppenvisualisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sit in a ring, arms linked, with deep rhythmic breathing; feel an energy circuit build among members; each projects a cord of energy into the centre; the cords twine into a column, visualised as free-standing and pulsing in rainbow colours."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBAirburstServitorLaunch (Condensed Chaos, 1995): there the Airburst is a servitor launch for one operator, usable by groups; here it is a group visualisation in a linked circle with cords twining into a column."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Smartie Servitor, p. 210; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCFourChaosAvatarsMarxBrothersNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The four Chaos avatars (Marx Brothers)"@en, "Vier Avatare des Chaos: Harpo, Chico, Zeppo, Groucho"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Marx Brothers' names are used as the four avatars of Chaos summoned by chanting in the Smartie Servitor."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "HARPO", "CHICO", "ZEPPO", "GROUCHO" ;
    pm:nameRole "avatars of Chaos summoned in ritual" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Smartie Servitor, p. 210; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCBanishingLaughter a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Banishing with laughter"@en, "Bannen durch Lachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A rite is closed by the participants laughing; Hine repeats the injunction when proposing magic as comedy."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondALaughterBanishing (Condensed Chaos, 1995): there some IOT Pact members are said to banish by laughing; here laughter is prescribed as the close of the Smartie Servitor and taken up again in the call to see magic as comedy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Smartie Servitor, p. 210; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Spiral Pentagrams
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSpiralPentagramYieldsAstralDoorway a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Spiral pentagram yields an astral doorway for Eris"@en, "Spiralpentagramm bewirkt eine astrale Pforte für Eris"@de ;
    skos:definition "Using the spinning curved pentagram is presented as opening a tunnel suited to invoking Eris."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicOrcSpiralPentagramYieldsDrawingIn (Oven-Ready Chaos, 1992): there a first working with Eris is reported to have gone very well; here Hine only finds the spinning figure fitting for invoking Eris and calls it a tunnel, without reporting a result."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicOrcSpiralPentagram ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicOrcAstralDoorway ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Spiral Pentagrams, p. 210; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Theurgy
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCErisDiscordianNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Eris (Discordian)"@en, "Eris (diskordianisch)"@de ;
    skos:definition "For Discordian magicians Eris is the hidden hand of Chaos, instigator of weird phenomena, coincidences and Fortean events, whose flipside is patroness of Bureaucracy; she is the cheerful anarchy of fools, clowns and children, unlike the primal Chaos of the Great Old Ones, and present in all events defying rational explanation."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondAErisNaming (Condensed Chaos, 1995): there Eris is named with her classical genealogy and the apple; here she is the Discordian hidden hand of Chaos and patroness of Bureaucracy."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Eris" ;
    pm:nameRole "goddess of chaos; patroness of bureaucracy" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Theurgy, p. 211; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCErisSpeaksStupidBookReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "Eris speaks in The Stupid Book"@en, "Eris spricht im Stupid Book"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine cites a short speech attributed to Eris in The Stupid Book, in which she says the past does not know her, each moment begins anew and she has shed the gown of unborn possibilities."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCErisStupidBook (Condensed Chaos, 1995): a different passage credited to Eris and The Stupid Book."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "Not stated; the words are credited to Eris and to The Stupid Book, with no author named" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "Eris" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "Quoted in the Erisian Theurgy section as a speech of Eris from The Stupid Book; no circumstances of reception are given." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Theurgy, p. 211; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCInspirationUnlookedInformationSynchronicityThrough a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inspiration, unlooked-for information and synchronicity through invoking Eris"@en, "Inspiration, unerwartete Information und Synchronizität durch Anrufung der Eris"@de ;
    skos:definition "Eris can be called on for inspiration, for information from an unexpected source, or to raise the level of synchronicities in an unfolding event system."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Theurgy, p. 211; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCErissBizarreHumourTowardThoseCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Eris's bizarre humour toward those who propitiate her"@en, "Eris' bizarrer Humor gegenüber jenen, die sie besänftigen wollen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Devotees report that though friendly to humanity, Eris turns a bizarre sense of humour on those who try to propitiate her."@en ;
    skos:note "Report of Eris's devotees."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCInspirationUnlookedInformationSynchronicityThrough ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Theurgy, p. 212; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCHiroshimaNuclearGoddessNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Hiroshima the nuclear goddess"@en, "Hiroshima, die Atomgöttin"@de ;
    skos:definition "A cartoon character Hine has come across being treated as a modern deity arising from contemporary mythology."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Hiroshima" ;
    pm:nameRole "modern pop-culture goddess" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Theurgy, p. 212; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCBugsBunnyWileECoyoteNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Bugs Bunny, Wile E. Coyote: trickster gods"@en, "Bugs Bunny und Wile E. Coyote als Trickster"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cartoon characters treated as archetypal trickster deities in the modern mythic landscape."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Bugs Bunny", "Wile E. Coyote" ;
    pm:nameRole "archetypal tricksters / modern gods" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Theurgy, p. 212; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCRitaGoddessParkingNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Rita, goddess of parking"@en, "Rita, Göttin des Parkens"@de ;
    skos:definition "A modern deity Hine has encountered, cited among new gods arising from contemporary culture."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Rita" ;
    pm:nameRole "goddess of parking" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Theurgy, p. 212; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCJohnLennonGodGrantMorrisonNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "John Lennon as god (Grant Morrison)"@en, "John Lennon als Gott (Grant Morrison)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Grant Morrison is said to have raised John Lennon to godhood and thus to an object of magical invocation."@en ;
    skos:note "Grant Morrison."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "John Lennon" ;
    pm:nameRole "deified pop figure for invocation" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Theurgy, p. 212; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCNewGodsNeedPriorOccult a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "New gods need no prior occult belief"@en, "Neue Götter brauchen keinen okkulten Vorglauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Modern deities appeal because no buy-in to occult belief is required; Hine's mid-1980s open Erisian events drew people uninterested in the occult who liked the idea of a chaos goddess stirring events."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Theurgy, p. 212; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAgainstClaimFictionalGodsLess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the claim that fictional gods are less valid than historical ones"@en, "Gegen die Behauptung, fiktive Götter seien weniger gültig als historische"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine rejects the argument that fictional entities are less valid than historical deities, likening it to holding that valid methods must be old, and to assuming deities never change; a teen identifying with a pop star shares the magician's intent of change through identification, equally or more effective, the only difference being that the magician learnt to invoke."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the opposing view is reported by him, not quoted from a named work."@en ;
    skos:note "Opponents: traditionalist occultists (unnamed)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFictionalEntitiesDefence (Condensed Chaos, 1995): there Hine answers critics who demand historical roots; here he adds the comparison of the invoking magician with the teenager modelling himself on a pop star."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Theurgy, p. 212; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAgainstSolemnReverenceGodsModern a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against solemn reverence for gods in modern paganism"@en, "Gegen feierliche Ehrfurcht vor Göttern im modernen Heidentum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine contests the modern magical and pagan taboo on laughing at the gods, calling its reverence Christian-like, and points to humour in historical paganism such as Norse tales of Loki and Thor in a dress."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the opposing view is reported by him, not quoted from a named work."@en ;
    skos:note "Disputed: some modern pagan circles."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Theurgy, pp. 212-213; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCMagicPlay a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magic as play"@en, "Magie als Spiel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reading the motto that nothing is true and all is permitted as placing magic alongside play, humour and entertainment, Hine notes shared contrast with the ordinary, game-like divination, play with identity, folklore and anecdote, and hoaxes and tricksters through magical history."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBMagicPlay (Condensed Chaos, 1995): there play and magic share their distance from the ordinary; here the point is drawn from Nothing is True and extended to divination, identity, folklore, hoaxes and comedy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Theurgy, p. 213; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCInvocationEvocationPlayImaginaryFriends a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Invocation and evocation as play with imaginary friends"@en, "Anrufung und Evokation als Spiel mit imaginären Freunden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine finds theories of subpersonalities and archetypes distance one from the entities; he prefers to relate to deities like a child's imaginary friends, and sees evocation as dressing the indefinable in imagination's colours."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Erisian Theurgy, p. 214; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Magical Misdirection
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCMagicalMisdirectionWiseFool a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical misdirection and the Wise Fool"@en, "Magische Irreführung und der weise Narr"@de ;
    skos:definition "Misdirection obscures roles: magicians like Crowley and Alex Sanders had trickster sides, and the Wise Fool (Tarot Fool, Anansi, Loki) mocks and threatens the establishment; once seen as a fool one gets away with much, and being dismissed as a crank is safer than persecution; Zen masters disguise status with humour."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Magical Misdirection, p. 214; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Social Disguises
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCLeavingPastSelfBehind a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Leaving family and friends for a place where one's past is unknown"@en, "Familie und Freunde verlassen für einen Ort, an dem die eigene Vergangenheit unbekannt ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "According to Castaneda's Don Juan, the would-be brujo first leaves every relative and friend behind and goes where nobody knows his former self."@en ;
    skos:note "Carlos Castaneda's Don Juan, whom Hine calls possibly fictional. Split out of pass-A record A3-0163 so that its order can be carried."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Social Disguises, p. 215; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCMaskOfTheBrujo a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The mask of the brujo (magical personality)"@en, "Die Maske des Brujo (magische Persönlichkeit)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Don Juan's mask of the brujo, which Hine glosses as the magical personality, is cultivated where one's past self is unknown; Hine takes it as a case of the status disguise magicians cultivate."@en ;
    skos:note "Carlos Castaneda's Don Juan. Split out of pass-A record A3-0163."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Social Disguises, p. 215; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCLeavePastSelfBehindCultivatePrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Leave past self behind to cultivate the brujo's mask (Don Juan)"@en, "Das frühere Selbst zurücklassen, um die Maske des Brujo zu pflegen (Don Juan)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Castaneda's Don Juan holds that a would-be brujo must first leave family and friends for a place where his former self is unknown and cultivate the magical personality."@en ;
    skos:note "Carlos Castaneda's Don Juan (Hine doubts he is factual)."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine doubts that Don Juan is factual; no consequence of skipping is named."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCLeavingPastSelfBehind ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCMaskOfTheBrujo ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Social Disguises, p. 215; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCHighAccordedStatusEasesTrance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "High accorded status eases trance induction and healing"@en, "Hoher zugeschriebener Status erleichtert Tranceinduktion und Heilung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The higher the status others grant a magician, the more readily one can put them in trance or heal them; a high-status director lets members let go in intense ritual, trusting he will keep it in hand; high status is a role to adopt and lay aside."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Social Disguises, p. 215; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCCravingPermanentHighStatusExaltedCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Craving permanent high status and exalted titles"@en, "Gier nach dauerhaftem hohen Status und erhabenen Titeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wanting permanent high status has led magicians to claim exalted titles and grades in one-upmanship that is destructive for all and tedious to watch."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCHighAccordedStatusEasesTrance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Social Disguises, p. 215; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCInsightStatusRoles a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Insight into status roles"@en, "Einsicht in Statusrollen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Status games are said to reveal which status roles people play."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Social Disguises, p. 215; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCStatusGamesYieldInsightStatus a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Status games yield insight into status roles"@en, "Statusspiele bewirken Einsicht in Statusrollen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Playing the Gurus and Disciples game reveals how status is performed."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCGurusDisciplesStatusGame ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCInsightStatusRoles ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Social Disguises, p. 215; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Social Disguises, Gurus and Disciples
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCGurusDisciplesStatusGame a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Gurus and Disciples status game"@en, "Statusspiel 'Gurus und Jünger'"@de ;
    skos:definition "One person plays a guru, the others disciples who beg answers on life and everything; the guru explains while disciples hang on every word; what matters is the manner, not the content."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Social Disguises, Gurus and Disciples, p. 215; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCExploitativeGurusDiscriminationCounselledCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Exploitative gurus; discrimination counselled"@en, "Ausbeuterische Gurus; Urteilsvermögen geraten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some would-be gurus seek money, power, sex or importance; seekers are advised to use discrimination before opening mind, wallet or legs and to ask why someone acts as a teacher."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCGurusDisciplesStatusGame ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Social Disguises, Gurus and Disciples, pp. 215-216; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCCuresDropWhenBeliefWithdrawnFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cures drop when belief is withdrawn"@en, "Heilungen sinken, wenn der Glaube schwindet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fringe medicines succeeded through clients' belief; once exposed as fraudulent their cure rate fell sharply."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: cures drop when belief is withdrawn. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on another party (loss of patient belief after exposure)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Social Disguises, Gurus and Disciples, p. 216; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCMagicalHealingWorksThroughPatients a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical healing works through the patient's belief"@en, "Magische Heilung wirkt durch den Glauben des Patienten"@de ;
    skos:definition "An impressive symbol system raises status; much magical healing tricks the person into healing himself through unquestioning belief in the magician."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Social Disguises, Gurus and Disciples, p. 216; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Merry Pranksters
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCMoneyRitualDiscordianStreetTheatre a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The Money Ritual (Discordian street theatre)"@en, "Das Geldritual (diskordianisches Straßentheater)"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Leeds on 2 November 1985 twenty people dressed as business people followed a leader holding a cardboard pound sign through a shopping centre, chanting praise of money with hands in prayer, swore allegiance to money outside a bank and continued through town; some onlookers threw money and at the last performance police arrested three."@en ;
    skos:note "Reported instance of Discordian street theatre."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Merry Pranksters, p. 216; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Advertising As Sorcery
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAdvertisingSorcery a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Advertising as sorcery"@en, "Werbung als Zauberei"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine treats advertisements as a development of sorcerous enchantment: compact hyper-real mythologies aimed at the unconscious, often built on problem, promise and an overt or covert myth, raising and then resolving dissonance between ideal and lived life to manipulate desire; the most successful create a glamour of taste and style."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Advertising As Sorcery, pp. 216-218; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Profaning the Sacred
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCSubvertingAdvertisingProfaningSacred a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Subverting advertising (profaning the sacred)"@en, "Werbung unterwandern (Profanierung des Heiligen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Discordian activists produce innocuous-looking advertising material carrying a subversive message, or add witty ripostes to billboards, using advertising's mythic power for their own ends in the manner of media sorcery."@en ;
    skos:note "Discordian activists generally; example of a sexist car advert with added rejoinder."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Profaning the Sacred, p. 218; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGraffitiMagicalAct a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Graffiti as magical act"@en, "Graffiti als magischer Akt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Graffiti can make hidden voices heard, reclaim urban space and form a magical tapestry marking places of power and a collective tarot of colliding signs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Profaning the Sacred, p. 218; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSymbolsEscapeMakers a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Symbols escape their makers"@en, "Symbole entkommen ihren Schöpfern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine recounts chalk symbols outside the occult publisher where he worked spawning a day of theories (magical attack, Tongs, fascist markers) until they proved to be directions to a band's gig; likewise readers of Morrison's Invisibles now spray 'Barbelith' on Liverpool walls; contrived magical fragments can take on a life of their own."@en ;
    skos:note "Barbelith from Grant Morrison's The Invisibles."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nice, Profaning the Sacred, p. 219; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Cthulhu Mythos Magic
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCMagicNonHistoricalFictionalSources a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magic from non-historical, fictional sources"@en, "Magie aus nicht-historischen, fiktiven Quellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "For some decades magicians have developed perspectives from literature, science fiction and urban myth; the Cthulhu Mythos of Lovecraft and his circle is a prime example of appropriating a fictional belief system."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Cthulhu Mythos Magic, p. 220; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGreatOldOnesNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Great Old Ones"@en, "Die Großen Alten"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Lovecraft's fiction, alien entities from stars or other dimensions who once ruled Earth and can now manifest only through their followers' rites or when the stars are right; mostly mindless 'idiot gods', huge and hungry, forming no pantheon and, as Lovecraft first conceived them, no elemental or good-evil scheme, which Derleth added later."@en ;
    skos:note "H.P. Lovecraft; later modifications by August Derleth."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCGreatOldOnesNaming (Condensed Chaos, 1995): there the Old Ones are characterised by their place outside human mythologies and the fear attached to them; here by Lovecraft's own account: idiot gods, no pantheon, no good-evil scheme until Derleth."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "The Great Old Ones" ;
    pm:nameRole "alien cosmic entities" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Cthulhu Mythos Magic, pp. 220-222; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGlimpsingOldOnesShattersSanityCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Glimpsing the Old Ones shatters sanity"@en, "Ein Blick auf die Alten zerstört den Verstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the Mythos even a brief glimpse of these beings can break one's sanity, and encounters in Lovecraft's fiction are almost always fatal to protagonist and bystanders."@en ;
    skos:note "Within Lovecraft's fiction."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGreatOldOnesNaming ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Cthulhu Mythos Magic, p. 221; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCNyarlathotepCrawlingChaosNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Nyarlathotep, the Crawling Chaos"@en, "Nyarlathotep, das Kriechende Chaos"@de ;
    skos:definition "The only Old One shown with something like human intelligence; occasionally appears as the 'black man' leading the cultists' sabbat, suggesting a human avatar for cult worship using physical routes to gnosis."@en ;
    skos:note "Lovecraft."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Nyarlathotep" ;
    pm:nameRole "Crawling Chaos; intelligent Old One; sabbat leader" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Cthulhu Mythos Magic, p. 221; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCCthulhuMythosCompleteMagicalBelief a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Cthulhu Mythos as a complete magical belief-system"@en, "Der Cthulhu-Mythos als vollständiges magisches Glaubenssystem"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine finds in the Mythos all key elements of a magical system: dream-borne information, sacred topology (astral spaces, Dreamlands, sites), relations among Elder Beings and slave-races; its entities lie beyond existing frames of reference and resist being fitted into the Qabalah, perceivable only via dreams, pathworkings, subconscious messages, rites at power spots or a human vehicle."@en ;
    skos:note "Against unnamed magical writers who map the Old Ones onto the Qabalah."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Cthulhu Mythos Magic, p. 222; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Embedding the Cthulhu Mythos
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCEmbeddingCthulhuMythos a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Embedding the Cthulhu Mythos"@en, "Einbettung des Cthulhu-Mythos"@de ;
    skos:definition "Enter through Lovecraft's Mythos stories and those of his circle, e.g. Clark Ashton Smith; attend to their emotional effect and resulting dreams; make images of visions or feelings, which can later serve as fetishes or talismans for willed exploration of the Mythos."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Embedding the Cthulhu Mythos, p. 222; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCCreepingParanoiaMythosReadingCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Creeping paranoia from Mythos reading"@en, "Schleichende Paranoia durch Mythos-Lektüre"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magicians in this paradigm often report that the tales work subtly on the emotions, an effect that can grow into creeping paranoia or fear, often announced in dreams."@en ;
    skos:note "Reports of magicians working with the Mythos."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCEmbeddingCthulhuMythos ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Embedding the Cthulhu Mythos, p. 222; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSpontaneousImagingFirstResultEmbeddingSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spontaneous imaging as first result of embedding"@en, "Spontane Bildgestaltung als erstes Ergebnis der Einbettung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Feeling prompted to make images of one's visions or feelings is the first result of the paradigm embedding itself, the mythic breaking through into waking life."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success of pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCEmbeddingCthulhuMythos: spontaneous imaging as first result of embedding; announced in advance by Hine, with no deadline or rate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Embedding the Cthulhu Mythos, p. 223; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Dreamscaping
#

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCDreamscaping a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dreamscaping"@en, "Traumlandschaftsarbeit (Dreamscaping)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keep a rigorous dream diary; take dreams with consistent Mythos elements as the basis for astral image sequences performed as meditation; follow the sequence while drifting into sleep; in time look for particular clues and places inside the personal dream-time thus woven."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Dreamscaping, p. 223; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCVividMythosDreamsContinuingConsciously a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Vivid Mythos dreams continuing a consciously built narrative"@en, "Lebhafte Mythos-Träume, die eine bewusst angelegte Erzählung fortsetzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Over time Mythos dreams become more vivid and the dream continues the consciously created narrative, giving access to a personal dream-time to explore."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Dreamscaping, p. 223; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCDreamscapingYieldsVividContinuingMythos a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dreamscaping yields vivid continuing Mythos dreams"@en, "Dreamscaping bewirkt lebhafte, fortgesetzte Mythos-Träume"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following meditated sequences into sleep is said to make Mythos dreams vivid and narrative-continuing."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCDreamscaping ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCVividMythosDreamsContinuingConsciously ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Dreamscaping, p. 223; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCDreamsGrowVividCarryNarrativeSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dreams grow vivid and carry on the narrative"@en, "Träume werden lebhaft und führen die Erzählung fort"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign of progress: Mythos dreams grow ever more vivid and the dreaming carries on the meditated narrative."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success of pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCDreamscaping: dreams grow vivid and carry on the narrative; announced in advance by Hine, with no deadline or rate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Dreamscaping, p. 223; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCExampleMythosDreamscapeSequenceRLyeh a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Example Mythos dreamscape sequence (R'Lyeh)"@en, "Beispiel einer Mythos-Traumsequenz (R'Lyeh)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's sample: on a night beach under unknown stars a dark messenger from the sea offers a black drink; after vomiting one sinks to R'Lyeh, flows through it in a shoggoth body as globules of consciousness to a crystalline chamber, reshapes into human form with the word 'Abaddon', reaches for a guarded box-like gateway, is struck back as a vast eye opens and darkness falls, then is whirled into ordinary dream."@en ;
    skos:note "Said to convey the emotional experience of working the Mythos; the reach for the gateway is repelled."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Dreamscaping, pp. 223-224; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCDeepOnesNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Deep Ones"@en, "Tiefe Wesen (Deep Ones)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sea-dwelling slave-race of the Old Ones that sometimes interbreed with humans producing hybrids; in Hine's dreamscape a barely formed messenger unlike Lovecraft's."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Deep One" ;
    pm:nameRole "slave-race / dream messenger" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Dreamscaping, p. 223; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCShoggothNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Shoggoth"@en, "Shoggoth"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Hine's dreamscape a shoggoth body is taken on as an ideal form for traversing R'Lyeh's tunnels and angles, impossible for a human shape."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Shoggoth" ;
    pm:nameRole "formless body assumed for astral travel" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Dreamscaping, p. 224; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCEntryMythosSlowLovecraftsFiction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Entry into the Mythos is slow; Lovecraft's fiction supplies the techniques"@en, "Der Eintritt in den Mythos ist langsam; Lovecrafts Fiktion liefert die Techniken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine notes that entering this paradigm is gradual and that Lovecraft's tales give the clues to the techniques for exploring it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Dreamscaping, p. 224; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCDreamsGatewayLucidConsistentDreaming a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dreams as gateway; lucid consistent dreaming as shamanic"@en, "Träume als Pforte; luzides, konsistentes Träumen als schamanisch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lovecraft denied the occult but his dreams gave him occult concepts he branded evil; magicians value dream images; internally consistent lucid dreaming is a core of shamanism, and astral sabbats and initiations like his protagonists' are common among magicians, spontaneously or through willed dreaming with sigils or psychoactives."@en ;
    skos:note "Some cultures recognise shamans by their dreams."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Dreamscaping, pp. 224-225; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCCthulhuNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Cthulhu"@en, "Cthulhu"@de ;
    skos:definition "The most prominent Old One, a winged cephalic star-being lying in death's dream in a crypt in R'Lyeh under the Pacific; lord of dreams, intermediary between human consciousness and wholly alien Old Ones; his dream transmissions trigger worldwide insanity when R'Lyeh surfaces."@en ;
    skos:note "Lovecraft, The Call of Cthulhu."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCGreatOldOnesNaming (Condensed Chaos, 1995): that node carries Cthulhu only as a name form beside the Old Ones; here Cthulhu is named as lord of dreams and intermediary."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Cthulhu" ;
    pm:nameRole "lord of dreams; intermediary Old One" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Dreamscaping, p. 225; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAzathothYogSothothNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Azathoth and Yog-Sothoth"@en, "Azathoth und Yog-Sothoth"@de ;
    skos:definition "Old Ones of truly alien nature to which Cthulhu mediates; in The Dunwich Horror Yog-Sothoth unites with a female cultist in a hieros gamos."@en ;
    skos:note "Lovecraft."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Azathoth", "Yog-Sothoth" ;
    pm:nameRole "utterly alien Old Ones" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Dreamscaping, p. 225; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSpareDreamAnglesFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spare could not set down the angles he saw in dreams"@en, "Spare konnte die im Traum gesehenen Winkel nicht festhalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Austin Osman Spare is said to have perceived weird angles and mathematics in dreams but to have been unable to put them on paper."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: Spare could not set down the angles he saw in dreams. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on another party (the nature of what is seen in dreams)."@en ;
    skos:note "Austin Osman Spare, as Hine reports him. Integrator addition; compare the Leng tarot images Hine himself could not set down."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Dreamscaping, p. 225; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCRLyehPsychicGateway a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "R'Lyeh as psychic gateway"@en, "R'Lyeh als psychische Pforte"@de ;
    skos:definition "R'Lyeh's non-Euclidean city consists of gates into other dimensions, comparable to the Tunnels of Set of Kenneth Grant, and a gateway to deeper consciousness where dreams carry two-way traffic between waking awareness and Deep Mind; Michael Aquino has identified it with Nan-Madol on Ponape."@en ;
    skos:note "Michael Aquino (Nan-Madol identification); Kenneth Grant (Tunnels of Set); Spare's interest in weird angles."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Dreamscaping, pp. 225-226; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCNameNecronomiconCameLovecraftDreamReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "The name 'Necronomicon' came to Lovecraft in dream"@en, "Lovecraft empfing den Namen 'Necronomicon' im Traum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lovecraft says in a 1937 letter to Harry Fischer that the name came to him in a dream; translating it, he did, per Robert M. Price, what oracles did in interpreting the gods' glossolalia."@en ;
    skos:note "Lovecraft letter to Harry Fischer, Feb. 1937; interpretation by Robert M. Price."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "H. P. Lovecraft" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "No speaker is named; the name is said to have come to Lovecraft in a dream" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "A dream, described by Lovecraft in his February 1937 letter to Harry Fischer; he then rendered the name into English himself, which Robert M. Price likens to oracles interpreting the glossolalia of the gods." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon, p. 226; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCOneiricRevelationCannotPutDirectly a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Oneiric revelation cannot be put directly into language"@en, "Traumoffenbarung lässt sich nicht unmittelbar in Sprache fassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Divine or dream revelations cannot be rendered directly; one can only sketch the edges of their fading afterglow."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon, p. 226; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCTarotImagesShownPlateauLengReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "Tarot images shown on the Plateau of Leng"@en, "Tarotbilder, gezeigt auf dem Plateau von Leng"@de ;
    skos:definition "In a dream of a monastery on the Plateau of Leng, a keeper showed Hine intricately detailed tarot images, remarking cynically that he knew Hine could not carry them into the physical world."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "Phil Hine" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "The keeper of the images in Hine's dream, unnamed" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "A dream, a few years before writing, of a cyclopean monastery on the Plateau of Leng; the keeper displayed the images and remarked that Hine would not be able to carry them into the physical world. No record survives, since Hine reports he could not set the images down." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon, pp. 226-227; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCDreamImagesCannotTransferredWakingFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dream images cannot be transferred to waking record"@en, "Traumbilder lassen sich nicht ins Wachprotokoll übertragen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Though Hine can easily recall the Leng tarot images, he finds it impossible to set them down, as the keeper foretold."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: dream images cannot be transferred to waking record. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on another party (nature of oneiric revelation)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon, p. 226; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCConcealmentDeferralMagicalDeviceEmpty a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Concealment and deferral as magical device (the empty Necronomicon)"@en, "Verbergen und Aufschieben als magisches Mittel (das leere Necronomicon)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lovecraft never discloses the Necronomicon's truths but defers them through hints, a device also in Chambers' King in Yellow and William Ward's accounts of Tantra; Kenneth Grant turns it into a technique luring readers from text toward gnosis; its secret is that there is no secret, and this concealing-revealing is paradigmatic of magic; Burroughs adds that naming something removes its power."@en ;
    skos:note "Robert W. Chambers; Rev. William Ward; Kenneth Grant (Typhonian Trilogies); William S. Burroughs, The Place of Dead Roads."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon, pp. 227-228; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCPublishedNecronomiconsDisappointFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Published Necronomicons disappoint"@en, "Veröffentlichte Necronomicons enttäuschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because horror must stay unrevealed, no literal Necronomicon can match the imagination; the grimoire-style editions are not blasphemous in themselves (only Giger's artbook unsettled Hine)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: published Necronomicons disappoint. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the method (literal text cannot match imagination)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon, p. 228; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCWorkingPublishedNecronomicons a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Working the published Necronomicon spell texts"@en, "Arbeit mit den veröffentlichten Necronomicon-Ritualtexten"@de ;
    skos:definition "One may choose to work the published books titled Necronomicon, spell and ritual texts in the manner of the medieval grimoires."@en ;
    skos:note "Only the working is named; no steps are given. Split out of pass-A record A3-0203."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon, p. 228; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCLeapGnosisNeededNecronomiconTextsPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Leap into gnosis needed for Necronomicon texts to reveal"@en, "Sprung in die Gnosis nötig, damit Necronomicon-Texte offenbaren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Working the published spell texts may lead to shocking revelation, but only through the magician's individual leap into gnosis."@en ;
    skos:note "No consequence of skipping is named beyond that the texts are not blasphemous in themselves."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondAGnosisAtWill ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCWorkingPublishedNecronomicons ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon, p. 228; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAstralBooks a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Astral Books"@en, "Astralbücher"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine suggests treating the Necronomicon as an Astral Book: reachable solely in dream or vision and passed on by automatic writing, channelling or possession by an entity or the book itself; such books are personal to their receivers, though many take them as new truths to proclaim."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon, pp. 228-229; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCReceiversAstralBooksTurningProphetCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Receivers of astral books turning prophet"@en, "Empfänger von Astralbüchern werden zu Propheten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many who receive such communications treat them as fresh revelations with themselves as prophets and feel driven to spread them, often via vanity presses."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAstralBooks ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon, p. 229; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCReceivingOnesAstralBook a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Receiving one's astral book"@en, "Empfang des eigenen Astralbuchs"@de ;
    skos:definition "The exercise and related routes help discover the nature of the book everyone is said to carry, which may come as text, sigils, diagrams, images, poetry or glimpses of entities."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon, p. 229; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCBookshelfExerciseYieldsAccessOnes a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Bookshelf exercise yields access to one's astral book"@en, "Bücherregalübung bewirkt Zugang zum eigenen Astralbuch"@de ;
    skos:definition "The visualisation is presented as a starting route into receiving one's book."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCFindingOnesBookBookshelfVisualisation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCReceivingOnesAstralBook ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon, p. 229; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCFindingOnesBookBookshelfVisualisation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding one's own book (bookshelf visualisation)"@en, "Das eigene Buch finden (Bücherregal-Visualisierung)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagine being an author before a large bookshelf; find your book and note spine colour and lettering; take it down, weigh it, feel and smell it, describe the cover; open it, look at the text, turn to page one and start reading."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon, p. 229; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSelfAwarenessBreaksReadingTranceFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-awareness breaks the reading trance"@en, "Selbstgewahrsein bricht die Lesetrance"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine usually finds people read only two or three pages of their book before awareness of what they are up to snaps them out of trance."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure of pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCFindingOnesBookBookshelfVisualisation: self-awareness breaks the reading trance. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the operator (conscious realisation)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon, p. 229; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCOtherRoutesAstralBookLetting a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Other routes to an astral book; letting it emerge uninterpreted"@en, "Andere Wege zum Astralbuch; es ungedeutet hervorkommen lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cast sigils to discover a book in dream, devise an astral journey to find it, or use dreamscaping; let whatever arises emerge in its own form."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon, p. 229; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCRefrainConsciousInterpretationWhileReceivingPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Refrain from conscious interpretation while receiving"@en, "Bewusstes Deuten beim Empfangen unterlassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The key is to resist consciously interpreting what flows and let it come out in any form; Austin Osman Spare mastered this, waking from trance to a finished picture."@en ;
    skos:note "Spare cited as exemplar (thirdParty)."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCOtherRoutesAstralBookLetting ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCReceivingOnesAstralBook ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, The Necronomicon, p. 229; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Scrying
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCScryingTwoWaySeenBecomeCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Scrying is two-way: the seen become aware of the seer"@en, "Kristallsehen wirkt in beide Richtungen: die Gesehenen bemerken den Seher"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Mythos tales scrying devices let the seer glimpse other dimensions while their inhabitants notice and eventually menace him; Dee's and Crowley's records mention spirits emerging from glass or mirror; a basic scrying method is in Condensed Chaos."@en ;
    skos:note "John Dee and Aleister Crowley magical records; English folk belief about the Devil in mirrors."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondBScrying ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Scrying, pp. 229-230; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Shape-Shifting
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGnosisForbiddenLoreChangesIrrevocablyCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Gnosis of forbidden lore changes one irrevocably"@en, "Gnosis verbotenen Wissens verändert unwiderruflich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lovecraft's message, which Hine relays, is that direct contact with forbidden lore changes the individual for ever: once one steps into the Mythos one is never the same."@en ;
    skos:note "Lovecraft (e.g. Pickman's Model, Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath)."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCEmbeddingCthulhuMythos ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Shape-Shifting, p. 230; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCAstralShapeShifting a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Astral shape-shifting"@en, "Astrale Gestaltwandlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take on zoomorphic forms on the astral to penetrate astral spaces, approach zoomorphic deities, or work with power animals; the dreamscape example uses it."@en ;
    skos:note "Some systems are said to hold that zoomorphic deities are best approached in bestial form."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Shape-Shifting, pp. 230-231; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCPenetratingAstralSpacesAnimalForm a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Penetrating astral spaces in animal form"@en, "Durchdringen astraler Räume in Tiergestalt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Zoomorphic astral forms allow entry into astral spaces and contact with zoomorphic deities and power animals."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Shape-Shifting, p. 230; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAstralShapeShiftingYieldsAstral a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Astral shape-shifting yields astral penetration"@en, "Astrale Gestaltwandlung bewirkt astrales Durchdringen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taking animal form on the astral is said to open astral spaces."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCAstralShapeShifting ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCPenetratingAstralSpacesAnimalForm ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Shape-Shifting, p. 230; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCRitualShapeShiftingAnimalPossession a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual shape-shifting by animal possession"@en, "Rituelle Gestaltwandlung durch Tierbesessenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Celebrants take on possession by animal or zoomorphic entities using masks, personal animal dance sequences and costumes, visualising and using kinaesthetic techniques to draw the astral form onto themselves; astral entities can be manifested this way."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Shape-Shifting, p. 231; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCZannumHiveEntityNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Zannum, the hive-entity"@en, "Zannum, die Bienenstock-Entität"@de ;
    skos:definition "A hive entity first met on a scripted pathworking into a beehive and later worked in ritual through a mantra, dance and a mask with exaggerated compound eyes and antennae."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Zannum" ;
    pm:nameRole "hive entity encountered on the astral and manifested in ritual" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Shape-Shifting, p. 231; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAlteredAnimalLikePerceptionPhysiological a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Altered animal-like perception and physiological oddities"@en, "Veränderte tierähnliche Wahrnehmung und körperliche Eigenheiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shape-shifting into animal form can bring perception matching the animal and physical oddities; some magicians report wolf-possessed celebrants giving off a rank animal smell."@en ;
    skos:note "Reports of some magicians (wolf smell)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Shape-Shifting, p. 231; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCRitualShapeShiftingYieldsAltered a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual shape-shifting yields altered perception"@en, "Rituelle Gestaltwandlung bewirkt veränderte Wahrnehmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Animal possession in ritual is said to alter senses and physiology."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCRitualShapeShiftingAnimalPossession ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAlteredAnimalLikePerceptionPhysiological ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Shape-Shifting, p. 231; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Strange Angles
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCLabyrinthsStrangeAnglesInwardJourney a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Labyrinths and strange angles as inward journey"@en, "Labyrinthe und seltsame Winkel als Weg nach innen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lovecraft's mazes and non-Euclidean geometry echo the inward turn toward the unconscious, losing oneself to find the true self; in the Witch-House story he hints quantum physics may lead to gnosis of the Old Ones."@en ;
    skos:note "Lovecraft."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Strange Angles, p. 231; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Frenzied Rites
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCFrenziedRitesPowerSpots a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Frenzied rites at power spots"@en, "Rasende Riten an Kraftorten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lovecraft alludes to group rites summoning star beings at stone circles or strange landmarks, resembling rationalist images of witchcraft or voodoo, with physical routes to gnosis (dance, flagellation, sex, chanting, drumming, hyperventilation); such rites show the interpenetration of celebrants' beliefs, sacred landscape, nature's terrors and the Old Ones' dimensions."@en ;
    skos:note "Lovecraft."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Frenzied Rites, p. 232; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAgainstTerrorMainGnosisMythos a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against terror as the main gnosis of Mythos magic"@en, "Gegen Schrecken als Hauptgnosis der Mythos-Magie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine says recent writers on Mythos magic wrongly assume terror is the chief emotional gnosis because Lovecraft's characters felt it."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the opposing view is reported by him, not quoted from a named work."@en ;
    skos:note "Unnamed recent writers on Mythos magic."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Frenzied Rites, p. 232; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCFearSoonPallsLeverGnosisFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear soon palls as a lever for gnosis"@en, "Angst verliert bald ihre Wirkung als Hebel zur Gnosis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fear may serve at first but quickly loses its effectiveness for reaching gnosis."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: fear soon palls as a lever for gnosis. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the method (fear as gnosis)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Frenzied Rites, p. 232; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCForbiddenSacredPrecinctsLykaianZeusCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Forbidden sacred precincts (Lykaian Zeus)"@en, "Verbotene heilige Bezirke (Lykaischer Zeus)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Theopompus records the folk belief that whoever enters the forbidden precinct of Lykaian Zeus will surely die within the year, and that inside it nothing casts a shadow; Hine uses it to show the Greek sense of places belonging to the gods."@en ;
    skos:note "Theopompus."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCFrenziedRitesPowerSpots ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Frenzied Rites, p. 233; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCPanicLandscapesDemandRitualPrecautionsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Panic landscapes demand ritual precautions"@en, "Panische Landschaften verlangen rituelle Vorsichtsmaßnahmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Like Lovecraft's hostile sentient landscapes, Greek 'panic' places were where strange things happened beyond human will; there humans were prey to greater powers and had to observe ritual precautions."@en ;
    skos:note "Classical Greek belief."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCFrenziedRitesPowerSpots ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Frenzied Rites, p. 233; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCPanNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Pan"@en, "Pan"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lord of wild, panic places; Apollodorus of Athens explains reports of Pan piping in caves as mixed echoes of unseen animals."@en ;
    skos:note "Apollodorus of Athens (4th c. BC per text)."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Pan" ;
    pm:nameRole "god of wild places" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Frenzied Rites, p. 233; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Barbarous Names
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCBarbarousNamesCthulhuoidLanguages a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Barbarous names and Cthulhuoid languages"@en, "Barbarische Namen und cthuloide Sprachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Mythos uses barbarous names of the Old Ones and a primal cultist tongue, which some magicians have used to craft Cthulhuoid languages; these recall possession glossolalia and grimoire barbarous names and add to the Mythos's plausibility."@en ;
    skos:note "Some magicians (unnamed) craft Cthulhuoid languages."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Barbarous Names, p. 234; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCWhyMythosWorksGapsUnbindable a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Why the Mythos works: gaps, unbindable entities, new experimentation"@en, "Warum der Mythos wirkt: Lücken, unbindbare Wesen, neue Experimente"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beyond the initial thrill of going where few dare, the Old Ones stand outside human mythologies like the Giants and Titans, cannot be bound into orthodox systems, and push the magician toward power places, folklore, atavistic resurgence and dream-work; the Mythos works because its gaps invite personal filling rather than literal following."@en ;
    skos:note "Writers using Lovecraftian material named: LaVey, Aquino, Carroll, K. Grant, Bertiaux (historical, not separately recorded)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCGreatOldOnesNaming (Condensed Chaos, 1995): that node carries the Old Ones' place outside human mythologies; here the point serves an account of why Mythos magic works, through its gaps and the new fields of experiment it opens."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Other Magical Elements, Barbarous Names, p. 234; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Beyond Good and Evil?
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCEscapeOnceAmongOldOnesCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No escape once among the Old Ones"@en, "Kein Entrinnen im Reich der Alten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lovecraft lets nobody escape doom: sorcerers who summon the Old Ones eventually pay with insanity or death, survivors carry the knowledge for ever, outwitting them is blind luck, and once one has passed into their realm there is no turning back."@en ;
    skos:note "Lovecraft's fiction as read by Hine."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGreatOldOnesNaming ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Beyond Good and Evil?, p. 235; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGoodEvilDualismLovecraftsMythos a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No good-evil dualism in Lovecraft's Mythos"@en, "Kein Gut-Böse-Dualismus in Lovecrafts Mythos"@de ;
    skos:definition "No powers of light can be called upon against the Old Ones; the Mythos has no room for dualistic good and evil."@en ;
    skos:note "Lovecraft."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Beyond Good and Evil?, p. 235; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAgainstNietzscheanReadingOldOnes a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the Nietzschean reading of the Old Ones"@en, "Gegen die nietzscheanische Deutung der Alten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine rejects intellectuals who cast the Old Ones as Nietzschean supermen beyond good and evil; Lovecraft shows they care for us as we do for cattle, and even devout worshippers end up eaten."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the opposing view is reported by him, not quoted from a named work."@en ;
    skos:note "Disputed: unnamed intellectuals applying Nietzsche."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Beyond Good and Evil?, p. 235; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSelfStyledDarkAdeptsNeverFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-styled dark adepts never actualise their will to power"@en, "Selbsternannte dunkle Adepten verwirklichen nie ihren Willen zur Macht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine finds that would-be satanists, supermen and outsiders claiming to command demons or the Old Ones are in the grip of two memes (Getting Even, Being Right) and never manage to realise their will to power, settling for vicarious thrills and icons."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: self-styled dark adepts never actualise their will to power. No deadline or rate is given; the cause is put on the operator (powerlessness and self-legitimising motives)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Beyond Good and Evil?, p. 237; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .


#
# Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Mythos Madness
#

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAgainstViewMythosWorkUniquely a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the view that Mythos work is uniquely dangerous"@en, "Gegen die Ansicht, Mythos-Arbeit sei einzigartig gefährlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine answers the common occult view that working with the Old Ones is inadvisable, because they ignore normal banishings or tip the unwary into obsession or madness, by saying any magical system can lead to madness and that changing is the point of magic."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the opposing view is reported by him, not quoted from a named work."@en ;
    skos:note "Disputed: general view in the occult milieu."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Mythos Madness, p. 237; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCMythosEntitiesSaidRespondNormalCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Mythos entities said not to respond to normal banishing"@en, "Mythos-Wesen sollen nicht auf übliche Bannungen reagieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "One explanation Hine has met for the danger is that Mythos entities do not answer to normal banishing rituals; others say the Mythos tips the unwary toward obsession or madness."@en ;
    skos:note "Unnamed occult sources; Hine reports and disputes."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCGreatOldOnesNaming ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Mythos Madness, p. 237; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAnyMagicalSystemCanLeadCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Any magical system can lead into madness"@en, "Jedes magische System kann in den Wahnsinn führen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine warns that working any system, Mythos or basic New Age witchcraft, can lead into madness; the trick is getting out again or at least hiding it, and the fear of insanity must be faced head-on."@en ;
    skos:note "Self-warning against magic generally, including his own approach."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondAMagicIsDangerousCautela (Condensed Chaos, 1995): there magic is called dangerous and not for everyone; here madness is said to wait in any system, and the fear of it is to be faced head-on."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCFearLosingControlWorseDerangement ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Mythos Madness, p. 237; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCObsessiveWeirdStatesIntenselyMagical a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Obsessive weird states as intensely magical"@en, "Obsessive seltsame Zustände als höchst magisch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine suggests obsession and brooding on lurking things could benefit one: such states are weird but intensely magical, akin to childhood fears of things under the bed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Mythos Madness, p. 238; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCFearLosingControlWorseDerangement a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear of losing control is worse than derangement itself"@en, "Die Angst vor Kontrollverlust ist schlimmer als die Zerrüttung selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Entering weird states feels like losing control but is really losing the illusion of control; the fear of where one might go often exceeds the process itself in dread and holds one back from surrendering to derangement, which Lovecraft is said to have drawn back from."@en ;
    skos:note "Occultists' saying that Lovecraft drew back at the abyss reported."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Mythos Madness, p. 238; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCRecognitionDriveChangeBeforeIdentityPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognition and drive to change before identity work"@en, "Erkennen und Veränderungswille vor Identitätsarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Hine's experience of Ego Magic, people work on an issue only if they see it needs attention and their drive to change outweighs the wish to stay the same."@en ;
    skos:note "The prior step, recognising the issue, is read onto the self-assessment practice of Condensed Chaos."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondASelfAssessment ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSurfacingOwningOnesHiddenDemons ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "The issue is not worked on."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Mythos Madness, p. 238; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSurfacingOwningOnesHiddenDemons a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Surfacing and owning one's hidden demons"@en, "Hervorholen und Annehmen der eigenen verborgenen Dämonen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Extreme belief systems like Mythos magic can let hidden demons leap out as dysfunctional behaviour, which one may eventually recognise, own and address; otherwise they stay hidden, gnawing from within."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Mythos Madness, p. 238; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCCthulhuMythosMagicYieldsSurfacing a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Cthulhu Mythos magic yields surfacing of hidden demons"@en, "Cthulhu-Mythos-Magie bewirkt das Hervortreten verborgener Dämonen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Working an extreme system such as the Mythos is said to provoke hidden demons into the open where they can be dealt with."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCEmbeddingCthulhuMythos, pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCDreamscaping ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSurfacingOwningOnesHiddenDemons ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Mythos Madness, p. 238; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCConfrontingSurfacedDemonsPainfulCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Confronting surfaced demons is painful"@en, "Die Konfrontation hervorgetretener Dämonen ist schmerzhaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recognising and dealing with demons that surface as dysfunctional behaviour is always hard and frequently hurts."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCSurfacingOwningOnesHiddenDemons ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PrimeChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Prime Chaos: Adventures in Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1999, second revised edition; first edition Chaos International, 1993), Part IV Liber Nice & Liber Nasty, Liber Nasty, Mythos Madness, p. 238; read in a full-text layer of the second revised edition" .
